{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews","id":69712,"title":"2014 Mummy Releases & Previews","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-11T02:27:59-08:00","id":69712,"title":"2014 Mummy Releases & Previews","content":"Mummy: the Curse is expected to add a number of supplements this year to its line! I think the only one whose due date is in 2015 is <i>Sothis Ascends</i>. Coming up fastest we have <i>Cursed Necropolis: DC</i> and <i>Book of the Deceived</i>.<br /> <br /> Back around October or November CAS hinted that we should expect a preview of <i>Book of the Deceived</i> within a month. It's February now and I was hoping if there's any more word on anything? I love this game and there's a number of AP threads out there now, but I'd love some developers and writers to talk up how great it is!<br /> <br /> I feel <i>Demon: the Descent</i> was successful for a lot of reasons, not the least of which is that Matt and Rose and some writers were very engaged with its fans. I guess now, for me, it's just coming down to simple jealousy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T04:10:38-08:00","id":69742,"title":"","content":"I'm likewise very excited for Book of the Deceived, if it's going to be as good as Belial's Brood was for Requiem. I'll see what CA has to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T09:28:00-08:00","id":69874,"title":"","content":"Teasers would be awesome, I'll ask CAS also","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T10:48:37-08:00","id":69908,"title":"","content":"Weren't we also getting a Rio de Janeiro book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T16:36:49-08:00","id":70128,"title":"","content":"I'm reliably informed there will be a DC preview in a week or so <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T17:00:37-08:00","id":70147,"title":"","content":"Great news! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yes, there's a <i>Cursed Necropolis: Rio</i> but I'm not sure about its release date. I think it was planned on being released either right before or right after <i>Sothis Ascends</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T16:41:58-08:00","id":72305,"title":"","content":"For folks who did not back the Kickstarter, the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/113112?affiliate_id=22713&amp;src=MMMOPPForums\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy Storyteller's Screen</a> is now available in PDF for only $1.99.<br /> <br /> -MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T11:15:47-08:00","id":75083,"title":"","content":"Come on, DC preview! My body is ready!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T14:46:40-08:00","id":77330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews#post69712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy: the Curse is expected to add a number of supplements this year to its line! I think the only one whose due date is in 2015 is <i>Sothis Ascends</i>. Coming up fastest we have <i>Cursed Necropolis: DC</i> and <i>Book of the Deceived</i>.<br /> <br /> Back around October or November CAS hinted that we should expect a preview of <i>Book of the Deceived</i> within a month. It's February now and I was hoping if there's any more word on anything? I love this game and there's a number of AP threads out there now, but I'd love some developers and writers to talk up how great it is!<br /> <br /> I feel <i>Demon: the Descent</i> was successful for a lot of reasons, not the least of which is that Matt and Rose and some writers were very engaged with its fans. I guess now, for me, it's just coming down to simple jealousy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>To my knowledge the following Mummy releases can be expected in the next 10 months or so for sure:<br /> <br /> Cursed Necropolis: DC (its in editing, earliest we are going to see it is end of March)<br /> Book of the Deceived (in second phase of redlining after rewrites)<br /> <br /> It's highly likely (but by no means guaranteed) that the following will also be released in 2014:<br /> <br /> Cursed Necropolis: Rio (Don't know the status of this one) <br /> Dreams of Avarice (A writer was decided upon on contracted in November last year according to Rich T's e-mail updates for Mummy Kickstarter backers, nothing heard since. I really wish they would update us on this via an e-mail at least.) <br /> <br /> The following are a big MAYBE for this year and very likely going to be out in 2015:<br /> <br /> Sothis Ascends<br /> Mummy Novel<br /> Fiction Anthology<br /> <br /> The other books have been discussed or teased, but we don't even know if they are on the schedule for next year yet:<br /> <br /> Book of Going Westward<br /> Book about Apothesis<br /> <br /> The former of these two was talked about at the end of the Kickstarter (as something the Dev's might do if Mummy sold well enough).<br /> The latter was something that CAS talked about in an interview on the Onyx Path website. Though to be clear he may have possibly been referring to Book of the Deceived or Sothis Ascends. <br /> <br /> In a previous thread we discussed if Mummy actually NEEDED any more books after these ones. The general thought was that a book to expand the Cult rules would be good. I believe there was also some talk about doing a sorta &quot;Antagonists Book&quot; to expand on the Lifeless a bit. Since at the moment the Shaukshan (spelling...gah) are a bit...one note as villains. <br /> <br /> I strongly agree with Reseru about the handling of Mummy following its initial release. Namely the lack of communication between CAS and the fans<br /> <br /> Rose and Matt have been supporting the Demon fanbase excellently by regularly staying in contact, answering questions and even incorporating fan feedback into their revisions and future products. OK maybe they have spoiled those of us that have been backing Demon as well, but I've found myself infinitely more well endeared to Demon due to the fact that I know there is a dialogue between the creators and fans. <br /> <br /> CAS on the other hand popped in to say <i>&quot;Hi I'm on the forums.&quot;</i> and then answered all of about 3 fan queries (one of which was posted by me as a hypothesis about the upcoming Book of the Deceived) and has been absent ever since (going on about 5 months). <br /> <br /> In the meantime the preview for Deceived not only failed to materialize in November but failed to appear in 2013 at all. Likewise, the DC preview mentioned on this very thread for &quot;the next week or so&quot; (made about 2 weeks ago) has once again failed to happen. <br /> <br /> Now, I might be being completely unreasonable, CAS might just be a very busy guy, he might not have the sort of time free that Rose or Matt spend on various forums chatting with fans. If so fair enough, I don't know his circumstances and it would be wrong of me to draw any conclusions without having all the facts. <br /> <br /> Not to flog a dead horse but there is the matter of product release issues as well. <br /> <br /> I know Onyx Path has a strict policy of: <i>&quot;Every date is just an estimate/guideline and we want to give our developers enough time to get every product perfect because they are free-lancers and are doing this out of love.&quot;</i> <br /> <br /> Still even with that in mind every single Mummy release has been delayed horribly. The Core book (not counting Kickstarter copies) was about 3 months delayed. Guildhalls was about 6 months late. Ready Made characters took forever to get to pdf let alone print. DC was originally estimated for October, Deceived for November. I thought adding 4 months to these release dates would practical on my part. At current DC may be as late as April in release (6 months delayed, its been in &quot;editing&quot; for 6 weeks, what are they using to edit it an old fashion tip-ex machine) and Deceived is looking to be an April release at earliest (more likely May, making it 7 months delayed). <br /> <br /> Now, I'm fully aware other lines in the NWoD have also suffered delays Blood and Smoke was 4 months delayed after all. Likewise, the first Demon supplement has already been pushed back by 2/3 months. However, all this stuff was mentioned at least a month before the original release estimate by the Devs in question. They gave explanations for these things, talked about what was being polished and improved and changed. <br /> <br /> With Mummy its just been the case that Rich T's Monday Morning blog has a single sentence (in some cases a single word) saying where the Mummy project is at current. No communication to the fans, no talk about how the projects developing, no explanation. Just that brief update. That's it. <br /> <br /> I'm a fan of Mummy, I'm running a game of it at current and have been for damn near a year. Hand's down I've been looking forward to Book of the Deceived since it came on the docket a year and a half ago. Now I'm just fed up waiting for it. It was in the first round of redlining for 6 weeks and in rewrites for another 6 weeks (and I see no indication it won't spend the best part of the next two months in redlining again), I appreciate that CAS is more involved with this book and maybe wants it &quot;perfect&quot; but at this point I', afraid if its anything less then &quot;prefect&quot; then I'm going to be so embittered by the prolonged wait that I can't be anything but disappointed in it. <br /> <br /> However, all that enthusiasm I had that's got piled into frustration could have easily been stoked by much higher heights if CAS could have been a little more fan-friendly and post previews, stoked some fan conversation and hinted at some stuff. <br /> <br /> OK, I've cast all my stones, had my gump<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and kicked all hell out of these old issues. You may all now commence retaliatory strikes as you see fit. I'll take my lumps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T22:44:48-08:00","id":77484,"title":"","content":"I don't know if anyone's going to retaliate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I understand developers and writers have lives, too, and both Matt and Rose have multiple responsibilities that gear them towards spending time online anyway (namely, being forum moderators on various sites). Any bit we get I'm grateful for and take as a blessing.<br /> <br /> The problem is that I feel like Mummy has been treated as a 'failed' or 'throwaway' line right off the bat. There <i>are</i> fans enthused for it but all we're given are delays (tolerable), promised previews that never come (slightly more annoying, but #firstworldproblems), and silence from those who could answer questions we have about game concepts that we're having difficulty grasping.<br /> <br /> I don't know how else to put it other than, &quot;I like what you've given us so far. I <i>want</i> to like all of it, but I don't understand some of it. Please help!&quot; And...nothing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T23:45:55-08:00","id":77501,"title":"","content":"Is mummy a failure though? It doesn't have as much fan love that Demon has gotten (and I do enjoy demon myself, it's a good book). I mean, mummy seems to have gotten a bad rap from day one. Early on there was a lot of criticism of the book. Some deserved (the layout and some rules), some not so much (the fiction and the sekhem rules). Maybe a lot of those issued could have been stemmed if, like Reseru and Hawkthorn said, the developers were more involved. But has it been enough to get all these lapses in the schedule? I really hope mummy doesn't end up as another Promethean or Geist, and at least we're getting more than 1 or 2 supplements. I can stand the delays. It's annoying but if all the supplements are as filled to the brim with content and info like Guildhalls was, or as thought provoking as the Ready Made Characters were, then I think it will be worth the wait. Hopefully. I am VERY ready for the Deceived to come out...like soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T05:11:38-08:00","id":77594,"title":"","content":"I've said it before and I'll say it again: Mummy is a good game. Its just not a complete game.<br /> <br /> I honestly believe its head and shoulders above some other games in terms of setting and themes (Werewolf springs to mind but I've never been a fan of &quot;shaman-the-spirit-cop&quot; theme anyway).<br /> <br /> You can't really understand how the Guilds work without Guildhalls (not to mention Bane relics, they should have been in the core), you can't really know how Nomes work without the DC book, good luck running a Decieved NPC (and not just making their rules up) without Book of the Deceived.<br /> <br /> Basically, it a very incomplete game out of the core. As such, more then maybe any other game line it REQUIRES splat books for its full potential to be reached. Which is very annoying when every single release is at least 4 months delayed.<br /> <br /> On the matter of Mummy being a &quot;failure&quot;. If were talking about sales I'd bet that its the lowest selling NWoD game after Giest and maybe Promethean, I won't be expecting many Mummy stretch goals in the upcoming Dark Era's kickstarter lets put it like that.<br /> <br /> We can take heart that thanks the Kickstarter it is getting decent line support, in so far as its guaranteed 6 splat books (Guildhalls, Ready Made Characters, DC, Deceived, Rio, Avarice) which is more then Giest or Promethean got (admittedly 4 of those are only due to the kickstarter). Plus its getting two fiction books (Novel and Fiction Anthology) which I will likely end up mining for plot and story, so kinda splat books for me at least. Also two other splats...sorta: Mortal Remains (for Hunter) and Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> If we are going for more abstract measures of &quot;failure&quot; well there are a few we could point to:<br /> <br /> 1) The game suffers for being released in NWoD 1.0 rules. Simply the old rules are weaker then the GM update ones. Likewise, GM was announced around the same time as Mummy and a lot of people &quot;wrote it off&quot; when they found out it was not going to be in the GM rules (about three quarters of my local gaming community in my case). Mummy is a game that would have benefited from the Condition rules a lot.<br /> <br /> 2) The Kickstarter ran 23 days instead of the usual 30 and took place over Christmas (should have waited until January). It was mishandled terribly in the last week (new years) due to basically real-life getting in the way of the people running it. As a result it did not get the sort of money it could have.<br /> <br /> 3) It got very little hype. Once again this ties in with the first point of people going off it before it even came out on rules basis. CAS did basically nothing to plug the game on various interactive forums and by the time of release even the Mummy Blog (which started out with regular updates) had pretty much gone silent. Contrast this with Demon, where Rose and Matt were EVERYWHERE on gaming websites plugging the game, not to mention running regular updates on Demons content and giving us a free pdf rough draft when the Kickstarter started.<br /> <br /> 4) Mummy tried to do something different. People mostly don't like change (could I be more general?). The whole player/storyteller divide in the middle of the book, the use of a hard cannon for the game and the reversal of the traditional power mechanic (Sekhem goes down) also turned a lot of people off it. On top of this Mummy made no effort to include itself in the wider NWoD. It very much feels like Mummy is in its own parallel universe to the rest of the games. Once again to contrast Demon, which dedicated a couple of pages to just how Demon's interact with all the other supernaturals of the NWoD except...Mummy's. Which pretty much reinforces the idea that Mummy is off in its own sandbox playing alone.<br /> <br /> 5) Not sure if this one extends beyond my local gaming community but I'll list it anyway. Mummy is seen as a bit...OTT by many. Its Dark Plup for sure and you can get into some really meaty character stuff with memory (which has been the focus of my game). However, most people seem to look at it, see how powerful Mummy's can be with a bit of XP and how powerful a lot of their antagonists are and get turned away. This is even more apparent when you realize that Mummy's basically have no Masquerade equivalent, make people believe in the supernatural and have powers that are so flashy and epic that people could not help but notice them. All of which I will admit does break away from the &quot;stay hidden&quot; aspect of all the other game lines.<br /> <br /> 6) The supplements have been so-so. Ready Made Characters read like a Vampire splat (at least to me) and did nothing to reinforce the themes of the game (save for the Maa-Keep character). Guildhalls had a load of good info in it that could have done with being in Core but it was a mish-mash of tone and mechanics. It suffered from having a different writer for each chapter. Worse it was obvious the authors had not tired to really talk to each other to see what other people were doing. Hence a sever lack of uniformity and some guilds getting more then others e.g. Sesha Hesbu vs Tef Aahebi anyone?<br /> <br /> The way I have come to look at is is that each new release makes Mummy a more complete game with more stuff for ST's to entice players with and widen their games plots and themes with. However, I'm fully expecting that we will get our 6 splat books and 2 fiction books and then Mummy will be expected to go live in a corner (much like Giest and Promethean) and get the of couple of page pdf thing now and then after 2015. IF we are really lucky they will update Mummy to GM rules as a &quot;Chronicle&quot; book around 2017 (keeping with the idea that they are doing 2 Chronicle books a year from this year forward), which I might add I would buy in a heartbeat.<br /> <br /> I mean honestly, compare the enthusiasm, hype, sales, communication, kickstarters and forum activity between Mummy and Demon, you'll notice a BIG difference. I'm pretty sure Demon's been the most successful game for NWoD since Changeling to give you an idea. Only Werewolf the Apoc and Exalted outrank it for Kickstarter earnings. It was only planned to have 3 splats (Translation Guide, Player Guide and Storyteller Guide) but the kickstarter alone added another 4 to that (Story Matrix, Heirs to Hell, Seattle City Book, Demon Seed Collection). Mortal Remains (for Hunter) and Dark Era's also providing an additional 2 splats on top of that. I will not be surprised if the 2015 release schedule adds at least another 2 (Antagonists Book + ?) splat books to the game line. Meanwhile I think any Mummy releases we see on the new 2015 schedule will be simply delayed products from this year or things like the fiction books.<br /> <br /> Sorry, did not mean this to be a massive downer. Just spelling out my take on the situation and reinforcing my belief that the game has made a few mistakes (both pre and post release) and has been mishandled.<br /> <br /> Once again feel free to throw rocks at this grumbling<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> bitter old man. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T06:09:03-08:00","id":77614,"title":"","content":"I hope you guys get some love. I personally don't like M:tC (hard canon for the background? specific focus on Egyptian lore? hard to pitch to a group? massive power level? eep!) but as a big fan of both Geist and Promethean, I don't want to see anyone else end up in our sad little corner. Fingers crossed for all three to get some more love down the line. I wish OPP would do some polling about what new books are wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T06:34:24-08:00","id":77626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said it before and I'll say it again: Mummy is a good game. Its just not a complete game.<br /> <br /> I honestly believe its head and shoulders above some other games in terms of setting and themes (Werewolf springs to mind but I've never been a fan of &quot;shaman-the-spirit-cop&quot; theme anyway).<br /> <br /> You can't really understand how the Guilds work without Guildhalls (not to mention Bane relics, they should have been in the core), you can't really know how Nomes work without the DC book, good luck running a Decieved NPC (and not just making their rules up) without Book of the Deceived.<br /> <br /> Basically, it a very incomplete game out of the core. As such, more then maybe any other game line it REQUIRES splat books for its full potential to be reached. Which is very annoying when every single release is at least 4 months delayed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. My biggest complain in how the game was handled is also half a compliment: not enough page-count. It's just kind of a dirty move to say, &quot;Here's the mysterious Lost Guild...that we provide zero information about even though it's in the celebrated, resurrected STORYTELLER'S SECTION, so you'll have to wait until we publish their supplement which, as a supplement it's option so, you might not even buy.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) The game suffers for being released in NWoD 1.0 rules. Simply the old rules are weaker then the GM update ones. Likewise, GM was announced around the same time as Mummy and a lot of people &quot;wrote it off&quot; when they found out it was not going to be in the GM rules (about three quarters of my local gaming community in my case). Mummy is a game that would have benefited from the Condition rules a lot.<br /> <br /> 2) The Kickstarter ran 23 days instead of the usual 30 and took place over Christmas (should have waited until January). It was mishandled terribly in the last week (new years) due to basically real-life getting in the way of the people running it. As a result it did not get the sort of money it could have.<br /> <br /> 3) It got very little hype. Once again this ties in with the first point of people going off it before it even came out on rules basis. CAS did basically nothing to plug the game on various interactive forums and by the time of release even the Mummy Blog (which started out with regular updates) had pretty much gone silent. Contrast this with Demon, where Rose and Matt were EVERYWHERE on gaming websites plugging the game, not to mention running regular updates on Demons content and giving us a free pdf rough draft when the Kickstarter started.<br /> <br /> 5) Not sure if this one extends beyond my local gaming community but I'll list it anyway. Mummy is seen as a bit...OTT by many. Its Dark Plup for sure and you can get into some really meaty character stuff with memory (which has been the focus of my game). However, most people seem to look at it, see how powerful Mummy's can be with a bit of XP and how powerful a lot of their antagonists are and get turned away. This is even more apparent when you realize that Mummy's basically have no Masquerade equivalent, make people believe in the supernatural and have powers that are so flashy and epic that people could not help but notice them. All of which I will admit does break away from the &quot;stay hidden&quot; aspect of all the other game lines.<br /> <br /> 6) The supplements have been so-so. Ready Made Characters read like a Vampire splat (at least to me) and did nothing to reinforce the themes of the game (save for the Maa-Keep character). Guildhalls had a load of good info in it that could have done with being in Core but it was a mish-mash of tone and mechanics. It suffered from having a different writer for each chapter. Worse it was obvious the authors had not tired to really talk to each other to see what other people were doing. Hence a sever lack of uniformity and some guilds getting more then others e.g. Sesha Hesbu vs Tef Aahebi anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Every thing. WoD comes back from a new core hiatus since 2009 but it's with an old edition they already have a new one in development for. The Kickstarter over Christmas and New Year's was a bummer; I think people were just impatient for Mummy's release so OP caved and gave it to us early. Little excitement from CAS does little to generate our own interests in the game. I think Mummy's 'masquerade' factor is fine, especially at lower levels of Sekhem when you should be fearing everything around you - it's a nice juxtaposition to your early power levels being so high. And yeah...Mummies that run a night club? That...just doesn't really fit Mummy's mood. Mummy isn't a game of drug, sex, and rock n roll in a bar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) Mummy tried to do something different. People mostly don't like change (could I be more general?). The whole player/storyteller divide in the middle of the book, the use of a hard cannon for the game and the reversal of the traditional power mechanic (Sekhem goes down) also turned a lot of people off it. On top of this Mummy made no effort to include itself in the wider NWoD. It very much feels like Mummy is in its own parallel universe to the rest of the games. Once again to contrast Demon, which dedicated a couple of pages to just how Demon's interact with all the other supernaturals of the NWoD except...Mummy's. Which pretty much reinforces the idea that Mummy is off in its own sandbox playing alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my other big complaint. The first few pages of the core state how it's going to usher in a new era of WoD by doing things differently, and then Demon comes out and it uses the same formula that's been successful for a decade. The Mummy core lists no inspirational material, unlike its predecessors and Demon, instead promising a website that still isn't running. The Mummy core mentions that DC is its signature city but doesn't provide an appendix describing it, unlike its predecessors and Demon, even though it has side-bars describing other locations; this is a big problem because, especially considering how the line boasts that it's <i>the most </i>politically-driven splat, we could have seen how Mummy society works right off the bat. Now it's like the Deceived where there's just a sign that says, &quot;Read about it in an optional upcoming supplement that, at the point of this writing, may or may not even be funded by Kickstarter.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again in lieu of the page count thing, I understand that they wanted to use page space for Mummy and not talk about other game-lines but again its predecessors (at least Promethean, off the top of my head, and I know Mage and Changeling discussed it in its supplements) and Demon had room to at least briefly mention them, so I just don't get it. All this makes it feel like Mummy got the shaft before it even came out, and now the fans are getting the shaft because no one's talking with us. Promethean did everything right, and Geist earned its respect and it's a tragedy it hasn't yet received more material. I don't want Mummy to die before its had a chance and I know that sounds fatalistic, but 1) a lack of understanding game concepts as they are presented and 2) no developer or writer engaging its fan base to answer those concerns is a recipe for failure, is it not?<br /> <br /> When (if?) all of Mummy's supplements are released I hope it soothes all our concerns about game concepts and makes it feel like a complete game. It'll just suck knowing that we got 80% of a game in the core, and rather than supplemental material being additional material we'll feel that it was some of the 20% that we should've had to begin with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","user":"reseru","date":". 02-23-2014, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T01:43:31-08:00","id":78174,"title":"","content":"There are a few very simple ways to increase interest in the game.<br /> <br /> Post Mummy stuff. Story hooks (there's a rather sizey thread for those), actual play notes, discussions regarding Mummy stuff, setting hacks, houserules, etc. Everything.<br /> <br /> Post reviews on relevant sites including drivethrurpg, rpg.net, etc.<br /> <br /> Buy Mummy books.<br /> <br /> Play the game. Run the game. Talk about the game.<br /> <br /> More interest in the game --&gt; more demand for Mummy books --&gt; more support.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T06:52:26-08:00","id":78284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=78174#post78174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a few very simple ways to increase interest in the game.<br /> <br /> Post Mummy stuff. Story hooks (there's a rather sizey thread for those), actual play notes, discussions regarding Mummy stuff, setting hacks, houserules, etc. Everything.<br /> <br /> Post reviews on relevant sites including drivethrurpg, rpg.net, etc.<br /> <br /> Buy Mummy books.<br /> <br /> Play the game. Run the game. Talk about the game.<br /> <br /> More interest in the game --&gt; more demand for Mummy books --&gt; more support.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. I'll be recording what happens in the <i><b>Eye of Judgment </b></i>game that I'll be running in a couple of weeks, including getting feedback from my players who are: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>New to WoD</li> <li>His girlfriend who hasn't played games before</li> <li>OWoD Veteran</li> <li>&quot;Casual&quot; gamer with more experience than the average D&amp;D-only player, has played Geist before but nothing else WoD</li> </ol><br /> And me, the Storyteller, whose longest game of WoD is my (as-of-now) 4-session Vampire: Blood &amp; Smoke game.<br /> <br /> I was blown away by Mummy after reading the core book, and I'm desperate to see this game do well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T08:18:48-08:00","id":78316,"title":"","content":"I don't think Mummy is a failure. It is a little overfocused on Egyptian mythology (but so were it's earlier renditions) and has a bit too much in the way of metaplot (but hey, I'm the storyteller so rewrites to fit my setting are always the order of the day; honestly, fluffy stuff is expendable). I do wish that the Mummy BRB had conformed to the GMC update. Several of us have posted our GMC-update houserules and hopefully the devs are looking at them and stealing any good ideas. I'm looking forward to the release of the next source book. <br /> <br /> Now if I can just find a stable group of players in the Chambana area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T09:36:39-08:00","id":78369,"title":"","content":"&quot;Failure&quot; in and itself is a term that lacks context.<br /> <br /> The game brought lots of enjoyment to my gaming group --&gt; for the purposes of my gaming group, it's a success.<br /> <br /> Whether or not it's a financial success, entirely different question, and not one we can answer.<br /> <br /> And Mummy doesn't have metaplot. Like, at all. It has lots of plot and lots of setting and backstory, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T11:04:53-08:00","id":78437,"title":"","content":"Failure is a strong word in this particular case. As Christ A pointed out, requires a context we mostly don't have access to. <br /> <br /> I still stick to my earlier statement: Mummy is a good game, it achieves what it sets out to do and if you can find people who find the game enjoyable then its doing its job. <br /> <br /> However, its also an incomplete game given just the core book, its made several mistakes (that I listed earlier in this thread) that have marginalized it among the WoD fanbase. <br /> <br /> So a good game, but a flawed one without doubt.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm still going to buy all the splat books (getting most for free for being a Kickstarter backer anyway) as I am enough of a fan to push the line despite my misgivings about it. I'm still looking forward to Deceived more then any other WoD release this year save maybe the upcoming Strix splats. <br /> <br /> My deepest hope is that the Mummy devs learn from the way the line has been treated in response to the mistakes made and the lack of communication and integrate that into a Chronicle book if Mummy gets one. I've got players who found Requiem 1.0 as dull as dishwater but are absolutely loving Strix to bits. Hopefully Mummy will see a similar upswing in interest at that time. Until then I'll continue to support the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T04:09:13-08:00","id":80148,"title":"","content":"I imagine I will be posting videos on my YouTube channel chronicling my adventures running the game. They seem to have stimulated interest in games in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:12:39-08:00","id":80451,"title":"","content":"My initial read on things is that Mummy got scooped by Demon and that the WoD fanbase isn't as mature as it thinks it is. The idea that you get less powerful over time is great for mature players, but anti-twink in the extreme and all of those players drooling over one day having Dominate 5 in a Vamp game aren't going to be drawn in. Promethean suffered as well, due to it's more mature themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T15:28:44-08:00","id":80561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=80451#post80451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial read on things is that Mummy got scooped by Demon and that the WoD fanbase isn't as mature as it thinks it is. The idea that you get less powerful over time is great for mature players, but anti-twink in the extreme and all of those players drooling over one day having Dominate 5 in a Vamp game aren't going to be drawn in. Promethean suffered as well, due to it's more mature themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you that on face value Demon seems to have got more love then Mummy has. Likewise, that its pulled in a wider range of players and has a larger fan base. <br /> <br /> However, the reasons for this are quite extensive really and cannot be boiled down to a single issue. I've listed some of them in the thread previously. Certainly a massive factor has been the fact that Rose and Matt have a very strong presence among the fans, while CAS does not. Likewise, I do honestly believe that Demon is a &quot;better&quot; put together game. Both in physical structure (the books layout is far less &quot;skip back-and-forth&quot; then Mummy) and in its themes, which I feel reach a broader spectrum of players. <br /> <br /> I think trying to reduce the issue to just being about the fact that Mummy's get &quot;weaker&quot; with time and this theoretically means that the characters get &quot;weaker&quot; as the game goes on is a bit of a fallacy really. Mummy's only get &quot;weaker&quot; in terms of supernaturals feats and mystical resource expenditure. A Mummy that's been active for long enough to reach the lower Sekhem levels is more likely to have a more organised cult and have made more immediate allies and contacts, not to mention being clued into the &quot;scene&quot; of the games ongoing plot by that point. &quot;Weaker&quot; is a very generic term basically. <br /> <br /> As for Promethean, I think it has its own problematic mechanics, themes and metaphysics which turn a lot of players off it. As my group like to say &quot;its the greatest game you'll never play&quot;. Honestly, I like it, but its one of the few roleplay games I think I would get a more enjoyable experience from running for maybe 2 players at most (just because small group numbers help reinforce the games themes and allow you to adiquately explore the type of character development that Promethean pretty much demands).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T05:17:16-08:00","id":80972,"title":"","content":"I don't think the nature of the Descent is what turned players off. I rarely heard or read any complaints about it. In fact, it seems it only gets brought up when people are trying to cite reasons for Mummy's unpopularity.<br /> <br /> I think the issue is that people open up Mummy and thought, &quot;What do I do? What story do I tell?&quot; And their answer was, &quot;Collect relics. Then collect more relics.&quot; Demon, for whatever reason, people gobbled up. &quot;I'm a biomechanical H R Giger spy? Hell yeah!&quot; It's not a very fair initial reaction because every game can be boiled down to one thing over and over. I hated the early days of Requiem because all I saw was &quot;nocturnal backstabbing politics and nothing else&quot; and that's very boring to me. Wicked Dead and Blood &amp; Smoke did a lot to fix that.<br /> <br /> Us diehard Mummy fans know there's more to the game than just collecting relics, though, but Mummy has a more complicated elevator pitch than Demon. If it's going in this direction I'm predicting, then I like that Mummy tries to balance the appeal of being supernatural and the appeal of Apotheosis. Most games go for the former, and Promethean focused on the latter aspect in a way. Mummy being on the fence maybe confuses people: &quot;Oh, so...we collect relics for 20 sessions and then when my character and actual-me-the-PC are sick of it we chase after Apotheosis? Uh...&quot;<br /> <br /> I like that! I love it, but Mummy might be too unique! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T08:13:04-08:00","id":81037,"title":"","content":"I've created a rather huge thread for the sole purpose of showing people the flexibility of this game. The whole &quot;this game is only about scavenger hunts&quot; thing doesn't hold up to reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T11:51:36-08:00","id":81152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=80972#post80972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Us diehard Mummy fans know there's more to the game than just collecting relics, though, but Mummy has a more complicated elevator pitch than Demon. If it's going in this direction I'm predicting, then I like that Mummy tries to balance the appeal of being supernatural and the appeal of Apotheosis. Most games go for the former, and Promethean focused on the latter aspect in a way. Mummy being on the fence maybe confuses people: &quot;Oh, so...we collect relics for 20 sessions and then when my character and actual-me-the-PC are sick of it we chase after Apotheosis? Uh...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Even worse, if you want to stick to the game's spoiler-y nature you can't tell potential players that Apotheosis is a real thing that they can achieve rather than a rumor and an ideaology for the &quot;bad guys&quot; to follow. You definitely don't want to let them know exactly what Apotheosis entails at any rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T14:03:12-08:00","id":81223,"title":"","content":"Another thing is, like the Gentleman up there said, Mummy is a storytellers game. It was built to give the majority of control in the storytellers hands. You don't make a detailed character, you can't really control what you do (I mean you can but it's a concerted effort to do so), and you don't know a lot of what's actually going on. That's a storytellers wet dream, but the players will probably see it as a game designed to destroy their fun. It's a game that's less about a power fantasy and more about mystery and story if I'm going to be blunt. For a player that loves story and intrigue than mummy is a great game, but for a player that just wants to beat people up and do cool shit...like my group...this game is kryptonite. Probably the truest definition of NICHE you can get in RPG gaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T17:26:52-08:00","id":81333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RisTigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=81223#post81223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing is, like the Gentleman up there said, Mummy is a storytellers game. It was built to give the majority of control in the storytellers hands. You don't make a detailed character, you can't really control what you do (I mean you can but it's a concerted effort to do so), and you don't know a lot of what's actually going on. That's a storytellers wet dream, but the players will probably see it as a game designed to destroy their fun. It's a game that's less about a power fantasy and more about mystery and story if I'm going to be blunt. For a player that loves story and intrigue than mummy is a great game, but for a player that just wants to beat people up and do cool shit...like my group...this game is kryptonite. Probably the truest definition of NICHE you can get in RPG gaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of disagree with this. I feel like Mummy's got a very firm sense of pulp mixed in with its horror, it just doesn't wear it on its sleeve and buries it in its systems, so that players can discover it emergently through play. Whether this is a good idea or not I'm not sure, but my group seems to be taking to it pretty well thus far. Specifically... Characters start in media res, without a lot of details on-stage about their backgrounds, apart from their origins, but acquire details of past adventures as their Memory grows. The Storyteller could make up all of that themselves, or they could work collaboratively with the players to flesh out past Descents. The Descent structure provides a built-in incentive for episodic play, with story arcs covering about a year of time spent in the living world, starting with lots of action and door-kicking and ending with more narrow victories and personal drama. While Sekhem resets mostly reward you for being an awful person, Memory - and Sebayt XP - are exactly the opposite, rewarding compassion and charity. Groups that don't completely ignore Memory will inevitably begin to unravel the mysteries of the setting, many of which their characters personally experienced. Cults give each character a built-in support network; they've always got minions that can attend to the details.<br /> <br /> Even the antagonists...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The villains we get the most up-front details on - the Shuankhsen - are basically stereotypical pulp villains. They've got hideous deformities, cackling evil, <i>literally eat people for power</i>, and are outright impossible to kill for good. They'll come back in a different body, and probably be very, very cranky about it.<br /> <br /> And the Amkhat? Last Dynasty? They're basically custom-built for horror-tinged pulp adventuring... Or pulp-tinged personal horror. Either way.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So yeah, I think that Mummy's pretty well-suited to beating people up and doing cool shit. It just needs the right tack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T18:43:33-08:00","id":81357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egarwaen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=81333#post81333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kind of disagree with this. I feel like Mummy's got a very firm sense of pulp mixed in with its horror, it just doesn't wear it on its sleeve and buries it in its systems, so that players can discover it emergently through play. Whether this is a good idea or not I'm not sure, but my group seems to be taking to it pretty well thus far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not realize it myself at first but one of my players pointed out just how pulp Mummy is in a lot of places pretty early into my campaign. After he pointed it out to me I can't not see it in the majority of the game theme and tone now. I'd go so far as to say <b>Dark Pulp</b> is the overall tone of Mummy. <br /> <br /> I think Mummy is a bit or a take it or leave it game. Out of my players about half seemed happy to entertain the idea and the ones that ended up playing Mummy's in my campaign really enjoyed it and would play in the setting again for sure. The ones that were not sure on it and did not play (and did not really every want to do so) are probably less sold on it then they were before I started the campaign. Nothing wrong with a game being polarizing through. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not running another Mummy campaign again for at least a few years (I'm moving away from WoD for about a year to broaden my roleplay horizons and after that everyone in my local group is pretty much betting for me to run Demon). At worst I want all the scheduled splat books out before I try my hand at it again. At best I might even weight and see if it gets a chronicle book and do Mummy 2.0. <br /> <br /> Not to say I am done with it completely. I'm definitely thinking about running a couple of session game set in DC or Rio once those books are out for just he fun of it. Likewise, I'm tempted to use Arisen in other games as background NPC's (even if their never even awake during the course of a game).<br /> <br /> Weirdly, and I don't know if anyone else thinks something similar, I think the Mummy antagonists are actually more cross-over friendly then the Arisen themselves. Last Dynasty can slip right into a Hunter game as a rival to Cherion, or be a group of hunters that are trying to refine Kindred Vitae in the same way the cannon version does stuff with Sekhem. Shaunkhsen are an interesting villain archetype with enough mystery and power (they are pretty nasty compared with several other lines standard antagonists) to be genuinely scare to a player group of Vampires, Mages, Hunters, Changelings or Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> The Deceived, despite being the &quot;big secret&quot; antagonist group could feature very interestingly into Promethean or Mage just due to the thematics of Name Magic (and this is before we know anything really about them). Hell, even the Heretic and is dossier &quot;Dreams of Avarice&quot; could provide an interesting plot point or NPC interaction in any game with a &quot;redemptive&quot; quality to it, mainly Vampire and Promethean but maybe Changeling too. <br /> <br /> Basically, even though I may be a voice of negativity on this thread (though I do love Mummy myself) I won't for a minute dispute that its a useful resource for any WoD game. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T07:11:26-08:00","id":81578,"title":"","content":"Mummy is very much a pulp game, that was no secret. I'm pretty sure it's even written on like the second page of the core book. I mean, you play a tomb robber looking for ancient treasure, and its Dark Era takes place between the World Wars. They practically spelled it out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T20:07:54-08:00","id":81896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=80972#post80972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like that! I love it, but Mummy might be too unique! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Echoing what was cited earlier, it suffers the same issues that Promethean does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T12:20:47-08:00","id":82216,"title":"","content":"I like mummy, however, as others have said a lot of my personal hangup is that I can't increase my power trait back up without well, burning out for a while.<br /> <br /> It is definitely an interesting system, and the thought of starting off ridiculously powerful and in the throws of rage is awesome. I just don't particularly want to not be able to get back to that and stay there over the course of a long game (In the vampire game I'm currently in and have played for around a year or more I'm sitting at BP 6. I'm one of those that heavily invests in power traits). Mummy doesn't suit my playstyle due to the lowering power trait.<br /> <br /> That isn't to say I wouldn't like playing mummy, because I did. I just didn't like that I couldn't increase my power trait.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see something along the lines of Apotheosis reversing the cycle of loss, but just stopping at one and such... not entertaining for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T10:01:51-08:00","id":83279,"title":"","content":"This is about said to death, but yeah, Mummy and Promethean both are really well-written games that are really hard to play. Also, Mummy is really thematically / aesthetically wayy too concentrated on the whole Egyptian culture, which is a very narrow market there. Lowering power trait, I think, was an interesting and even charming mechanic, but it's really not consistent with other splat's power-stat growth system.<br /> <br /> Which brings me another thing. Mummy is nigh-impossible to crossover, especially in a long-term games. Same detriments come to Prometheans, but I think Mummy suffers for it more. I can only say for my experience, but the big draw for the nWoD is crossover games, and Mummy is quite lacking on that front there. I mean, it CAN be done, but you'd have to give up a lot of themes that makes Mummy for what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T10:32:27-08:00","id":83297,"title":"","content":"Thematically, it should be easy to cross-over with Vampire and possibly even Mage and/or Geist, but yes, generally speaking it takes more work for the storyteller to cross Mummy over with games like Changeling and Werewolf, partially because of Mummy's ingrained cultural bias and metaplot.<br /> <br /> One of the issues I think makes cross-over difficult is that all nWoD games are distinct entities from one another, despite needing the &quot;Core&quot; rulebook to play any of them. Themes are a bit underdeveloped (Hunter, and Geist) or weird (Werewolf, Mage, Promethean and Mummy). On the whole, Vampire and Changeling (and possibly Demon now) do the best job of making players walk the fine line between human and monster. Werewolf could definitely have benefited from a much more humanistic viewpoint (humans are pack animals too) and Mage is simply consequence-free with respect to humanism. Ultimately these are damaging to the horror aspect of these games, as horror is a genre that is based upon the human/other dichotomy.<br /> <br /> Note that I don't mean the current themes of these games should be rewritten. They are popular as is, so expecting a lot of change isn't something I expect or even advocate for. I am trying to articulate what it is about these games that I think makes it hard to run them as HORROR games and to cross them over with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T14:20:59-08:00","id":83464,"title":"","content":"I dont think we'll ever see a Chronicler's guide for mummy, but It's the game that could probably use it the most, giving different takes in the mummy idea, like growing sekhem and that stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/524-angrycucaracha","name":"AngryCucaracha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T14:45:52-08:00","id":83480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=83279#post83279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is about said to death, but yeah, Mummy and Promethean both are really well-written games that are really hard to play. Also, Mummy is really thematically / aesthetically wayy too concentrated on the whole Egyptian culture, which is a very narrow market there. Lowering power trait, I think, was an interesting and even charming mechanic, but it's really not consistent with other splat's power-stat growth system.<br /> <br /> Which brings me another thing. Mummy is nigh-impossible to crossover, especially in a long-term games. Same detriments come to Prometheans, but I think Mummy suffers for it more. I can only say for my experience, but the big draw for the nWoD is crossover games, and Mummy is quite lacking on that front there. I mean, it CAN be done, but you'd have to give up a lot of themes that makes Mummy for what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've just picked up Mummy recently, and I'm looking forward to running it sometime soon. These are two points against it that I see pretty frequently, but I have to admit they rather baffle me. I love that Mummy is focussed on Egyptian culture. I'm not sure why anyone would expect it to be anything else. How often do you hear stories about frozen Incan mummies coming down from the mountaintops as horror antagonists? When I hear &quot;Mummy&quot;, at least in the context of a horror game, there is absolutely nothing springing to mind except the image of the Egyptian mummy. Non-Egyptian stuff doesn't even enter into it. It seems like complaining that all the vampires are rooted in European mythology, rather than being a hodge-podge of different creatures like the Yara-ma-yha-who or Chinese hopping vampires. I really like that there is a solid, unifying mythology, and that they went with a spin on the most archetypical &quot;Mummy&quot; as the basis for that.<br /> <br /> As for crossover games, I have always been under the impression that people playing them are in the minority. I always run my WoD games in closed universes, where the only creatures that exist are those pulled from that particular game's mythology (plus occasional omnipresent blue book stuff, but even that is fairly rare). The game lines are just flat out not balanced against one another gameplay-wise, and it makes it exponentially harder to get a handle on any given line's themes when you're trying to balance it with two or three other games as well. This one is much more of a personal preference though, I guess, but crossover games have never seemed to me like something WoD games ever put much emphasis on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T16:00:29-08:00","id":83558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, I might be being completely unreasonable, CAS might just be a very busy guy, he might not have the sort of time free that Rose or Matt spend on various forums chatting with fans. If so fair enough, I don't know his circumstances and it would be wrong of me to draw any conclusions without having all the facts. </div> </div> </div>The contact that we've been getting with game developers in recent years has us all a bit spoiled (myself included). Game writers tend to be freelancers with multiple projects going at any given point and not all of them are going to be social media gurus, public-relations oriented, or continually available for discussions they are not being paid to have. And even if they love their projects and their fans, they have to concentrate on their daily bread. Given the immediacy of the internet, however, we are expecting more and more of them, whether they are compensated for it or feel up for it or not. Not everyone who signs up to work on a book or game line is prepared to serve it forever after. Having a more organized way of getting updates and spoilers to fans without relying on the writers to promote them themselves would be ideal, if unlikely.<br /> <br /> Mummy might be a difficult sell because it insists on being what it is, but that doesn't mean that its chosen focus or mechanics are mistakes or that they have to work out for the worst. Its success as a game will likely depend on how Storytellers pitch it and run it, since it does demand a lot from the ST and the ST can do a lot to set the tone (and make it sexy to players). Its financial success will depend on a number of factors, including how visibly it's run (at stores, cons, etc.), how much information is available for it online, and whether or not it gets a God-Machine update (even if it's just a short conversion guide to bring it up to speed). But its financial success shouldn't be laid at CAS's feet alone, or even primarily.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say I don't have my own issues with the game; nothing is perfect. But not every game is going to be everyone's cup of tea nor should we expect each line to appeal to everybody. This is part of why the WoD has as many splats as it does, and why it promotes some games that come at things differently (like Promethean and Mummy). If one splat doesn't work for you as written, you can try another or you can take what you like from a splat and rework the rest to suit your tastes. It was refreshing to see Mummy shaking things up, even if it risked offending or turning some folks off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My own attempt to support Mummy has gone well beyond that one game, <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">but it's something</a>, and I do try to post Mummy spoilers and such when I find them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":227,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","user":"KismetRose","date":". 03-03-2014, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T18:04:54-08:00","id":83643,"title":"","content":"I am not convinced that the Egyptian flavor is mandatory. While many mummies still associate themselves with that style, some do not. While exotic forms of mummification could've been utilized, it would've been harder to keep cohesive and might've resembled Atlantis too much. Aside from skin tone and cosmological origin, you can still play Incan or Chinese mummies. While the mummy won't be a native per se, the mindset and style could match. I've even translated the Pillars into Greek and Taoist style vocabulary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T19:10:50-08:00","id":83669,"title":"","content":"I don't mean to sound like I'm blaming CAS. Mummy is my favorite WoD, period, even if I do sound like I complain a lot. I just think the core-book had some things missing and Guildhalls, while answering some questions, left a lot of concerns unanswered. I'm only saying that I wish there was more of a relationship between us fans and the writers so that those concerns could be addressed and help us run the game we love.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KismetRose</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't to say I don't have my own issues with the game; nothing is perfect. But not every game is going to be everyone's cup of tea nor should we expect each line to appeal to everybody. This is part of why the WoD has as many splats as it does, and why it promotes some games that come at things differently (like Promethean and Mummy). If one splat doesn't work for you as written, you can try another or you can take what you like from a splat and rework the rest to suit your tastes. It was refreshing to see Mummy shaking things up, even if it risked offending or turning some folks off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T21:34:06-08:00","id":83756,"title":"","content":"Oh, I know you're a fan, reseru, and I have my own gripes with games, so I dig it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But what you touched on is at the heart of the matter: From a fan's perspective, more access to the writers makes sense and is a great use of time. From a game writer's perspective, the opposite seems to be true (in most ways). It's all too easy for writers to become inundated with all the questions, concerns, and complaints, to the point that they don't have time to actually write for their projects. What's more, the visions that players have for a game line are inevitably going to be at odds with each other and with established goals for the game. There's just no way to please or guide everyone. <br /> <br /> It would be awesome if we could perhaps compile a list of questions, maybe get a vote going, and submit the top 10 for some answers (with a pretty please)...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T23:02:18-08:00","id":83790,"title":"","content":"To briefly bring this thread back to its defining topic, looks like we won't get to see DC as soon as expected since they lost an editor. My Ab sunk a little when I read that. So this changes things slightly, do you think we will see Deceived first or is DC still going to come out sooner? ANY possibility of a mummy book coming out this year? My money is on probably but it will most likely come out much later, probably in the summer.<br /> <br /> And this is the game I thought, &quot;you know what, I love mummies! This is going to be my first WoD game I'll buy all the books for!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T02:46:28-08:00","id":83885,"title":"","content":"Mummy certainly isn't their highest priority.<br /> <br /> (Which is only prudent, insofar as Mummy probably isn't exactly a cash cow for them. Bad for us, but it also brings me back to my original point - it's up to *US* to make sure Mummy sells, so that we motivate Onyx Path to adjust their priorities).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T05:36:36-08:00","id":83909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=83643#post83643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not convinced that the Egyptian flavor is mandatory. While many mummies still associate themselves with that style, some do not. While exotic forms of mummification could've been utilized, it would've been harder to keep cohesive and might've resembled Atlantis too much. Aside from skin tone and cosmological origin, you can still play Incan or Chinese mummies. While the mummy won't be a native per se, the mindset and style could match. I've even translated the Pillars into Greek and Taoist style vocabulary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well for a starter, all those terms for stats and skills are in Egyptian language, and that's a HUGE part of the fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T06:56:49-08:00","id":83926,"title":"","content":"Few interesting additional points brought up in the last couple of posts. <br /> <br /> 1) Is the game too mono-cultured? Personally, I have no problem with the Egyptian emphasis. Do I think it is a problem for other people looking at the game? Absolutely. All the other game lines have made a point of trying to be as universal in their cultural underpinnings as possible. <br /> <br /> Yes Vampire is inherently based off of Eastern European myth. However, the developers made every effort with the different clans to give different cultural bases for each. Bloodlines only made vampires more multicultural and in B&amp;S even the Covenants change from country to country. This same approach was applied to Werewolf, Mage, Promethean, Changeling and Hunter. All are based in one cultures idea of a supernatural &quot;type&quot; at their heart (Werewolf has more in common with Native American ideas then the Western European Werewolf folklore) but branches out into many other cultures ideas of the same type of being an incorporates them all into the splat type. <br /> <br /> Giest and Demon take a different approach by basically paying lip service to their central concept (Ghosts and Demons) while kinda being a deconstruction of that creature type. In addition, they rely on game specific fluff which has little to know precedence in real world folklore traditions. So they effectively side-step the whole issue. <br /> <br /> Mummy is inherently Egyptian, even if its fluff roots in in &quot;proto-Egypt&quot; it uses all the tropes and language we associate with Ancient Egypt and even some the meta stuff relies on its culturally specific nature to say the least. Would the game have been more accessible if they had gone for a more multi-cultural take on Mummy's? Maybe, I would have liked to see the other types e.g. self-mummified, bog mummy's, ice mummy's etc. and this could have been accomplished by using a less culturally focused &quot;Ur&quot; civilization. However, that's neither here nor there really. The fact is that cultural specificity has heard the game to a certain extent. <br /> <br /> 2) Mummy being difficult to Crossover. This points been discussed at length already. The only thing I have to add is that I don't see crossover gamer's in the NWoD as a &quot;minority&quot; (to use Azahul's term) you see a crossover thread spring up at least once a week in the more active forums on this website. Plus I know from the conventions I've been too that its a common practice among many gamer groups. So the issue that Mummy is not crossover friendly is indeed an issue with the game that will have impacted it's reception. <br /> <br /> 3) Writer - Consumer contact. KismetRose brought this one up again from one of my earlier posts. I agree that social media allows for a greater level of interconnection between creators and consumers. Likewise, I believe it makes such communication much more available to constant. Is is detrimental to the writers process? Could be, could not be. <br /> <br /> Rose and Matt have outright admitted that the time they have spent with the fans on the forums has helped them shape games and been useful in weeding out problems that might have otherwise made it through into the final version of said games. Has their correspondence taken away from time they could be writing? Yes. Has the fact that fans have pointed out issue that have meant the writers have had to go back and rewrite things, thereby taking away from their time to write new content? Yes. Have either of these things been inherently bad? No. They've only made the fanbase feel appreciated and hightened the quality of the games being produced. <br /> <br /> I don't believe for a second that any writer in correspondence with the fans is going to take the time out to address every question, complaint and issue people post to them. I do believe they will read these things and answer what they feel is most important or interesting. Ultimately, that's fair. They have lives and jobs to be getting on with and them taking the time to answer such things is a blessing for us. Considering the common sense factor involved. I honestly don't think any amount of fan feedback will &quot;stop a writer from writing&quot;. <br /> <br /> I don't know how many projects CAS is juggling. I don't know his schedule or his workload at the moment. So I can't say anything for certain. What I can say from the evidence I have is that CAS was enthused about Mummy, it was a vision of a game he had in his mind since the OWoD version came out. In every interview his love for the game has come across. He was obviously passionate about it. He wanted it to be a good game with interesting things going on. <br /> <br /> Given all that, I would expect him to care about the feedback the fans of the game are giving him via social media. As its the best lipnus test he has to see about the games reception and what people might want from it as the line progresses. At least perhaps indulging in the basically interesting activity of having a bit of banter on the forums with the fans. From what evidence I have it's not like the Mummy fan base inundated him with requests, complaints and questions. From what I have seen on this forum at least we've been slinging around the same old complaints and questions since shortly after the game came out. Sure some of these questions are &quot;spoilers&quot; for the metaplot getting revealed as the game line continues. Others are not and it would hurt no one for them to be answered or explained. <br /> <br /> 4) DC's editor problems. Personally, I'm glad they got a new editor. Considering that the last one had not finished editing a 100 page book in 7 WEEKS! I mean come on, even part time that's a joke. I know editors (part time ones) and they have got through 300 pages of text in 2 weeks. Hopefully the new editor won't be such a joker and actually get on with it. Also am I the only one thinking they should have put out for art while the 7 WEEKS of editing were going on? That way the book could have gone straight into layout.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T08:23:31-08:00","id":83965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rose and Matt have outright admitted that the time they have spent with the fans on the forums has helped them shape games and been useful in weeding out problems that might have otherwise made it through into the final version of said games. </div> </div> </div>And it sounds like Rose and Matt are quite comfortable with the whole arrangement and are using it to their benefit, which is awesome! I suppose my point here is that not all game writers can be expected to be the same in regard to social media, feedback, or fan interactions. To some, it is a joy; to others, a necessary evil; and to more than a few, it is an outright intrusion and something to be avoided. We see this with all creative types and entertainment. Now, whether writers will be able to stay away from social media and be as successful and well-distributed is another matter (and worth some consideration, to be sure).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I honestly don't think any amount of fan feedback will &quot;stop a writer from writing&quot;. </div> </div> </div>It has seemed to me that so many things strive to get in your way when you're writing, whether it's for fun or for profit, so it's not about whether they'll stop writing as much as how delayed their projects will become. And delays only make fans even more (understandably) cross, as we've seen here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In every interview his love for the game has come across. He was obviously passionate about it. He wanted it to be a good game with interesting things<br /> going on. Given all that, I would expect him to care about the feedback the fans of the game are giving him via social media. </div> </div> </div>Just to continue to play devil's advocate, consider that he can be perfectly passionate about the game without necessarily caring about feedback via social media whatsoever. One does not necessarily lead to or imply the other. Much depends on one's process, inclinations, and priorities. This is part of why I wish we had a buffer or filter between the writers and the fans, someone or some group that could help organize the flow of spoilers and feedback released to the fans so that regardless of the writer's online time, information would get passed along. They need a good PR person/secretary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T09:38:23-08:00","id":84012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=82216#post82216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like mummy, however, as others have said a lot of my personal hangup is that I can't increase my power trait back up without well, burning out for a while.<br /> <br /> It is definitely an interesting system, and the thought of starting off ridiculously powerful and in the throws of rage is awesome. I just don't particularly want to not be able to get back to that and stay there over the course of a long game (In the vampire game I'm currently in and have played for around a year or more I'm sitting at BP 6. I'm one of those that heavily invests in power traits). Mummy doesn't suit my playstyle due to the lowering power trait.<br /> <br /> That isn't to say I wouldn't like playing mummy, because I did. I just didn't like that I couldn't increase my power trait.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see something along the lines of Apotheosis reversing the cycle of loss, but just stopping at one and such... not entertaining for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside...and noting you probably won't see this.<br /> <br /> Since Guildhalls the whole losing Sekhem thing is really a non-Issue. An organised Mummy (and you've had 6000 years as a character to get organised) can quite happily sling around Tier 3 Utterances at Sekhem 1.<br /> <br /> Use of a common Affinity allows for bottling of supercharged Utterances above and beyond that for future use. Correct use of the Affinity that raises your effective Sekhem helps further.<br /> <br /> A Mummy that has achieved Apotheosis but retains their powerful Talisman has an effective Sekhem rating equal to their Memory stat AND access to most or all of their Utterances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:23:07-08:00","id":84039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=83926#post83926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't know how many projects CAS is juggling. I don't know his schedule or his workload at the moment. So I can't say anything for certain. What I can say from the evidence I have is that CAS was enthused about Mummy, it was a vision of a game he had in his mind since the OWoD version came out. In every interview his love for the game has come across. He was obviously passionate about it. He wanted it to be a good game with interesting things going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there was a lot of excitement on this forum and rpg.net leading up to Mummy's release where he and the others were posting a lot of previews and hints. Then the game is released and there's silence.<br /> <br /> I know it's not fair because we don't know how much CAS necessarily has going on, including his personal life, but aren't there deadlines for these books? I know OP is playing it looser with their time-scale and there's the Monday Meeting schedule of works-in-progress, but Book of the Deceived is going on a four month delay from its re-worked scheduling and, last blog entry I read, it was beingredlined?!<br /> <br /> At the very least I'd like to hear more of why the books are being delayed. DC has an editor issue? Okay, fair enough. Can't we still get a preview? We don't need a .pdf preview, just a couple of blurbs on a blog for it like the one preview they blogged for <i>Guildhalls</i>.<br /> <br /> It's not that they necessarily owe it to us. It's that I don't understand why, a year and a half ago, there was all this developer and writer talk and now there's none. It's that I don't understand why we were told we'd be getting <i>Book of the Deceived</i> previews in October or November and there hasn't been one and it's March. It's that I don't understand why the DC preview we were promised hasn't shown up after a month either. It's that I don't understand why CAS posted on this forum saying he 'was on' as if to imply his brain would be readily available for us to pick it and he hasn't shown up since except to promise previews that never come.<br /> <br /> <br /> PS: I love Mummy's Egyptian mood but I hope, and half expect, that later supplements will explore post-Iremite attempts at the Rite which will inevitably be Lifeless mockeries for the Arisen to run around and beat up, whether they're Chinese or Incan styled Mummies or some weird, new concepts (hopefully both)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:41:47-08:00","id":84054,"title":"","content":"The vocabulary isn't all that hard to replace (except for the Guilds, which is the hardest bit of Egyptian to avoid). In game, since the major NPCs were among the deathless who got REALLY into the Diaspora, most of our vocabulary is mixed. One mummy spent a lot of time in India and China--KotE's soul aspects translated, if a bit roughly, into the Pillars. Anyone with access to the 2e Mummy or M:tR from the cWod has access to a bit of mummy-related jargon from at least a handful of cultures that could be translated without too much work. I did my greek ones from scratch in five minutes (helps that Pathos, Logos, and Ethos already come as a package deal). To anyone who has the concept of a non-egyptian mummy, I'd suggest giving it a try. Its amazing how much of Irem you can remove from a game (especially considering Memory). While it may not be as easy to make &quot;any mummy you can imagine&quot; as it is for other nwod games, its still possible. I'm pretty sure that not ALL ambiguity was taken from the game. Some of the gaps regard the ST section could be deliberate so as to allow ST's some degree of the other nwod's cosmological flexibility. It could be that, due to the specific details we've been given, that we are expecting most things to have specific, spoilerable answers. They may not--the devs may have liked one M. Night Shamalan twist with a specific piece of information that is objectively true, but left the other &quot;truths&quot; in ST hands as usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T15:25:15-08:00","id":84246,"title":"","content":"I'll confess, my knowledge of the details of Vampire is a bit shaky, but the Clans all look like different aspects of classic European vampires. At first glance, it really doesn't look any more multicultural than Mummy.<br /> <br /> The thing I find puzzling about the monocultural complaints is that all of these Chinese, Incan, and bog Mummies aren't really... well, monsters. They're just preserved corpses. If there are common stories or mythologies revolving around what they are and what they might do, they have gone completely over my head. There is nothing like we have for Egyptian mummies. Whether because of modern movies or books, or because of actual myths, we actually have a concept of the Egyptian mummy as a monster. For the others, they're really just dead bodies that happen to have been well-preserved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T17:08:15-08:00","id":84289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=84246#post84246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll confess, my knowledge of the details of Vampire is a bit shaky, but the Clans all look like different aspects of classic European vampires. At first glance, it really doesn't look any more multicultural than Mummy.<br /> <br /> The thing I find puzzling about the monocultural complaints is that all of these Chinese, Incan, and bog Mummies aren't really... well, monsters. They're just preserved corpses. If there are common stories or mythologies revolving around what they are and what they might do, they have gone completely over my head. There is nothing like we have for Egyptian mummies. Whether because of modern movies or books, or because of actual myths, we actually have a concept of the Egyptian mummy as a monster. For the others, they're really just dead bodies that happen to have been well-preserved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The clans are different archetypes of portrayals of vampires but they're by no means 'multi-cultural.' For that you'd have to look to <i>Night Horrors: Wicked Dead</i> for other cultural takes on vampires as well as new spins, like a blood-borne disease-thing or a writhing pile of maggots.<br /> <br /> THAT'S what I'd want to see for Mummy: quasi-Egyptian comes first, follow up with 'cultural' and new, weird mummies as Lifeless antagonists in a later supplement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T17:42:47-08:00","id":84304,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sure. That works. I'm all for all kinds of craziness in a Night Horrors book. But as priorities go, it's pretty far down there, and doesn't have a whole lot to do with the main line. As an appendix of antagonists for a game with a heavy pulp focus, it's a fantastic idea, but I don't think it would do much to stave off the monoculture criticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T06:03:33-08:00","id":85266,"title":"","content":"Okay, everyone! Time for the thread to get back on track as this Monday Meeting's blog has some relevant updates for us Mummy fans!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mummy the Curse </b>- <b>Cursed Necropolis DC</b> is in editing. We actually had an editor have to drop off this, so this editor is a new editor.<br /> <br /> <b>Book of the Deceived</b> (MtC): Redlines. The loss of a writer means their section has to be given to a new writer, CAS is on top of it</div> </div> </div> </div>So these upcoming Mummy releases have fallen prey to some setbacks but luckily they're pulling through! Also, Rich commented on some...vocal, opinionated folks on the various forums; not that it's anyone of us in this particular thread, necessarily, so we'll just fall back on blaming the Exalted forums as usual. Still, I'm reassured that not only our sometimes negative criticisms are being heard, but also our passion for the game and our desire to see it shine with success!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T13:39:37-08:00","id":85593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=85266#post85266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So these upcoming Mummy releases have fallen prey to some setbacks but luckily they're pulling through! Also, Rich commented on some...vocal, opinionated folks on the various forums; not that it's anyone of us in this particular thread, necessarily, so we'll just fall back on blaming the Exalted forums as usual. Still, I'm reassured that not only our sometimes negative criticisms are being heard, but also our passion for the game and our desire to see it shine with success!</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that us? The worst thing we've said about CAS is that he could have planned stuff out better and been more vocal in the forums. The third comment on that blog post was how Mage Awakening sucks. We've been pretty civil so far. No personal attacks or dismissing people that have said they're not fans of Mummy. I like the mummy forums.<br /> <br /> As for the news, it's good we actually have some (maybe they're listening to us!) even if it's not great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T14:09:15-08:00","id":85615,"title":"","content":"A couple people commented on the Monday Meeting blog asking about Mummy love. Here's what we got!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll talk to CAS about getting some new info up, and popping into the forums more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think we've been fairly civil, too, but I'll still eat crow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T17:25:02-08:00","id":85733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RisTigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=85593#post85593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was that us? The worst thing we've said about CAS is that he could have planned stuff out better and been more vocal in the forums. The third comment on that blog post was how Mage Awakening sucks. We've been pretty civil so far. No personal attacks or dismissing people that have said they're not fans of Mummy. I like the mummy forums.<br /> <br /> As for the news, it's good we actually have some (maybe they're listening to us!) even if it's not great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm almost certain that Rich's notes were not aimed at the Mummy fans. We've been civil in our exchange of ideas and viewpoints about the game and CAS's handling of the line. At worst we've (by which I mean I) have been a little bolshy.<br /> <br /> I'd lack to thank Reseru and Lazarus for requesting more info about the upcoming Mummy books then the bare minimum of stuff the Monday morning meeting notes are making. I for one am dying to know more about the creation process. As the necessarily brief reports from the Monday Morning notes sometimes confuse me frankly (Redlining for 3 months? Editing for 7 weeks?).<br /> <br /> As for how the lines next to books are coming:-<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy the Curse </b><i>- </i><b>Cursed Necropolis DC</b><i> is in editing. We actually had an editor have to drop off this, so this editor is a new editor.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Book of the Deceived</b><i> (MtC): Redlines. The loss of a writer means their section has to be given to a new writer, CAS is on top of it</i><br /> <br /> My brains response -<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Hippocampus:</b></span>HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAH!!!!! (sound of breaking glass)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Neocortex: </b>I do believe he's had a psychotic break old boy.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Frontal Lobe:</span> </span></span></b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Looks like it old chum...whatever shall we do?</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> You get the idea.<br /> <br /> Its unfortunate that they had a writer drop of the project, we can all agree that sucks.<br /> <br /> Though I must question while whole section of the book have yet to finalized considering that writing supposedly started on Book of the Deceived in November. At this point I'm kinda just hoping that CAS writes the section himself because that will (hopefully/theoretically) save time.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I thought I was being conservative back in November saying that Deceived would be a March or April release. Seems I was being overly optimistic. I think I'll reset my expectations to August 2014. Basically, Deceived seems to have inherented the core books curse of every possible thing that could happen to delay its release has happened At current we are looking at something is going to have what is looking like an 8 month delay (original release date was October 2013, revised one was December 2013, at current it looking like a June 2014 release that's a 6-8 month delay depending on how you count it)<br /> <br /> At current I am basically holding onto the thin, thin thread of hope that the new editor for DC is actually on the ball (as the old one evidently was not 7 Weeks to edit at best a 120 page text, that's just...I have no words) and that DC shoots through the rest of development by mid-April. I'm not counting on it though.<br /> <br /> Right....rant done, seam vented, reactor core stable.<br /> <br /> P.s Not to rub salt in the Mummy scheduling wound, but I can't help but notice that all the extra Kickstarter Demon projects have all gone into first draft within a month of one another and within 2.5 months of the Kickstarter finishing. About a third of Mummy's are not even scheduled yet and we only know that Rio and Dreams have had writers &quot;approached for negotiations&quot; due to a single e-mail way back in November. Once again, either Demon's popularity seems to be getting it fast-tracked (ala Changeling) or the Demon dev crew seem to be a lot more on the ball.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 03-07-2014, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T23:55:34-08:00","id":85867,"title":"","content":"Could also be that it's easier to find writers who want to write for Demon than Mummy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T03:53:43-07:00","id":87402,"title":"","content":"Probably, though if it takes way longer than usual to complete a project, then some questions must be answered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T23:34:52-07:00","id":89280,"title":"","content":"Just to keep the thread going, let's look at the new updates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mummy the Curse </b>- <b>Cursed Necropolis DC</b> is in editing. </div> </div> </div>Looks like DC is back on track. Hopefully this new editor will be a bit faster than the last one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Book of the Deceived</b> (MtC): Redlines. The loss of a writer means their section has to be given to a new writer, CAS is on top of it. </div> </div> </div>Still nothing new here. Oh well. Hope springs eternal for mummy fans.<br /> <br /> Final bit of news, Eve of Judgment is on sale for GM Day. If you've got the full Mummy the Curse book then you've already got this story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T00:52:40-07:00","id":90726,"title":"","content":"I think a main incentive to doing Apotheosis is their ability to create new Relics, which is something that your vanilla Arisen can't do. Freedom from the chronic memory loss is another as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T08:56:48-07:00","id":91672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=85615#post85615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think we've been fairly civil, too, but I'll still eat crow</div> </div> </div> </div>Right now, yes, but I seem to recall the forum got heated when the core book was delayed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T03:00:46-07:00","id":92202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=90726#post90726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a main incentive to doing Apotheosis is their ability to create new Relics, which is something that your vanilla Arisen can't do. Freedom from the chronic memory loss is another as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...take your Talisman with you and you can still throw around potentially up to Tier 2 and even 3 Utterances (some Utterances are 1, 2, 4 while others are 1, 3, 5. The 1, 2, 4s can be used at Tier 2 without needing to have them stored in your Talisman dots at all), use of the Affinity that buffs your Sekhem while in your Tomb and the Affinity for storing Utterances (or is that a Guild Affinity? Do you lose those if you reach Apotheosis? I don;t remember anything saying you do) means you could store multiple instances of high power Utterances for use while out and about.<br /> <br /> So Sekhem 1 is not necessarily a huge limiter on your ability to use your mightiest powers and that in concert with the fact you treat your Memory (at least 7 I believe?) as your Sekhem for other purposes means you can spend Pillars to buff your stats efficiently as well and have a better dice pool on all of those opposed Stat+Sekhem rolls than most Mummies you meet. Just stay away from the newly arisen for a couple of days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T14:40:34-07:00","id":94473,"title":"","content":"I know there's a thread up about it, but here's the update for this one because relevance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mummy: the Curse Facebook page</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And CURSED NECROPOLIS: D.C. has finally made its way to layout!<br /> <br /> Stay tuned for a proper spoiler post.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T19:54:58-07:00","id":94655,"title":"","content":"Not to be a buzzkill (though I may secretly enjoy such a practice) but I think we've all seen projects been in layout for two months plus before. Art still needs to be sorted and then their's the approval process before we get the rough pdf. I'm still expecting a late April release at earliest for this one. <br /> <br /> I do however like that the new editor took 2/3 weeks to do what took the last one 7 before the change over happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T10:04:06-07:00","id":95013,"title":"","content":"It comes when it comes. I stopped paying attention to the updates in the Monday blogs for Mummy stuff a while ago. Seemed like a rather irrelevant thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T01:11:01-07:00","id":98187,"title":"","content":"Here's the Monday Meeting update!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mummy the Curse </b>- <b>Cursed Necropolis DC</b> is in layout and art is coming in.<br /> <b>Book of the Deceived</b> (MtC): Redlines. The loss of a writer means their section has to be given to a new writer, CAS is on top of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>DC</i> is in layout! Things really picked up speed for this once it got the new editor, so hopefully we'll see this book released sometime in April!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T07:23:27-07:00","id":98328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=98187#post98187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>DC</i> is in layout! Things really picked up speed for this once it got the new editor, so hopefully we'll see this book released sometime in April!</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. I hope it will be out towards the end of April as a realistic estimate. Maybe mid-May at the latest. Deceived...that's anyones guess off the very limited info we have about that book at current. In my head I'm thinking early July, giving them another 3 and a half months to progress. <br /> <br /> I'm still sorta confused about the writer thing. Not that it happened or that a person had to drop a book, that sorta thing happens. Its that the idea of getting a section re-written at the point the book was at seems odd. <br /> <br /> From the updates we know that first drafts of Deceived finished up in late November last year redlining happened and then second drafts happened and then CAS was redlining those second drafts. Now, with most books it seems they go through two lots of redlining then move on to editing. Sure their are some exceptions that have three lots of redlining. However, if Deceived was allowing normal standard for most books released by Onyx path CAS just needed to finish redlining the second batch before editing could happen. Now it seems likely that different writers were getting their stuff to him to redline at different times, hence the reason the process has taken a while. <br /> <br /> Now one of the writers drops out for whatever reasons, life happens and all that. However, we can assume that said writer was working on the second draft version of his section. Meaning that he's closer to what CAS finally wants in the section then when the writer started presumably. Now it seems CAS is either currently sorting out a replacement writer or has already done so (we don't know what &quot;on top of it&quot; really means) to start the section the same way all the other writers started their with his outlines presumably. <br /> <br /> However, would it not be quicker and easier for CAS to take what the original writer had (which is likely at least partially in second draft) and finish it himself (obviously still crediting the writer for his work, no plagiarism)? After all CAS stressed in his few updates that he's personally working on Book of the Deceived as well as just being the developer/overviewer. <br /> <br /> Surely that would be quicker, get CAS exactly what he wants out of the section anyway and not delay and already hugely delayed book for a game line that atrophying from lack of releases, niche nature and a general lack of an integrated community. <br /> <br /> \u200bI know there is a lot of assumption in the above theory/line of questioning. I would like to be more specific but we simply don't have the info in the community to make more solid statements about how the Mummy books are being made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T10:37:01-07:00","id":98466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=98328#post98328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surely that would be quicker, get CAS exactly what he wants out of the section anyway and not delay and already hugely delayed book for a game line that atrophying from lack of releases, niche nature and a general lack of an integrated community.</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite all that I would prefer a re-write, if CAS felt there needed to be one, and have a higher quality book than to have it sooner","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T11:40:54-07:00","id":98512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=98466#post98466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Despite all that I would prefer a re-write, if CAS felt there needed to be one, and have a higher quality book than to have it sooner</div> </div> </div> </div>See also &quot;it's only late until it ships.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T18:25:07-07:00","id":98839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=98466#post98466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite all that I would prefer a re-write, if CAS felt there needed to be one, and have a higher quality book than to have it sooner</div> </div> </div> </div>I get you. I'm a big fan of quality over quantity too and I do support the approach that Onyx Path has taken to make sure that its products are the quality that its writers and creative team want them to be before releasing them to the fans. <br /> <br /> It's just that without knowing context to frame the re-write decision it just hangs appears as another delay to a project that is along the most delayed in Onyx Path history as is. If one goes by original release estimates at the time of the Mummy Kickstarter Deceived was first scheduled for October/November last year I believe. So 6 months and its not out of writing yet.<br /> <br /> (I'm not 100% on that, as the schedule for this book has changed about 5 times)<br /> <br /> I mean the Players Guide for Demon is going to likely be about 4 months (it was originally scheduled for December) by the time it comes out but its been very, very steady with its progress and its always been &quot;moving forward&quot; in some way. Deceived seems to have been stuck where it is for the entirety of its development history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T17:03:17-07:00","id":103722,"title":"","content":"Welcome to April! Here's what we got:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mummy the Curse </b>- <b>Cursed Necropolis DC</b> is in layout and art &amp; maps are in.<br /> <b>Book of the Deceived</b> (MtC): Redlines. The loss of a writer means their section has to be given to a new writer, CAS is on top of it.<br /> <b>nWoD: Dark Eras:</b> Second drafts except for one chapter which is in first drafts.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>DC</i> is so close I can almost taste it. Let's keep track of <i>Dark Eras</i>, too, since it's technically going to be a Mummy supplement, too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> With second drafts already going on in April, I'm feeling confident about its August release","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T06:06:57-07:00","id":103988,"title":"","content":"Cursed Necropolis DC is listed as 5/7, meaning that it should be pre-released as PDF to backers any day now, then after errata corrections about another month before general release &amp; POD. BotD is listed as April, but its 2/7, meaning that it probably takes another 3-4 months away. We just have to be patient folks, if the Mummy core was any indication, this project moves at super slow Arisen speed...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T07:11:21-07:00","id":104022,"title":"","content":"If DC can be released to us in April awesome. I've become utterly cynical of Mummy though when it comes to new content. So I won't be surprised if its a May release. <br /> <br /> Luckily I have found a solution, namely get distracted by other lines. I've got a load of Demon the Descent stuff to catch up on, so that's taking my time at the moment. Mage the Ascension too. I can enjoy those and when Mummy graces us with a release I won't have been sitting on hooks waiting for it above all other WoD books for the last 6 months.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I'm happy to take this viewpoint for the next 4/5 years until/if they do a Mummy chronicle book and finally bring it up to date with the rest of the updated NWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T04:49:06-07:00","id":104757,"title":"","content":"I'll admit I've been looking over <i>Monsterhearts</i>, and I'm giving second reads to <i>Mouseguard</i> and <i>Atlantis: the Second Age</i> (since <i>Geographica</i> came out yay!).<br /> <br /> With that said, <i>Mummy</i> is the first game I've run since <i>D&amp;D 3.5</i> almost ten years ago, and it is the first game I've used to introduce my partner to the hobby. It has a special place in my heart, and anytime I lose interest I just listen to DaveB's <i>Mummy</i> podcast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T05:44:53-07:00","id":104778,"title":"","content":"Link to the podcast please? :-)<br /> <br /> Mummy also has a special place in my heart, Im the only ST running it for DGS, been running it for over a year now and making do with the core and Guildhalls. Added content, teasers and bonus materials are great to have, just wondering why we dont get them on the Mummy blog or Facebook page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":311,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","user":"JoeB","date":". 04-03-2014, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T07:38:05-07:00","id":104812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=104778#post104778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Link to the podcast please? :-)<br /> <br /> Mummy also has a special place in my heart, Im the only ST running it for DGS, been running it for over a year now and making do with the core and Guildhalls. Added content, teasers and bonus materials are great to have, just wondering why we dont get them on the Mummy blog or Facebook page.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that would require some engagement with the game's community. <br /> <br /> Every since the Core came out last March (for general release) its become increasingly apparent that CAS has no interest in fostering a Mummy community or having dialogue with the games fans. <br /> <br /> Honestly, if you look pre-Core release there were the blog posts, yes they got increasingly delayed as things went on but they were a thing. When the Kickstarter happened a lot of people joined in on it and it got a good community going while it lasted. Rich T was overseeing that for the most part though. Shortly after its release we got a couple of Kickstarter e-mails, a Dark Days Radio Podcast, a two part interview and then a single Guildhalls teaser. Around the Guildhalls release CAS came and made about 3 posts on the then &quot;new&quot; forums. Since then its been utterly silent. <br /> <br /> Weirdly, I'm not actually surprised by this in retrospect. I reread CAS's old interview the other day and re-listened to the Dark Days podcast. I get the impression from it all that CAS has a very clear vision of what he wants Mummy to be. He has a VISION for the game. This makes sense, according to sources he's had this idea and wanted to implement it since at least the time he was writing Mummy the Resurrection. <br /> <br /> If he has a solid idea of what Mummy is and can be and what it is not and can't be that's fine. I do get the impression that its making him want everything to be 110% perfect before he even tried to develop it further. Sounds awesome right? Means every product released is going to be super high quality. Yeah maybe, but it also means its utterly shaped to the developers preference and what he deems right or wrong for the setting a game line. If things have to be one persons version of perfect, then that can degrade their appeal to people who don't share that vision. Plus, we've all worked with perfectionists everything takes 3 times as long and their's no guarantee anythings is better then it was before the perfectionist nick-picked and corrected it for the Nth time. <br /> <br /> CAS's negative attitude and dismissal of Crossover stuff in interviews is a good example of developer vision hurting the wider appeal of the game. CAS sees Mummy as a game concerned with the (and I use the term loosely) metaplot of the history of Irem, the Shan'Iatu and the quest for Apothesis. That's a fine set of things for the game to run off when combined with the PC's personal history and memory and such. However, being so consumed with the idea that a player and ST have to engage with that aspect that one does not provide support for if an ST or player wants to take the game in a different direction (say a cross over with Mage about hunting down ancient relics that may be Atlantian or may be Iremian and something else is afoot with the Seers) is restrictive and looses the broader appeal the game could have. All of this because the game is so tailored to the vision of the developer. <br /> <br /> If the developer has such a strong standpoint on the game, then why would he go and get feedback from the community? Why engage with them other then to reveal the occassional preview so that they can get a feel for whats coming and talk about how awesome the new stuff is? The only time open-development (as for the new chronicle books or V20 line books) or lots of community intensive discussion (as for Demon the Descent) works is if the devs are interested in getting the community's input on the game and letting them shape it in some tiny way. Otherwise that stuff is just time and energy the dev could be using to write the game line. <br /> <br /> I don't want to sound like the Mummy devs &quot;owe&quot; the fans anything. They don't we have no real ownership of the game, its not &quot;ours&quot; its a great bit of fiction that we can use as a spring pad for our imaginations to have a fun time. As such we should be thankful for the fact that the devs came up with this stuff. I am. Honestly, despite all the bitching and the disagreements I might have over the way the Mummy line is being handled and developed I am greatful that it exists. Likewise, I know how easy it is to sit here behind the anonymity of the internet and cut into hard working peoples efforts and generally be negative. I'm aware how much harder it is to be writing these books and continuing to develop this line and setting. <br /> <br /> The only thing I want to add to that is that I'm a big believer in &quot;death of the author&quot;. People take what they take out of a story. The author can intend to imply or want to imply or outright state certain things with their writing. That's great and I'm happy to listen to their explanations of this stuff and treat it as &quot;cannon&quot;. At the same time, books and games are different. Your audience is going to want a wider array of possible interpretations and uses out of the writing of a game. As a game's writer surely then its benefits you to at least make a nod or effort towards options or interpretations outside of those you see as cannon. Even if they are 100 word long sidebars. <br /> <br /> Wow, this ended up being a lot longer then I intended...stupid rants. Going to take a step back again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T22:53:31-07:00","id":106744,"title":"","content":"Hi, guys,<br /> <br /> Apologies for not being very accessible of late. As some have said, I'm responsible for quite a bit in the overall Onyx Path operation, and so I'm not quite as online and interactive as some of my OPP colleagues and developers.<br /> <br /> But I'm back (and there's a new teaser post up; as announced, <i>D.C.</i> actually is in layout!), and if there's any questions you have, I'm happy to answer them here. You can also expect to see a new Development Tease for every project with which I'm involved, as they roll into the queue.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your interest in our stuff, and for your patience with the various and sundry demands on my time.<br /> <br /> C.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T23:41:48-07:00","id":106754,"title":"","content":"Damn, CAS! You beat me to the thread's update! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm not at home so I can't post more at the moment, but I'm going to read the preview now! Thank you for the game, CAS, and tolerating our impatience <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T01:16:04-07:00","id":106781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=104812#post104812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CAS's negative attitude and dismissal of Crossover stuff in interviews is a good example of developer vision hurting the wider appeal of the game. CAS sees Mummy as a game concerned with the (and I use the term loosely) metaplot of the history of Irem, the Shan'Iatu and the quest for Apothesis. That's a fine set of things for the game to run off when combined with the PC's personal history and memory and such. However, being so consumed with the idea that a player and ST have to engage with that aspect that one does not provide support for if an ST or player wants to take the game in a different direction (say a cross over with Mage about hunting down ancient relics that may be Atlantian or may be Iremian and something else is afoot with the Seers) is restrictive and looses the broader appeal the game could have. All of this because the game is so tailored to the vision of the developer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any good reason as for why Colin should give us a Mummy game that isn't true to its roots and its basic mythology. Given the little wordcount available - it's not like we're going to get a new Mummy book every month- I want Mummy books to include Mummy content. Crossover is optional, and, indeed, undesirable. Make something up yourself; the system and setting already lends itself well towards creative hacking.<br /> <br /> There are, in my opinion at least, plenty of aspects of the Mummy setting that benefit from being explored in more detail - there's absolutely no need to go off topic and do crossover.<br /> <br /> Also - respectfully, if I was the Mummy developer I'd stay the hell away from this forum after reading that sort of thing. Have you ever considered that this kind of thing is the reason as for why Colin doesn't interact with the Mummy community around here all that much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T01:40:19-07:00","id":106789,"title":"","content":"Well crossover should be , of course , fleshed out by the players , but smaler Stuff like the stereotypical view or some historical count of Interaction would be nice.<br /> <br /> <br /> btw while talking of Crossover , as iremember seeing somewhere in on of the Mage books (Imperial Mysteries i guess but not sure) , a picture of a Mage who had some kind of Vision . In said vison one can see Wahinington DC with a Ziggurat, from wich a light comes form. A possible clue or just coincidence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T01:49:29-07:00","id":106790,"title":"","content":"That's a picture of the Prince of 100,000 Leaves, an Annunaki that was introduced in Awakening's first ever supplement, long before Mummy was a glimmer in a necromancer's eye. There won't be any mummy/mage crossover books. CAS doesn't want to do one, <i>I</i> don't want to do one. We'd both have to change our minds, then persuade Rich to change <i>his</i> mind, then persuade CCP to sign off on it, and we both have plenty of book ideas for the lines as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T04:38:08-07:00","id":106827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=106781#post106781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see any good reason as for why Colin should give us a Mummy game that isn't true to its roots and its basic mythology. Given the little wordcount available - it's not like we're going to get a new Mummy book every month- I want Mummy books to include Mummy content. Crossover is optional, and, indeed, undesirable. Make something up yourself; the system and setting already lends itself well towards creative hacking.<br /> <br /> There are, in my opinion at least, plenty of aspects of the Mummy setting that benefit from being explored in more detail - there's absolutely no need to go off topic and do crossover.<br /> <br /> Also - respectfully, if I was the Mummy developer I'd stay the hell away from this forum after reading that sort of thing. Have you ever considered that this kind of thing is the reason as for why Colin doesn't interact with the Mummy community around here all that much?</div> </div> </div> </div>Christian man speaks truth.<br /> <br /> I was discussing this with C.A. not too long ago in fact. Mummy doesn't exist in a vacuum, but the Arisen do very much have their own path, their own vision and their own masters. They also exist at arbitrary points in time not decided by them, so any relationships they make with an individual werewolf or entire covenant may well pass and fade as quickly as Memory. If the Judges do not will the Arisen to recall his agreements with this Promethean, then why should the mummy have a preconceived opinion of that supernatural being?<br /> <br /> I don't object to crossover of course, but in a game like Mummy I suspect that it would be hard for Arisen &quot;society&quot; to form a complete picture or stereotype of any other supernatural. It's going to be so subjective based on personal Deathless experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T09:18:08-07:00","id":106932,"title":"","content":"Through the Dread Powers system, at least Hunter: Mortal Remains is going to be an official book that crosses over Mummies into the Vigil setting. That should be fun. Mummies make for great crossover NPCs. I wouldn't want to use them as PCs in a mixed game due to the mechanics of the Descent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T11:01:47-07:00","id":106984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=106781#post106781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't see any good reason as for why Colin should give us a Mummy game that isn't true to its roots and its basic mythology. Given the little wordcount available - it's not like we're going to get a new Mummy book every month- I want Mummy books to include Mummy content. Crossover is optional, and, indeed, undesirable. Make something up yourself; the system and setting already lends itself well towards creative hacking.<br /> <br /> There are, in my opinion at least, plenty of aspects of the Mummy setting that benefit from being explored in more detail - there's absolutely no need to go off topic and do crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, the crossover issue got take out of context. <br /> <br /> To clear that issue up, particularly now that devs like Dave B have weighed in on the issue. I am not nor was I ever saying that there should be an entire book in the Mummy line that is dedicated to crossover with other lines. As Dave B said, I can imagine most people don't want to do them and frankly they aren't needed. <br /> <br /> What I was talking about was the idea of one of the Mummy books having between 6-10 pages of fluff about Mummy's interaction with other Supernaturals. Combined with bits of crunch that might come up e.g. if a Mummy can be fed off by a vampire, are Mummy's immune to the blood-bond etc. That's it, the same basic treatment on the issue that every game line so far published for the NWoD has done. <br /> <br /> Likewise, Christian A, I agree with your point of view that the Mummy setting would benefit from being explored in a lot of detail by its splat books. One of the issues I had with the Core was how incomplete it felt in a lot of regards. Each of the splat books is amending this issue but its still an issue. For a &quot;complete&quot; game of Mummy I believe you'd need: The Core, Guildhalls, DC, Deceived and Sothis. While personally I don't hold the fact that five books are necessary to run a complete game I can see some people taking umbridge with it when you compare it to a lot of other game lines that one can run with a single book (Promethean, Demon) or a couple (Mage, Werewolf). <br /> <br /> Even after those five books I think something to further flesh out antagonists, a book on duat/the judges/ammut, a book on cults and a book on apotheosis would all be important to really round out the setting. Not as vital as the five books I mentioned above but nice to have. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=106781#post106781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I was discussing this with C.A. not too long ago in fact. Mummy doesn't exist in a vacuum, but the Arisen do very much have their own path, their own vision and their own masters. They also exist at arbitrary points in time not decided by them, so any relationships they make with an individual werewolf or entire covenant may well pass and fade as quickly as Memory. If the Judges do not will the Arisen to recall his agreements with this Promethean, then why should the mummy have a preconceived opinion of that supernatural being?<br /> <br /> I don't object to crossover of course, but in a game like Mummy I suspect that it would be hard for Arisen &quot;society&quot; to form a complete picture or stereotype of any other supernatural. It's going to be so subjective based on personal Deathless experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see this point as valid on the Micro level. Individual Arisen may not really have &quot;sterotypes&quot; about the other supernaturals sure. It just does not hold water on a Marco level though. The Guilds don't keep info on the other Sups that they have had literally millennia to observe infiltrate human society? Really. <br /> <br /> The Su-Menet don't have any info on the various Necromantic Supernaturals e.g. Sin-Eaters, certain Vampires etc? <br /> <br /> The Maa-Keep don't keep tabs on the way that the Seers or the Vampires pull a lot of strings in mortal society? Though surely these groups are their main competition? <br /> <br /> The Sesha-Hesbu with all their knowledge gathering, secret keeping and occult research have never found out about any of the other Supernaturals? <br /> <br /> This is without even mentioning the general trend of Mages and Sin-Eaters to also go after items that Mummy's might be chasing as Relics? Really, no record at all of the competition? <br /> <br /> While not strictly a guild issue no Mummy has ever though to report to her guild about Cults going AWOL when a Vampire takes them over (Mekhet, Circle of the Crone and Ordo Dracul all love em some cults) or when an &quot;angel&quot; suborns them (because the God-Machine never uses pre-existing groups...)? <br /> <br /> Also I find the idea that Mummy's are so specialized in nature and the sort of thing they do that they just don't have any lasting or significant interaction with other Supernaturals and their cultures to be a bit of stretch. That would be the same as Demon saying that because only Demons and a few humans can see the God Machines presence on Earth and because they are the only one that can interact with it to the extent they do they will never interact with other supernaturals who don't have any idea about the GM. <br /> <br /> Instead Demon takes the wrought of saying that when it come to GM stuff Demons are usually going it alone. However, they still live in the larger NWoD and therefore can't help but run into and interact with the other weird stuff that's out there. Mummy's could pretty much be done the same way. Yes when it comes to Duat stuff and their specific antagonists maybe they are going it alone. The rest of the time they are out and about in a world that is full of other weird stuff. If anything considering the number of Supernaturals that chase supernatural objects (Mages, Sin-Eaters, Changelings and some Hunters) they should get more interaction with the &quot;weird stuff&quot; then Demons (who spend most of their time pretending to be as human as possible). <br /> <br /> Once again, want to stress I'm not all about the Crossover, its just an obvious point of disparity between Mummy and the other games, so it makes a good example for my original point. Namely, Mummy is a little more niche, a little more attached to a meta-arch/story and a little more detached from the wider NWoD then any of the other games (yes including Promethean). Is this a bad thing? Maybe in some ways, likely not in others. Unique is good, but personally I feel that between these things and the slips to the general production schedule that Mummy is a &quot;limited run&quot; game and I will be surprised if it has more then two books listed on next years schedule and any on the year after that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=106781#post106781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also - respectfully, if I was the Mummy developer I'd stay the hell away from this forum after reading that sort of thing. Have you ever considered that this kind of thing is the reason as for why Colin doesn't interact with the Mummy community around here all that much?</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much doubt my posts are behind CAS absence from the forum. Considering that started in November. The first post I made that someone could have taken as overly negative was maybe 5 weeks ago. Sorry, time line does not match up. <br /> <br /> Also while righteous indignation on behalf of the developer is all well and good, in this case its utterly unnecessary and misguided. Firstly, I acknowledge in my last post that I did seem overly negative and the post itself contains an apology for that. Secondly, CAS himself has since appeared on the thread and seems not to have taken issue with any of the points I have made. I'm sure if we found the post offensive or widely inaccurate he would have either posted a reply to that end or PM'd me about the issue. Since neither has occurred, it obviously not an issue for him and its not for me. <br /> <br /> So in general, please spare me any future outbursts you feel the need to share in an attempt to make me feel guilty over having a point of view and expressing that point on a public forum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=106744#post106744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for not being very accessible of late. As some have said, I'm responsible for quite a bit in the overall Onyx Path operation, and so I'm not quite as online and interactive as some of my OPP colleagues and developers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I\u2019m kinda interested to hear about your roll in Onyx Path\u2019s operation. I thought you were just a line developer, but do you have a position more like Rose?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=106781#post106781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Through the Dread Powers system, at least Hunter: Mortal Remains is going to be an official book that crosses over Mummies into the Vigil setting. That should be fun. Mummies make for great crossover NPCs. I wouldn't want to use them as PCs in a mixed game due to the mechanics of the Descent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am greatly looking forward to Mortal Remains, as are most people I think. Interestingly I believe Machine VI wrote the Mummy chapter of that book. Does anyone know if he worked on any of the Mummy books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T13:10:43-07:00","id":107043,"title":"","content":"I think Machine VI took over development of the book, but Filamena Young is writing at least part of the Mummy chapter, including the compact of Hunters who ritually eat the Arisen. I haven't seen either of their names on previous Mummy books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T15:22:54-07:00","id":107109,"title":"","content":"According to some google-fu Filamena Young worked on:<br /> <br /> God Machine Fiction Anthology<br /> God Machine Rules Update<br /> A Mistborn supplement...interesting. <br /> Vampire the Requiem - Ancient Mysteries<br /> Vampire the Requiem - Ancient Bloodlines <br /> World of Darkness - Immortals<br /> <br /> Those last three make me think its going to be good. The first two make me think that the God Machine update stuff in Mortal Remains is going to be solid. Looking forward to this even more now. <br /> <br /> I remember reading somewhere that originally the immortals (or at least he Purified) from Word of Darkness Immortals were going to be mentioned in Mummy but that content got cut from the core book. Do hope it shows up at some point. Really hope Sothis Ascends has some &quot;other&quot; immortals that are kinda later-day Arisen knock-offs. God knows the setting needs some diversity in its immortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T15:53:04-07:00","id":107121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=107043#post107043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">including the compact of Hunters who ritually eat the Arisen.</div> </div> </div> </div>This concept already exists in <b>Mummy</b>. In fact, it's the modus operandus of mummies' chielf mortal antagonist.<br /> <br /> Also, there's a reason hunters don't ritually eat the Arisen in the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T15:58:04-07:00","id":107126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=107121#post107121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This concept already exists in <b>Mummy</b>. In fact, it's the modus operandus of mummies' chielf mortal antagonist.<br /> <br /> Also, there's a reason hunters don't ritually eat the Arisen in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is that reason exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T16:25:28-07:00","id":107131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=107121#post107121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This concept already exists in <b>Mummy</b>. In fact, it's the modus operandus of mummies' chielf mortal antagonist.<br /> <br /> Also, there's a reason hunters don't ritually eat the Arisen in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read all of the storyteller's section yest (our Storyteller is just about ready to begin!)<br /> <br /> I was referring to this: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-the-vigil-the-faithful-of-shulpae/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-the-vi...ul-of-shulpae/</a><br /> <br /> That said, they could be eating the Purified. From what I understand, monsters that appear in Vigil aren't <i>necessarily</i> the protagonists or monsters from the other lines. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T16:53:09-07:00","id":107146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=107131#post107131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I understand, monsters that appear in Vigil aren't <i>necessarily</i> the protagonists or monsters from the other lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly right (which is why the <b>Hunter</b> material probably shouldn't feature proper terms like &quot;Arisen;&quot; the 'mummies' those characters are hunting aren't <b>Mummy </b>mummies).<br /> <br /> Especially since in the world of <b>Mummy</b>, what they're up to would be destined to catastrophic failure (on top of being redundant).<br /> <br /> C.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T17:06:37-07:00","id":107153,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the catastrophic failure involves having the Arisen resurrect him or herself around said hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T20:21:30-07:00","id":107222,"title":"","content":"Hey, Hawthorn!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=106984#post106984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CAS himself has since appeared on the thread and seems not to have taken issue with any of the points I have made. I'm sure if we found the post offensive or widely inaccurate he would have either posted a reply to that end or PM'd me about the issue. Since neither has occurred, it obviously not an issue for him and its not for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mean to call out a fan (and I appreciate your being a fan!), but I can't say that this part is as &quot;obvious&quot; as you might think. While I didn't find your post offensive at all -- you've the right to express yourself here, certainly -- it might be a bridge too far to say that I take <i>no</i> issue whatsoever with some of the points it raised. Of course I don't want you to feel overly challenged by those who've stood 'against' you on this thread, but it's probably fair to say that those fellas had valid reasons themselves for taking the positions they took.<br /> <br /> At any rate, of course there's no &quot;issue.&quot; We're all buds here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=106984#post106984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought you were just a line developer, but do you have a position more like Rose? &lt;snip&gt; Interestingly I believe Machine VI wrote the Mummy chapter of that book. Does anyone know if he worked on any of the Mummy books?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not allowed to discuss details yet, but I think that's fair to say, sure. As others have pointed out, we're a scattered operation here at Onyx Path, and most of us have other duties to which we must attend to pay our bills, but a handful of us are a little more central/full-time with OPP than the rest, and Rose and I are in that smaller circle, yep. I am a busy dood.<br /> <br /> Thanks for being into the game. With any luck, the headaches of yestermonth are behind us now, and the pace will be a bit more crackling from here on out. I've noticed the phenomenon you mentioned, BTW; with this game in particular, it seems there's a stronger sense of urgency to see each successive supplement (and I agree that <b>Mummy</b> getting a smaller corebook than the other game lines did certainly didn't do it any favors, though I think it presents enough to get people started and to run enough satisfying stories while they wait for new content). Certainly, one can write and run a game in, say, Rio just out of the corebook, but there's no substitute for a full citybook; it's like a little 'case study' of the material in the other books, and for me, there's nothing more impressive than a well-conceived and -written setting book. Those are what I started my writing career with, and I'm one of the few who's been blessed with the opportunity to write not just one for White Wolf, but several. So yeah, once <i>D.C.</i> is in hand, that <i>could</i> well make the game feel that much more complete. That's fair to say.<br /> <br /> C.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":277,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","user":"CAS","date":". 04-06-2014, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T21:43:36-07:00","id":107251,"title":"","content":"This may be unable to be answered, but.. will this book be exclusively core content explained via fluff, or can we expect new materials? I expect some fun new relics or some such, but might we get a new piece of material (antagonist, new system) or spoilers (on Irem or the judges?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T23:56:00-07:00","id":107282,"title":"","content":"Thanks for taking the time to post these responses CAS. You're a little bit my savior right now. I did successfully run a short game of Mummy with only the core book, and it wasn't a short run because of lack of content. I'm waiting on <i>DC</i> to start up my longer chronicle and I'm very excited.<br /> <br /> I don't want to bombard you with too many questions so I'll try to stick to the thread's overall topic: We know <i>Book of the Deceived</i> lost a writer, so how has that extra responsibility been going? Will you be doing a Development Tease for <i>Mummy</i>'s section in <i>Dark Eras</i>? I'm not sure who was put in to write that chapter; will the <i>Dark Eras</i> chapters still be developer passed by their respective line lead developers or is there one primary developer for the book who will oversee everything?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=106790#post106790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a picture of the Prince of 100,000 Leaves, an Annunaki that was introduced in Awakening's first ever supplement, long before Mummy was a glimmer in a necromancer's eye. There won't be any mummy/mage crossover books. CAS doesn't want to do one, <i>I</i> don't want to do one. We'd both have to change our minds, then persuade Rich to change <i>his</i> mind, then persuade CCP to sign off on it, and we both have plenty of book ideas for the lines as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've come to the conclusion that DaveB is a genie of some kind, and he'll magically appear anywhere on the internet where the words, &quot;Mage&quot; and &quot;Awakening&quot; appear three times","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T01:48:30-07:00","id":107330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=106984#post106984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wow, the crossover issue got take out of context. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div> If I may be so bold, why not create a thread to discuss Mummy's crossover potential? There is a lot to brainstorm on the subject - from other supernaturals crossing over to MtC and vice versa, to how to make different themes mesh (or clash, for that matter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T04:46:04-07:00","id":107368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=107222#post107222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Hawthorn!<br /> <br /> I don't mean to call out a fan (and I appreciate your being a fan!), but I can't say that this part is as &quot;obvious&quot; as you might think. While I didn't find your post offensive at all -- you've the right to express yourself here, certainly -- it might be a bridge too far to say that I take <i>no</i> issue whatsoever with some of the points it raised. Of course I don't want you to feel overly challenged by those who've stood 'against' you on this thread, but it's probably fair to say that those fellas had valid reasons themselves for taking the positions they took.<br /> <br /> At any rate, of course there's no &quot;issue.&quot; We're all buds here.</div> </div> </div> </div>God damn it CAS. Just when I'm all fired up to sling fire and brimstone and blame all the weaknesses of the human condition on you. Then you have to go and be so god damn...cordial and accommodating and polite. Why? Why couldn't you be a cackling fiends. <br /> <br /> Anyway, all drama aside, I appreciate you addressing the point and being a gentleman about the whole issue. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=107222#post107222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not allowed to discuss details yet, but I think that's fair to say, sure. As others have pointed out, we're a scattered operation here at Onyx Path, and most of us have other duties to which we must attend to pay our bills, but a handful of us are a little more central/full-time with OPP than the rest, and Rose and I are in that smaller circle, yep. I am a busy dood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean that like Rose you'll be a forum regular now? (One can hope.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=107222#post107222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for being into the game. With any luck, the headaches of yestermonth are behind us now, and the pace will be a bit more crackling from here on out. I've noticed the phenomenon you mentioned, BTW; with this game in particular, it seems there's a stronger sense of urgency to see each successive supplement (and I agree that <b>Mummy</b> getting a smaller corebook than the other game lines did certainly didn't do it any favors, though I think it presents enough to get people started and to run enough satisfying stories while they wait for new content). Certainly, one can write and run a game in, say, Rio just out of the corebook, but there's no substitute for a full citybook; it's like a little 'case study' of the material in the other books, and for me, there's nothing more impressive than a well-conceived and -written setting book. Those are what I started my writing career with, and I'm one of the few who's been blessed with the opportunity to write not just one for White Wolf, but several. So yeah, once <i>D.C.</i> is in hand, that <i>could</i> well make the game feel that much more complete. That's fair to say.<br /> <br /> C.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you've obviously got an impression of some of the issues that the fanbase has been wrestling with since the Core. Mummy as a game has a lot of potential, no doubt and its frustrating to see that potential be stymied by the issues like the Core book length and the terrible, terrible time Mummy has had in its development cycle. I believe their is so much impetus on the supplements for this game because they add whole new aspects to the game. Guilds were not really a huge thing until Guildhalls (and there was no sense of a Mummy community really). The Deceived are a huge aspect of the game, but are basically absent (save fan creations) until their book comes out. <br /> <br /> For me especially the thing/chronicle I have in my head for Mummy requires pretty much every splat on the list: Guildhalls for the history, Deceived for plot, Sothis for different time periods and Dreams of Avarice for in-game props and plot. <br /> <br /> You can see why I'm going hell-for-leather when it comes to getting all the supplements that are currently on the release schedule out. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InfernalGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=107222#post107222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may be so bold, why not create a thread to discuss Mummy's crossover potential? There is a lot to brainstorm on the subject - from other supernaturals crossing over to MtC and vice versa, to how to make different themes mesh (or clash, for that matter).</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda did, way back when the Core first came out. Had some interesting discussion and generated some rules that I used later in Changeling/Mummy game I ran (which ran itself into the ground). Frankly, while I am interested in out-of-the-box theories that the fans come up with, I kinda do want the official line on this stuff. I'm perfectly happy to wait for it and personally I think it would fit into Sothis Ascends kinda nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T05:23:39-07:00","id":107378,"title":"","content":"I'm very interested in something Crossover related.<br /> <br /> Simple fact is that - unless someone here runs a PbP and I get in on it - I won't ever be playing a game of M:tC.<br /> <br /> Mummies will be antagonists in games I run or maybe someone will one day let me play one in a mixed nWoD splats game or something but none of my players were interested at all when I gave them the core nor Guildhalls.<br /> <br /> So, crossover stuff is about the only way I'll ever see a Mummy in action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T05:43:23-07:00","id":107386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=107378#post107378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very interested in something Crossover related.<br /> <br /> Simple fact is that - unless someone here runs a PbP and I get in on it - I won't ever be playing a game of M:tC.<br /> <br /> Mummies will be antagonists in games I run or maybe someone will one day let me play one in a mixed nWoD splats game or something but none of my players were interested at all when I gave them the core nor Guildhalls.<br /> <br /> So, crossover stuff is about the only way I'll ever see a Mummy in action.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the feeling. Pretty much the only reason I ran a Changeling/Mummy crossover was because one of my players just did not get Mummy and did not really want to try and get Mummy. Hence the Crossover. It worked for about 6 months on and off, then went bad, as in the player disengaged from the game bad. Did not last long after that.<br /> <br /> Learned my lesson about running what you want rather then what's demanded of you out of some sense of obligation. <br /> <br /> Also Scutarii, look on the bright side, the Deceived are going to be presented as playable. So depending on how different they are from the Arisen your group might agree to a Deceived game. Alternatively, if Sothis Ascends has &quot;knock-off&quot; latter day Arisen imitation immortals you might convince people into a house-ruled game of those.<br /> <br /> The other option is to push for a mixed splat game and if people of issue with the Arisen try using one of the other Mummy's I suggested above or even a Sadikh who's master is asleep but gave her an open ended enough task that she's not in a dream coma while he/she is asleep in Hennet. <br /> <br /> Never say Never. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T05:44:16-07:00","id":107387,"title":"","content":"Sorry about the double post. I wanted to separate out the questions I had from any other forum post I might make on here.<br /> <br /> With CAS being around now I thought I better capitalize on the chance to ask him some questions about the planned products for the Mummy game line. Since we've got a chance to increase the transparency of the lines development now.<br /> <br /> I've listed the various products in the order that they were 50th and currently final Kickstarter backers e-mail for Mummy the Curse on the 3rd of December 2013. For the sake of completeness I've included products in the line that are already out.<br /> <br /> In general, even if you can't answer the questions I pose CAS for spoiler reasons a more detailed update on where each of these projects is at would be great.<br /> <br /> - <b>MtC Ready Made Characters:</b> Already released as of December 23rd 2013<br /> <br /> - <b>Guildhalls of the Deathless:</b> Already released as of October 30th 2013<br /> <br /> - <b>Cursed Necropolis: D.C.:</b> As of 1st of April its has all Art for it completed and is currently in layout. Written by Harry Heckel, (who did the classic Vampire the the Masquerade book <b>DC By Night</b>) and Neall Raemonn Price (who wrote on Exalted's Manual of <b>Exalted Power: Alchemists</b>)are writing this.<br /> <br /> <u>Questions:</u><br /> <br /> 1) To reiterate Cleverest of Things is this book going to contain some new content material beyond being a setting book e.g. antagonists, relics and such?<br /> <br /> 2) Is the aim to get this out before the end of April?<br /> <br /> - <b>Book of the Deceived: </b>As of 1st of April Redlines (on second drafts I believe) one writer had to drop his section so a new one is being located.<br /> <br /> <u>Questions:</u><br /> <br /> 1) Who are the writers on this one? I know you mentioned CAS that you wanted very particular people working on this book, also who is the new writer?<br /> <br /> 2) Can you explain some of the stuff that made this book such a difficult one to develop? Obviously this might be nothing to do with the book itself and everything to do with everything else going on and distracting you from working on it. Still, I got the impression from your previous comments about this book that you wanted it to be a particular way due to it being the &quot;spoiler&quot; book for the whole line basically.<br /> <br /> 3) Can you give you any new info/teases about the Deceived? Mainly I' interested in knowing how they play differently from the Arisen while still being Mummy's and still being PC characters. Obviously without spoilers, can you give any info on how they might &quot;play differently&quot; from the Arisen?<br /> <br /> - <b>Mummy Fiction Anthology:</b> In December this was in the &quot;Writing&quot; stage.<br /> <br /> <u>Questions:</u><br /> <br /> 1) Who are the writers for this? Can you give us any hints as to if the story's are interlinked or stand alone?<br /> <br /> 2) Is this still being written or has it moved onto editing? (Do fiction anthology's have a redline stage?)<br /> <br /> - <b>Dreams of Avarice:</b> In December a writer had been brought onboard and was being contracted.<br /> <br /> <u>Questions:</u><br /> <br /> 1) Did you get the writer you wanted?<br /> <br /> 2) Is this in the writing stage or has it moved any further?<br /> <br /> - <b>Mummy: The Curse Novel:</b> As of the first week of December Rich T and Colin were discussing this.<br /> <br /> <u>Questions:</u><br /> <br /> 1) Has a writer been contacted? If so can you tease where the novel will be set (or when for that matter)?<br /> <br /> - <b>Sothis Ascends: </b>This was not actually included in the December update because its the last book on the official release line for Mummy that we know of.<br /> <br /> <u>Questions: </u><br /> <br /> 1) Is this still in concept?<br /> <br /> 2) Do you know which writers you want for this book? Are any of them working on Deceived?<br /> <br /> 3) When you think writers might be able to make a start on drafts for this one?<br /> <br /> Apart from these projects (yes I'm aware I missed out <b>Cursed Necropolis: Rio</b>, I could not think of any questions for it) there are two other projects relating to Mummy currently in the works:<br /> <br /> - <b>Hunter the Vigil: Mortal Remains:</b> As of the 1st of April this has had to go back into editing and has art coming in for it.<br /> <br /> <u>Questions:</u><br /> <br /> 1) How much involvement did you have with the Mummy chapter of the book? Your comment earlier in the thread implies that you did not get first pass or something.<br /> <br /> 2) What are the themes you think putting a Mummy into a Hunter game/setting can invoke? Human fragility in the face of the timeless/immortal is one I think can be focused on, but I'm very interested to hear your take on this issue.<br /> <br /> - <b>World of Darkness: Dark Eras:</b> As of the 1st of April this is in mostly second drafts with one exception.<br /> <br /> <u>Questions:</u><br /> <br /> 1) We know the Mummy setting is sorta 1880-1920's British Empire, which makes sense with the Egyptian craze that swept through English society at the time. Do you know who's writing the Mummy Chapter for Dark Era's?<br /> <br /> 2) Is there anything in particular that you want to do with/in the Dark Era's Mummy expansion? Considering that Sothis Ascends is going to address the issue of playing Mummy in other time periods in general. Do you think you could use the Dark Era's setting to &quot;focus in&quot; on that idea with a unique example?<br /> <br /> I know there is a lot to cover here. If you can answer even a fraction of these questions CAS I'll be a happy man.<br /> <br /> All my frustrations and negativity were pretty much coming out of the lack of communication and transparency between the devs and fans over the last sixth months really. So I'm happy that your back and around and really, really hoping this can be the start of a new phase of Mummy development that leaves the issues that have previously plagued the line in the past at last.<br /> <br /> Many Thanks,<br /> <br /> \u200bHawthorn","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T05:44:20-07:00","id":107388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=107146#post107146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's exactly right (which is why the <b>Hunter</b> material probably shouldn't feature proper terms like &quot;Arisen;&quot; the 'mummies' those characters are hunting aren't <b>Mummy </b>mummies).<br /> <br /> Especially since in the world of <b>Mummy</b>, what they're up to would be destined to catastrophic failure (on top of being redundant).<br /> <br /> C.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for claryfing this CAS. When read the teaser for the Shulpae hunters it didnt seem to describe True Arisen and I immediate thought about the effects of digesting Arisen's sahu. Glad these hunter mummies are not <b>Arisen Mummies</b>.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T00:14:31-07:00","id":108013,"title":"","content":"This week's Monday Meeting updates:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mummy the Curse </b>- <b>Cursed Necropolis DC</b> is in layout and looking for dev comments to the last proof.<br /> <b>Book of the Deceived</b> (MtC): Redlines. The loss of a writer means their section has to be given to a new writer, CAS is on top of it.<br /> <b>nWoD: Dark Eras:</b> Second drafts except for one chapter which is in first drafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the only notable change is with DC, in that its getting its final developer pass!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","user":"reseru","date":". 04-08-2014, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T02:01:15-07:00","id":108042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=107388#post107388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for claryfing this CAS. When read the teaser for the Shulpae hunters it didnt seem to describe True Arisen and I immediate thought about the effects of digesting Arisen's sahu. Glad these hunter mummies are not <b>Arisen Mummies</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a minor Sothis Ascends teaser, but that's not to imply some mortals of the Lakhmid Kingdom don't try...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T01:16:55-07:00","id":111334,"title":"","content":"Hiya,<br /> <br /> We're definitely hoping to get at least the beta-proof on <b>D.C.</b> out by month's end, yep.<br /> <br /> The writers on <b>Book of the Deceived</b> include Malcolm Sheppard, George Holochwost, Michael Goodwin, Heather Curatola, and myself. The Deceived are Deathless, like the Arisen, but are ultimately more different from the Arisen than, say, the vampires of Belial's Brood are from the vampires of other covenants. A different breed.<br /> <br /> The anthology will be called <b>Curse of the Blue Nile</b>. It has been contracted and is being written. One of the authors is a six-time Bram Stoker Award-winner.<br /> <br /> Likewise, both <b>Dreams of Avarice</b> and the tie-in novel have their writers and things are progressing apace. The former is being written by Malcolm Sheppard.<br /> <br /> <b>Sothis Ascends</b> is coming due for redlines, and I've already seen some text. Good stuff. As mentioned, the Gentleman Gamer is one of the writers.<br /> <br /> The <i>Mummy</i> chapter of <b>Dark Eras</b> has been turned in and is now in development. It was written by Jesse Heinig.<br /> <br /> I've had no involvement in any <i>Hunter</i> books.<br /> <br /> C.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T03:11:26-07:00","id":111364,"title":"","content":"That is awesome news <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And nice to see that the Gent is taking another stab at game writing after his sea horrors rpg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T04:49:51-07:00","id":111390,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the updates! Not that I doubted it necessarily, but I'm glad to see that the other supplements are starting to be worked on despite <i>Book of the Deceived</i>'s delays of author drop-out.<br /> <br /> And...congratulations to Gentleman Gamer? I know he's got a Youtube channel but I'm unfamiliar with his bibliography so if congratulations are in order then...there you go! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T09:15:42-07:00","id":111531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=111334#post111334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hiya,<br /> <br /> We're definitely hoping to get at least the beta-proof on <b>D.C.</b> out by month's end, yep.<br /> <br /> The writers on <b>Book of the Deceived</b> include Malcolm Sheppard, George Holochwost, Michael Goodwin, Heather Curatola, and myself. The Deceived are Deathless, like the Arisen, but are ultimately more different from the Arisen than, say, the vampires of Belial's Brood are from the vampires of other covenants. A different breed.<br /> <br /> The anthology will be called <b>Curse of the Blue Nile</b>. It has been contracted and is being written. One of the authors is a six-time Bram Stoker Award-winner.<br /> <br /> Likewise, both <b>Dreams of Avarice</b> and the tie-in novel have their writers and things are progressing apace. The former is being written by Malcolm Sheppard.<br /> <br /> <b>Sothis Ascends</b> is coming due for redlines, and I've already seen some text. Good stuff. As mentioned, the Gentleman Gamer is one of the writers.<br /> <br /> The <i>Mummy</i> chapter of <b>Dark Eras</b> has been turned in and is now in development. It was written by Jesse Heinig.<br /> <br /> I've had no involvement in any <i>Hunter</i> books.<br /> <br /> C.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the update CAS.<br /> <br /> Are you worried about getting a load of material to redline at once? Deceived has at least one chapters worth I presume from the new writer? (Which might need more then one round of redlines)<br /> <br /> Plus Sothis Ascends and possible Dreams of Avarice coming in close behind Deceived?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T02:20:09-07:00","id":111964,"title":"","content":"Hiya folks. I was super-stoked to work on the <b>Dark Eras</b> material for <b>Mummy</b> at the behest of CAS. I can't go into a lot of detail about it as it's in development hands now, but it was a great honor to work on such a striking game and I hope that I did justice to the important themes and topics of <b>Mummy</b>.<br /> <br /> My goal was to cover the era in a way that would give inspirations and story hooks to <b>Mummy</b> players who want to use that period of history. In this information age, anyone can look up the historical facts of the Boer War or the fall of the Ottoman Empire or the formation of Turkey. What's useful is giving people ideas on how to place those elements into their chronicles.<br /> <br /> The <b>Mummy</b> segment of <b>Dark Eras</b> is also useful even to people who don't set a chronicle in that period, in that it can serve as a flashback device. Mummies might acquire lost memories of time spent in that era. Plus, that time period is recent enough that cultists might be grandchildren of people who lived through some of those events, which allows groups to play with narrative threads that follow the familial and cultural ties of various mummy cultists and their mortal associates.<br /> <br /> Naturally, I also included a few new Merits and powers that are pertinent to the time period.<br /> <br /> I'm sure CAS will let you know more as the book gets closer to release!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2716-jesse-heinig","name":"Jesse Heinig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2716_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T09:25:11-07:00","id":112070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InfernalGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=111364#post111364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is awesome news <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And nice to see that the Gent is taking another stab at game writing after his sea horrors rpg.</div> </div> </div> </div>You never know - They Came From Beneath The Sea! may emerge from the depths one day... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T09:26:16-07:00","id":112071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=111390#post111390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the updates! Not that I doubted it necessarily, but I'm glad to see that the other supplements are starting to be worked on despite <i>Book of the Deceived</i>'s delays of author drop-out.<br /> <br /> And...congratulations to Gentleman Gamer? I know he's got a Youtube channel but I'm unfamiliar with his bibliography so if congratulations are in order then...there you go! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the congratulations!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T10:19:06-07:00","id":112104,"title":"","content":"Wow I didn't know you were a writer Gentlemen Gamer! Good Onya Sir! You already seemingly achieved the impossible with your podcast Guests, so I know you can pull off some mighty spiffy things!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Could we possibly get some Mummy Books worked on after Dreams of Avaris/Sothis Ascends? Because I for one thing Relics could really use a book. They are something all Mummy Storytellers will need access to, and while can mine other books for them and create our own, for flat out usefulness in every mummy game a Relic books would be a must have for me. It could even be tied in with a Temple, Cult, Magic Book.<br /> <br /> Thanks for showing up CAS! I didn't know you were going to be a heavy duty regular in Onyx Path now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T10:37:11-07:00","id":112109,"title":"","content":"Good to have you here, Jesse!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T11:56:21-07:00","id":112158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=112070#post112070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You never know - They Came From Beneath The Sea! may emerge from the depths one day... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Here's hoping <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T02:42:39-07:00","id":112508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesse Heinig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=111964#post111964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this information age, anyone can look up the historical facts of the Boer War or the fall of the Ottoman Empire or the formation of Turkey.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Boer War, huh? With Mummy's obvious ties to Egypt, I was fully expecting we'd see the rise of Egyptology, the fall of the Ottoman Empire (and the Khedivate), al-Thawra (the Arab revolt), pan-Arabism, the Mahdist campaign in Anglo-Egyptian Sudan, Gallipoli, the Young Turks, the Khalifat Movement, maybe even early Zionism. T. E. Lawrence, Howard Carter, Muhammad Ali Pasha, Atat\u00fcrk, Omar Mukhtar, Freya Stark, Abdel-Kader al-Djazairi, Richard Francis Burton, Charles George Gordon ... all that. The Boer War seems rather further afield than I was expecting, though I'm certainly glad to see it included. Its a damned interesting subject, and its always good to see more coverage of Africa in the WoD. Especially since the Nameless Empire penetrated very deep into Africa, perhaps all the way down to the Cape now?<br /> <br /> Makes me wonder what other surprises we'll see. The French Foreign Legion and their conflicts with Touaregs and tje Wassoulou and Toucouleur Empires in the Sahara? Italy's attempts at colonizing Libya and Somaliland? Perhaps even the British colonial venture in India? Yeah, its a bit further afield but it fits tangentially. Mummy's era is decades after the Sepoy Mutiny and company rule has already ended in India (as has the Mughal Empire; the last Mughal Emperor, Bahadur Shah II, going into exile in Burma). The British are ruling India directly at this point. Nationalism, colonialism, Theosophy, Orientalism and many other isms are all mingling in weird ways. Also, with the collapse of the Ottoman Empire, there was a movement in Muslim India (which was never ruled by the Ottomans) to revive the title of Caliph.<br /> <br /> All very tantalizing. Can't wait for the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The <b>Mummy</b> segment of <b>Dark Eras</b> is also useful even to people who don't set a chronicle in that period, in that it can serve as a flashback device. Mummies might acquire lost memories of time spent in that era. </div> </div> </div>I like this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, that time period is recent enough that cultists might be grandchildren of people who lived through some of those events, which allows groups to play with narrative threads that follow the familial and cultural ties of various mummy cultists and their mortal associates. </div> </div> </div>But I like this even more. Cultists really are taking their place as a big part of M:tC, and I'm looking forward to seeing that role expanded as future supplements come out. Really hoping we'll see a &quot;player's guide to cultists&quot; or some such somewhere down the road, but maybe that's just me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Naturally, I also included a few new Merits and powers that are pertinent to the time period. </div> </div> </div>Sweet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1449-zakariya-ali-sher","name":"Zakariya Ali Sher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T03:31:24-07:00","id":112520,"title":"","content":"I'm sure the <i>Mummy</i> chapter will be fairly comprehensive, as all the Eras seem to be. I'm even more sure that Howard Carter and the explosion of interest in Egyptian archaeology is the reason why this is <i>Mummy</i>'s Dark Era, though, so I'd expect to see plenty of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zakariya Ali Sher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=112508#post112508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I like this even more. Cultists really are taking their place as a big part of M:tC, and I'm looking forward to seeing that role expanded as future supplements come out. Really hoping we'll see a &quot;player's guide to cultists&quot; or some such somewhere down the road, but maybe that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really the only other extra supplement I'd like to see (assuming/hoping the <i>Book of Going Westward</i> gets in) other than what is scheduled. Something that expands cult rules and talks more about the sadikh and witnesses, and their role in the <i>Mummy</i> world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T04:38:53-07:00","id":112540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=112520#post112520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure the <i>Mummy</i> chapter will be fairly comprehensive, as all the Eras seem to be. I'm even more sure that Howard Carter and the explosion of interest in Egyptian archaeology is the reason why this is <i>Mummy</i>'s Dark Era, though, so I'd expect to see plenty of that.<br /> That's really the only other extra supplement I'd like to see (assuming/hoping the <i>Book of Going Westward</i> gets in) other than what is scheduled. Something that expands cult rules and talks more about the sadikh and witnesses, and their role in the <i>Mummy</i> world</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a subject on which I'd love to write more. I love a good cult with lots of layers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T08:43:56-07:00","id":112673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=111334#post111334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writers on <b>Book of the Deceived</b> include Malcolm Sheppard, George Holochwost, Michael Goodwin, Heather Curatola, and myself. The Deceived are Deathless, like the Arisen, but are ultimately more different from the Arisen than, say, the vampires of Belial's Brood are from the vampires of other covenants. A different breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice.<br /> <br /> With Book of the Deceived not being out and all, would it be possible to give us a little storytelling advice on how to run the Deceived? Not asking for a huge essay on the topic, of course; that's what the Deceived book is for, but a little something on how to properly portray the Lost Guild in the context of the game would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T15:43:28-07:00","id":112980,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine the Mummy Dark Era will be a time of great change. Not only is it the collapse of Empires, it's also likely when many mummies lost to time are found in the egyptology boom. It makes me wonder if some object or Mummy was uncovered, prompting Mummies to push the study of Egypt, in search of more relics and tombs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T19:37:30-07:00","id":113071,"title":"","content":"I think the Sothic turn of the 5th or 6th century is the sort-of-emigration from Egypt, where Mummies left en masse. Surely others left over the thousands of years before then, but still.<br /> <br /> Personally, I have a slinking feeling that the <i>Mummy</i> Dark Era is when the Heretic achieved Apotheosis, since it's stated that he achieved it within the last century<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And if they don't write that then it's still canon for my game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T19:48:50-07:00","id":113078,"title":"","content":"Here's this week's Monday Meeting news! I didn't mean to double post, but I saw that it was up after I posted the reply above. Let's hope CCP still cares about WoD books even without an MMO<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mummy the Curse </b>- <b>Cursed Necropolis DC</b> is in layout and almost ready for approval proofing once all the art gets in.<br /> <b>Book of the Deceived</b> (MtC): Redlines. The loss of a writer means their section has to be given to a new writer, CAS is on top of it.<br /> <b>nWoD: Dark Eras:</b> Second drafts coming in.</div> </div> </div> </div>In case you missed it, too, CAS let in some details up-thread: <i>Mummy</i> anthology is being written, <i>Dreams of Avarice</i> is being written, and <i>Sothis Ascends</i> is even in redlines!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T16:48:11-07:00","id":117732,"title":"","content":"Uh...sorry for what's turning out to be a triple post? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mummy the Curse </b>- <b>Cursed Necropolis DC- </b>waiting for CA to return the final approval proof so we can get it to CCP for their approval too.<br /> <b>Book of the Deceived</b> (MtC): Redlines.<br /> <b>nWoD: Dark Eras:</b> Second drafts coming in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wondering what <i>Book of the Deceived</i>'s status is; the redlines of what the dropped-out author was supposed to write that CAS filled in for, I guess? I'm willing to bet the city-book will be out in a couple weeks, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T19:06:00-07:00","id":117782,"title":"","content":"Here's a little something you might enjoy. (Not mine; something I found while doing research.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/pyroll/sets/72157633714555898/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.flickr.com/photos/pyroll...7633714555898/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2716-jesse-heinig","name":"Jesse Heinig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2716_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T10:26:14-07:00","id":117984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zakariya Ali Sher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=112508#post112508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really hoping we'll see a &quot;player's guide to cultists&quot; or some such somewhere down the road, but maybe that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=112520#post112520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's really the only other extra supplement I'd like to see (assuming/hoping the <i>Book of Going Westward</i> gets in) other than what is scheduled. Something that expands cult rules and talks more about the sadikh and witnesses, and their role in the <i>Mummy</i> world</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy is quite rich in the number of ways that mortals can engage with its mythos - cultists and sorcerers obviously - but also anything in the art and antiquities world (the relics and amkhata are fascinating in their own right), pulpy adventurers* (of whom mummies and their entourage are particularly suitable foes), secret societies that aren't run by mummies (for whom shadowy history, sacred geometries, ancient relics, and alchemical secrets are bread and butter). And all of these can intersect with each other as well as they can with mummies themselves. Add in the fact that playing one mummy and surrounding mortals is one of the suggested campaign frames, and a &quot;mortal player's supplement&quot; would be a grand addition.<br /> <br /> * Who I really hope get a mention in Dark Eras.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T09:02:28-07:00","id":118453,"title":"","content":"Our mummy game has 3 cultists and 2 Arisen. Gentleman Gamer's game with CAS and Mark Rein-Hagen had 2 cultists and 1 Arisen. I definitely think we'd get a lot of use out of either a Mummy player's guide to cults or a blue book on cults with additional support for mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T10:57:21-07:00","id":118501,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure theres enough new crunch for a whole book of cults, if Sorcerers are covered in Deceived (or sothis ascends). Mostly, the only new stuff I can imagine is new cult benefits. Mostly, every blue book is useful for filling in mortals. A mummy specific cult book would need mummy specific mechanics. Granted, relics and tomb benefits/drawbacks would also be interesting, and would fit for a Cult book. I'd more expect, however, for us to get a few new tidbits in other books (like new cult benefits and relics possibly being in the DC book). Sothis ascends could double as an endgame supplement, meaning hopefully we will see more things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T11:54:23-07:00","id":118525,"title":"","content":"Aside from new benefits and GMing advice, there could be sample Cults written up. Maybe there'd be two examples for each category (tribal, conspiracy, enterprise)? Then there'd be rules expansions for sadikh (a la the ghouls supplement for <i>Vampire</i>), who are especially interesting because, even if only one can be awake at a time, you can have a closet full of them. Finally there's Witnesses, mortals blessed/cursed with Sybaris-immunity, who could be expanded similar to <i>Mage</i>'s sleepwalkers and proximi.<br /> <br /> I think there's plenty of room","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T20:34:32-07:00","id":121427,"title":"","content":"Pulling into the end of April, I'm feeling 100% certain we'll see <i>DC</i> in May<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <b>Mummy the Curse </b>- <b>Cursed Necropolis DC- </b>final proof to CCP for their approval.<br /> <b>- Book of the Deceived</b> (MtC): Redlines.<br /> <b>- nWoD: Dark Eras:</b> Second drafts coming in.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0