Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T01:14:10-07:00","id":123017,"title":"","content":"So Mortal Remains and Curse Necropolis DC in the same 24 hours. I suddenly went from waiting for 5 Mummy books to waiting for 3...odd feeling. Nice to see some movement on the line finally.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'm impressed by the speed of the approval on DC, it was what? 3 Days? That's the quickest approval for any product I've seen CCP produce.<br /> <br /> Now if only Book of the Deceived could get out of its 6 month Redline period and it will be the best Mummy related week since the Core was released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T04:36:23-07:00","id":123062,"title":"","content":"Well, I was beaten to the punch. <i>Cursed Necropolis: DC</i> is out and I'm downloading it, fretting at how I know have to suddenly start the <i>Mummy</i> campaign I've been promising my partner <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I'll be leaving for Boston in three hours, too...maybe I can get the file to my ipod touch but I'm the least tech-savvy 26 year-old out there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T18:49:17-07:00","id":126329,"title":"","content":"<i>Cursed Necropolis DC</i> is out to KS backers, and it's super awesome<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <b>Mummy the Curse </b>- <b>Cursed Necropolis DC- </b>KS backer PDF out last week. Compiling and inputting errata before making the on-sale PDF and PoD versions.<br /> <b>- Book of the Deceived</b> (MtC): Redlines.<br /> <b>- nWoD: Dark Eras:</b> Second drafts are almost all in.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T01:38:02-07:00","id":126548,"title":"","content":"Sigh...Redlines...(I'm kinda frightened that my pessimistic release date of August might come true with Deceived) <br /> <br /> My kingdom for an editing phase.<br /> <br /> Still DC turned out to be the best Mummy supplement yet, so hopefully the quality will continue at this level for all future Mummy releases. <br /> <br /> Also am I the only one that wishes that Sothis Ascends and Dreams of Avarice were added to the Monday Morning notes? Since CAS mentioned they were in Redlines and second drafts respectively I've been wondering about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T02:16:39-07:00","id":126554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=126548#post126548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also am I the only one that wishes that Sothis Ascends and Dreams of Avarice were added to the Monday Morning notes? Since CAS mentioned they were in Redlines and second drafts respectively I've been wondering about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought they would be, too. Maybe we can ask Rich as a comment on the blog","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T02:36:45-07:00","id":126556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=126554#post126554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought they would be, too. Maybe we can ask Rich as a comment on the blog</div> </div> </div> </div>I think someone did a few weeks ago. Rich mentioned that he gets the update off Rose, who gets them off the various line developers.<br /> <br /> So I guess CAS has not passed along those updates to Rose. To be fair, he might not want to flood the update with three more Mummy books (Sothis, Dreams, Rio)that are between first drafts and redlines. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T02:38:38-07:00","id":126558,"title":"","content":"You're right. We wouldn't want to clog up all the V20 and W20 space <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T02:59:12-07:00","id":126567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=126558#post126558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right. We wouldn't want to clog up all the V20 and W20 space <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't thought about it like that. <br /> <br /> I guess its more the case that Sothis can't go into Redlines until Deceived has finished up. Since the writing and redline phases are the ones that are most time consuming for CAS. As editing are brought on for a book-by-book basis and art is Mike Chaney's thing isn't it? Obviously final proofs go back to CAS, but yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T16:47:25-07:00","id":157061,"title":"","content":"I haven't kept track of the Monday Meeting updates in this thread for about the past month or so because there weren't any updates in the blog. That's changed a little this week, so let's hope things start picking up! A W20 Kickstarter goes up tomorrow, and after that, I think, should be the one for <i>Dark Eras</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- </span></span></span><b>Mummy the Curse </b><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- </span></span></span><b>Cursed Necropolis DC- </b><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">PDF, physical copy PoD, and PDF/PoD combos version are on sale on DTRPG. </span></span></span><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/129144/Cursed-Necropolis-DC\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...-Necropolis-DC</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>-<span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Book of the Deceived</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> (MtC): Redlines. \u201cAlmost off my desk\u201d says CA Suleiman.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>nWoD: Dark Eras:</b></span><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Second drafts are almost all in.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T07:32:59-07:00","id":157818,"title":"","content":"The subtle hints in the DC book makes me really itch for the Book of the Deceived. It sounds like they can do some very, very odd stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T11:43:35-07:00","id":173005,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of updates this week. I feel like I missed them on my first read-through, because there's a couple exciting additions to our list now!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>- Book of the Deceived</b> (MtC): Post writing development. Writer given a section of the text back for tweaks, and power outage ripped away several hours of dev work that need to be redone.<br /> <b>- Sothis Ascends</b> (MtC): First draft heading into redlines.<br /> <b>- Cursed Necropolis: Rio</b> (MtC): First draft heading into redlines.<br /> <b>- nWoD: Dark Eras:</b><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> All but one 2nd draft is in, and Black Hat Matt expects to be able to run a focused dev pass on that to get it to editing too.</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T06:32:28-07:00","id":177880,"title":"","content":"The only thing that will make me feel better about this are some sweet, sweet spoilers about the Deceived. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T06:54:33-07:00","id":177887,"title":"","content":"My Changeling game finally came to a close over the weekend. I plan on starting my Mummy game in five weeks' time. If the Book of the Deceived comes out before then I will be the happiest little GM imaginable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T15:04:02-07:00","id":178264,"title":"","content":"I'm with you there. My partner and I still haven't started our big <i>Mummy</i> campaign and it's just getting more delayed than ever as we're moving to Boston. <i>Book of the Deceived</i> is becoming so delayed, though, I'm tempted to just hold off on the campaign until it comes out, seeing as we won't be starting soon anyway. That and <i>Dark Eras</i>, where I'll be using <i>Mummy</i>'s Era as the campaign setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T11:30:46-07:00","id":179083,"title":"","content":"If the wait is going to be similar to how <i>Mummy the Curse </i>took awhile to come out as a hard copy, I will be eager but patient as I wait for <i>Book of the Decieved. </i>Its been fairly interesting so far to see what the players tend to do as they play with/as/against mummies in the few campaigns I have been doing. Each companion book for MtC so far has added new fun twists to the campaigns I been running and my players seem to be enjoying it as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3338-child_of_osiris","name":"Child_of_Osiris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T04:54:14-07:00","id":179575,"title":"","content":"The rapture is at hand, and the Judges are most pleased that the <i>Book</i> is in editing...or are they? <span style=\"font-size:8px\">yes</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>- Book of the Deceived</b> (MtC): In Editing.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>- Sothis Ascends</b> (MtC): First draft heading into redlines.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>- Cursed Necropolis: Rio</b> (MtC): First draft heading into redlines.<br /> <b>- nWoD: Dark Eras:</b><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> All but one 2nd draft is in, and Black Hat Matt expects to be able to run a focused dev pass on that to get it to editing too.<br /> </span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T07:49:07-07:00","id":179705,"title":"","content":"Whelp, I'm excited. And kinda wishing that I'd known about the existence of Mummy when it was in Kickstarter. I'm going to have to hope that it's out by the time I'm back in the country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T07:58:08-07:00","id":179710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=179575#post179575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rapture is at hand, and the Judges are most pleased that the <i>Book</i> is in editing...or are they? <span style=\"font-size:8px\">yes</span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't realized I counted as a Judge. Yes, I am pleased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T13:10:51-07:00","id":179982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=179575#post179575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rapture is at hand, and the Judges are most pleased that the <i>Book</i> is in editing...or are they? <span style=\"font-size:8px\">yes</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I worked on the very last chunk of stuff that needed fine tuning for Deceived. There was one thing in particular we wanted to get just right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T13:45:32-07:00","id":180041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=179982#post179982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe I worked on the very last chunk of stuff that needed fine tuning for Deceived. There was one thing in particular we wanted to get just right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting...I'm anxious to maybe hear about this once it's released. I'm always curious in the design/development process, because it's interesting to see what concepts were troublesome to execute. If I remember correctly, amkhata in the core were reworked a few times; I'm still curious about that, too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T13:50:46-07:00","id":180043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=179982#post179982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe I worked on the very last chunk of stuff that needed fine tuning for Deceived. There was one thing in particular we wanted to get just right.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...any chance at a spoiler?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T18:45:56-07:00","id":180258,"title":"","content":"Can't wait for Book of the Deceived and Dreams of Avarice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T04:25:25-07:00","id":180668,"title":"","content":"A spoiler would be fantastic. The anticipation is killing me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T05:08:12-07:00","id":180704,"title":"","content":"I'd love to just see the table of contents. We know that the Deceived will be presented as playable characters as well as antagonists, as well as part 2 of the Avarice Chronicle campaign, but what else will the supplement contain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T11:34:18-07:00","id":181056,"title":"","content":"A bag of star shaped confetti, naturally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T15:59:52-07:00","id":181322,"title":"","content":"Maybe a few new affinities, maybe a few new utterances, and maybe some new relics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3338-child_of_osiris","name":"Child_of_Osiris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T17:23:32-07:00","id":181464,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about Affinities and Utterances. What we know about the Deceived suggests that their magic is very different from that of the Arisen, and the developers have been heard to say that there is a marked difference between the two kinds of Deathless. So I'm not really counting on there being much in the Book of the Deceived that would be all that useful to Mummy players (unless they were to play as Deceived). Everything suggests that the Deceived learned the Will, the free-form part of Iremite magic, while other Arisen were busy learning the Word.<br /> <br /> Judging by D.C. though, we might be getting abstract concepts as relics. That should be pretty awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T00:24:46-07:00","id":181737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=181464#post181464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure about Affinities and Utterances. What we know about the Deceived suggests that their magic is very different from that of the Arisen, and the developers have been heard to say that there is a marked difference between the two kinds of Deathless. So I'm not really counting on there being much in the Book of the Deceived that would be all that useful to Mummy players (unless they were to play as Deceived). Everything suggests that the Deceived learned the Will, the free-form part of Iremite magic, while other Arisen were busy learning the Word.<br /> <br /> Judging by D.C. though, we might be getting abstract concepts as relics. That should be pretty awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>You guys are so good at reading the deep down stuff in the mummy books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T02:50:13-07:00","id":181791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RisTigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=181737#post181737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You guys are so good at reading the deep down stuff in the mummy books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. When you're trying to write a campaign and one of the splat's principal antagonists are nothing more than vague rumours and the occasionally mentioned point of difference, you end up trying desperately to piece together what little you do have into something cohesive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T05:02:30-07:00","id":181822,"title":"","content":"Surely there will be affinities as all Mummies seem to get them in one way or another. By &quot;all Mummies&quot; I mean the only two we know about, but that's enough of a precedent to feel confident that the Deceived will have them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Utterances are independent of Mummy power and are ambiguously stolen secrets after the Rite was completed. I'm sure the Deceived will have a way to access them, just like the Shuankhsen have a way. While the Deceived are a unique breed and warrant a different play experience, on a pragmatic level I don't think they would write a book and say, &quot;Here's a new type of character, but they can't use <i>any</i> of the powers in the <i>core book</i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T05:36:27-07:00","id":181841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=181822#post181822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surely there will be affinities as all Mummies seem to get them in one way or another. By &quot;all Mummies&quot; I mean the only two we know about, but that's enough of a precedent to feel confident that the Deceived will have them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Utterances are independent of Mummy power and are ambiguously stolen secrets after the Rite was completed. I'm sure the Deceived will have a way to access them, just like the Shuankhsen have a way. While the Deceived are a unique breed and warrant a different play experience, on a pragmatic level I don't think they would write a book and say, &quot;Here's a new type of character, but they can't use <i>any</i> of the powers in the <i>core book</i>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Affinities are a possibility (aspects of the soul and everything). However, all the information we have indicates that Utterances are manifestations of &quot;the Word&quot;, to use the Sesha-Hebsu term. The Sesha-Hebsu are also quite sure that the Sixth Guild dealt with &quot;the Will&quot;, which gave them the dangerous knowledge of how to create rituals and spells of their own. Utterances, stolen though they may be, are still just rote magic. There's no experimentation to be done with them. You utter the spell, the spell has an effect, and it will always have that same effect (barring the occasional Utterance like Dream of Dead Gods that lets you pick from a few different ones). The Will is described in very different terms. From what I've read, having access to the Will is like a grounding in something like Chemistry. You understand the underlying laws of magic, why it works the way it does, and that means you can experiment with a reasonable idea of what the effects will be. It sounds more like Mage magic than the rote-powers of the Arisen.<br /> <br /> As Deathless though, I fully expect Deceived to follow many of the other Mummy rules. I'm sure they'll have Pillars and Sekhem for example, although I imagine they'll have their own spin on the Sekhem rules. Maybe even use Sekhem more like a normal power stat like the other splats. The Deceived were destroyed before Irem fell, after all. Since the other Mummies are aware of the betrayal, that means that it was before even the Rite of Return. Which means that any Deceived that still exist must be around due to some spell of their own devising, rather than the work of the Shan'iatu, which likely means they'll be operating on a very different wavelength to Mummies (I doubt they'll have bound themselves to the service of a Judge, for example, so no dropping Sekhem for not following your purpose).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T09:34:20-07:00","id":182051,"title":"","content":"I imagine that the Deceived have some way to exist entirely independent from the Judges, because they sure aren't friends of the Judges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T11:21:41-07:00","id":182117,"title":"","content":"I'm with Azahul on this one. Particularly in regard to the different template aspects the Deceived might have in relation to the Arisen. Since all they really have in common is that they are both Deathless creatures. <br /> <br /> <b>Affinities -</b><br /> <br /> The Deceived MIGHT have affinities, but that's a big maybe. <br /> <br /> Considering that affinities were powers designed into the Arisen through the Rite of Return by the Shan'Iatu. As Azahul mentioned, the Deceived were purged before the Rite of Return was starting to be enacted. So they never underwent the Rite. Its implied that their ability to manipulate Names allowed them to make their own method of becoming Deathless. So there is in-universe absolutely no reason for them to have access to affinities. On a more pragmatic out-of-game look, I'd bet they have something similar/equivalent if they just don't have outright access to them in some sort of &quot;universal truth/backdoor&quot; way.<br /> <br /> <b>Utterances -</b><br /> <br /> I really hope the Deceived actually don't have access to Utterances. Mainly because Utterances are perfect examples of &quot;rote magical effects&quot; that very much fit with the idea that the Arisen only have the &quot;word&quot; part of the magic puzzle. The Deceived will, once again, likely have something that is equivalent, but I really hope the big reveal about Name/Will magic is not just a set of unique Utterances, that would be a massive let down. <br /> <br /> <b>Pillars -</b><br /> <br /> I'll be interested to see if the Deceived have a favored pillar/decree. Since that aspect of the Arisen seems to be tied into their relationship with the Judges. It would make sense given the metaphysical underpinning of Mummy that they have Pillars and a five-fold soul, but with the information we have I can't see them having decrees. Then again, one rumour about them talks about them all being Ren decree. So maybe they do only have one pillar but its not capped at 5? <br /> <br /> \u200bThen again the whole Ren thing stinks to me of the Arisen trying to rationalize something they know basically nothing about in terms they understand. <br /> <br /> <b>Sekhem -</b> <br /> <br /> Goes without saying they will have this. Though I will be interested to see how their Sekhem system works. Does it behave more like traditional power stats and climb? Does it rise and fall? Does it every drop to 0 like with the Arisen? I guess this all links into the idea of if the Deceived are continuous immortals in contrast to the Arisens bursts of activity. <br /> <br /> <b>Relics -</b> <br /> <br /> Seems Deceived interact with the abstract matrix of magic that forms different relics depending on its shape rather then the physical aspect of a relic. So I'd say they can and do interact with all the relic types we are familiar with. Likely as well or better then Arisen of the Relics's corresponding Guild at least. They also likely have some unique &quot;abstract&quot; relic aspect that is likely part of their magic system. <br /> <br /> <b>Misc -</b><br /> <br /> I am wondering how much like the Arisen the Deceived are physically as well. Are they as tough and unkillable? Considering a lot of the Arisen's template's perks are designed to keep them going to do the Judges will the Deceived could be very different in this regard as well. Perhaps something more like the &quot;Reborn&quot; type immortals in the Immortals splat book for core WoD. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=181822#post181822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While the Deceived are a unique breed and warrant a different play experience, on a pragmatic level I don't think they would write a book and say, &quot;Here's a new type of character, but they can't use <i>any</i> of the powers in the <i>core book</i>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly, I'm taking the opposite view. Even with the idea that the Shaunkshen have Affinities and can steal Utterances comes from the fluff relating them to the Rite and the similar relationship they have with their patron that the Arisen have with the Judges. The Deceived meanwhile, seem to be working on a completely different paradigm to achieve their Deathless state. <br /> <br /> I really hope the Deceived are such a different type of Deathless that the books about the Arisen basically don't apply to them in terms of mechanics except for when it comes to Deceived magic effecting Arisen and Arisen magic effecting Deceived. Sure common names such as Sekhem and Pillars can and probably should apply, but the systems for those traits should behave differently. <br /> <br /> Though for me the perfect Deceived would be a variation on the Arisen template with true free-form Mage style magic running along the themes of - Names, Matter, Energy, Death and Astronomy. Similar to the expanded Blood Magic rules for Vampire found in Blasphemies and Sacraments. <br /> <br /> Just my 2p on the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T13:39:57-07:00","id":182188,"title":"","content":"Man, I could use a spoiler or two right now.<br /> <br /> If the Deceived represent the flip-side of the Arisen, tapping into a deeper understanding of the Nameless Empire's magic, I wonder if the magical effects they can accomplish will somehow be limited in power or scope when compared to the upper limits of what the Arisen can do. In other words, the Deceived sacrifice power for flexibility. If that's the case, I further wonder whether a Deceived and an Arisen, working in unison, can recreate the true magic of the Shan'iatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T15:19:42-07:00","id":182257,"title":"","content":"Alright, alright. You guys have convinced me.<br /> <br /> Y'all are leaving out the most important factor, though: Memory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T16:36:29-07:00","id":182360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=182257#post182257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, alright. You guys have convinced me.<br /> <br /> Y'all are leaving out the most important factor, though: Memory</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point actually. All the evidence we've been given about the Deceived so far paints them has having basically &quot;true&quot; recall of what Irem was REALLY like. So if they have Memory as a stat its going to work on a different level of sins and what information they have access to at what ratings for sure. <br /> <br /> I wonder really if their morality stat will be Memory at all. They, like the Shuankshen might be on Morality. Though like the Shuankshen they are likely pretty terrible at it. Given that the examples we've seen of them so far seem to be somewhat...lacking...in moral fortitude. <br /> <br /> Then again they might have a whole new Morality system? Who knows, we can't say without knowing more about how their Deathless state works really. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'm wondering if the Apothesis link from Guildhalls is a bit of a red-herring and its the Arisen confusing certain aspects of the Deceived's innate state with their own transcendence. Or maybe they are partially linked. Maybe the Deceived display certain qualities only assigned to the the Apothesis state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T23:54:47-07:00","id":182682,"title":"","content":"Well the Deceived are mummys, so i guess that they will definitvley share atleast some traits with the Arisen, like decrees and pillars . But the greatest Question is , what was the great betreyal? Who betrayed Whom and Why? Thats the thing iam most courios about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T05:01:47-07:00","id":182800,"title":"","content":"Here's a fair speculation about the Deceived:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I think the Sixth Guild heard about the Shan'iatu's plans for the Rite of Return, and probably having to sacrifice the entire Empire to pay the cost of the Rite and whatever else they cooked up, and...disagreed. Hence they were wiped out...or were they? The answer, of course, is no they weren't.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> But a couple of posters above brought up a good point. If they weren't part of the Rite of Return then who bound them up as Mummies and why? Hell, since they hated the Shan'iatu and the Judges then what made them want to be [Deceived] Mummies? If they didn't want to be part of the Rite then why would they want to be part of some other coven's Mummification rituals? Or were they tricked into that plan anyway?<br /> <br /> Or...were they...<b>DECEIVED</b>?!<br /> <br /> Come on! That's gotta be it now! They thought that they were fighting against the Shan'iatu and their Rite of Return, but in their blind rebellion they didn't realize they had fallen for some other trap - a <b>deception </b>that led them right where they didn't want to end up. Now they hunt down the Arisen for being loyal servants of the bastard that had tricked them (the Deceived) into becoming Mummies after all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:53:54-07:00","id":183061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeadGuy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=182682#post182682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the Deceived are mummys, so i guess that they will definitvley share atleast some traits with the Arisen, like decrees and pillars . But the greatest Question is , what was the great betreyal? Who betrayed Whom and Why? Thats the thing iam most courios about.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said before, considering the Deceived where not part of the Rite of Return there is no real in universe president for them to have a Decree. Pillars I can see, as that's an underpinning aspect of the magical metaphysics of the Mummy setting. The Decree is however directly tied to the Arisens relationship with the Judges and their involved in the Rite of Return that sent them to Duat.<br /> <br /> At current, well, we have no idea exactly how the Deceived managed to become Deathless. There is some vague stuff about their Name Magic allowing them to do it, but that's really abstract and seems to basically be a guess on from the Arisen's perspective. <br /> <br /> I've always seen it (in my own headcannon, soon to be joshed no doubt) that they inflicted the Deathless state on themselves to basically get revenge on the remaining Iremites. To be fair, all the fluff we have for them that does include even a light aspect of their own point of view seems to paint them as very anti-Irem, however, I don't think their innately anti-Arisen if that makes sense. Screw with Irem's legacy and the Judges &quot;divine plan&quot; or whatever, but I think they have a more humanistic view on individual Arisen. After all, the only thing better then destroying the tools of your enemy is to turn them back upon their masters. Hence the link to Apothesis possibly. <br /> <br /> I never saw it as them getting fooled into a sorta &quot;backup ritual&quot; or something. Though its entirely possible and does provide an explanation for their name. Though I do wonder what the Deceived call themselves? Do they keep their old Iremite Guild Name? Have they rejected that and created a new title? What do they call the Arisen?<br /> <br /> All those questions are kinda fascinating really and one of the many, many reasons that I am looking forward to this book immensely. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T11:03:55-07:00","id":183067,"title":"","content":"It's interesting and entirely plausible, but, uh, do we know if the Deceived actually call themselves by that name? Because every bit of information we have on them, as far as I'm aware, is from an Arisen perspective. Which means that &quot;the Deceived&quot; is a name given to them by their enemies, lending itself to a very different set of connotations. To me, it suggests that the Deceived claim some kind of higher knowledge, which Arisen dismiss by claiming that they must have been mislead/deceived. It does raise the question of who, or what, deceived them however.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A random thought occurs. As Hawthorn mentioned, it is believed that all members of the sixth Guild were of the Ren Decree (although whether that is a reliable piece of information is unknown). Now, the Ren are the serpent-headed, and in Iremite mythology there is a Serpent-headed God (one of the six gods who stand above the Judges) called Sutek, or the Nameless Serpent, who was responsible for the death and then the resurrection/ascension of Azar. We know that the Arisen have a connection to Anpu, the Jackal-headed God whose job it is to ferry souls back and forth between the world and the afterlife, perhaps the Deceived have a similar relationship with Sutek?<br /> <br /> Intrigued by this thought, I went and skimmed over a few of the relevant sections in the corebook. Sutek was asked to become the guardian of the ladder that allows beings to ascend to heaven. He's also closely linked to the Amulet of Two Fingers (to the extent that the &quot;two fingers&quot; are considered by some to actually be Sutek's own fingers), supposedly a vital part of achieving apotheosis. The Deceived and their lost lore have been linked to Apotheosis before, like in one of the Sesha-Hebsu sections of Guildhalls.<br /> <br /> I'm reaching pretty hard here, but the brief mentions of Irem's proper gods have always intrigued me and I'm fascinated at the prospect of using Anpu in my games. It'd be interesting if Sutek were similarly prominent for the Deceived. They are, after all, both gods who watch over spaces of transition, which makes it easy to imagine scenarios in which they would come up. Anpu, of course, guides Arisen through the Death Cycle, Sutek would naturally appear when a character seeks to climb the Ladder of Sutek (which basically seems to mean the same thing as &quot;achieve Apotheosis&quot;.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As for why they might want to become Deathless, my current theory is that it was an act of desperation. With five Guilds plus the combined might of the Shan'iatu closing in on them, the sixth Guild chose to preserve themselves beyond death. They were the ones with access to, I suspect, the very kind of magic that was used to forge the Rite of Return. Exactly what price they may have paid for this knowledge... I cannot say. Perhaps, in keeping with the astronomy theme running through them, they are bound even more to the movements of the cosmos than the Arisen? Just speculation there.<br /> <br /> I will say that I don't think them hating the Judges/Shan'iatu would have had much to do with the decision to become Deathless. The way the Rite is described makes me feel that it was explicitly created to bind Arisen to serve the Judges, rather than &quot;serve the Judges&quot; being an essential part of fuelling the spell or anything.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ok, Hawthorn beat me to it with my first and last points. The stuff in the spoiler is still good though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 06-28-2014, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T17:26:04-07:00","id":191843,"title":"","content":"The new schedule indicates that Book of the Deceived will release in October and Sothis Ascends will arrive in December. <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule\" target=\"_blank\"> Current Projects &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/schedule </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T06:53:21-07:00","id":192347,"title":"","content":"If we're not getting the Deceived until October, I think some spoilers are in order to tide us over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T07:03:37-07:00","id":196752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=192347#post192347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're not getting the Deceived until October, I think some spoilers are in order to tide us over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to sound anti-social, but can you PLEASE stop asking for spoilers on every page of this thread (or making every post you contribute be a basic spoilers request). Requesting spoilers is fine, but doing so multiple times (in a row) without contributing any other sort of content or discussion to a forum is (basically making it the only reason you post on this thread), I feel, bad etiquette.<br /> <br /> (Yes I realize its a pretty massive irony for me to talk about etiquette, I was the guy that basically bad-mouthed the devs a couple months ago before DC came out.) <br /> <br /> The dev's will give us spoilers when they have spoilers to give and they feel its about the right time. With previous Mummy books (Guildhalls and DC) this was a month or two before the book was released and consisted of a single blog entry or forum post. <br /> <br /> I can understand wanting to make sure people know that we the fans what spoilers (and see said request), as I am pretty sure we do, as a community, enjoy them. However, while the devs might not be on the forum board that much, I suspect they do actually back read stuff in forum discussions they find interesting. So making more then one request is kinda unnecessary and kinda tedious. <br /> <br /> Please know I'm not trying to be a jerk here, its just something I felt needed to be mentioned for all the reasons I mentioned above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T13:06:03-07:00","id":197117,"title":"","content":"Man, I am getting more and more fascinated with the Deceived as I reread the Mummy corebook in preparation for my upcoming campaign.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I was flicking through the Shuankhsen section and the bit about the principles of magic caught my eye. Basically, the two core principles are that power must be paid for with suffering, and that no being may avoid paying that price. I guess Relics are the current prime example of this, even if they do get around the latter principle to some extent due to Guild sympathies. However, if Deceived do come with some kind of unique magic system, the above makes it sound like it could involve some rather nasty trade-offs. The synopsis of the Book of the Deceived on the site calls the Deceived &quot;dark reflections&quot; of the Arisen, and if they wield a more free-form kind of magic that relies on suffering for its fuel... well, I'd certainly say that counts as a &quot;dark reflection&quot;.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The sad thing is that I'm currently shying away from the Deceived having any significant role in my campaign at present, due to not having any real information on them. I could probably figure out some workarounds here, but I feel like the Shuankhsen I have written up should be ample foils for the player characters. When the Book of the Deceived comes up, we'll see if I can slot a member of the Deceived or two into the game at a later point.<br /> <br /> One thing I'll be interested to see is if it is theoretically possible for Arisen to learn Deceived magic. The bits in DC make me think that it might be, since the city was apparently built using some knowledge from the Deceived, and the ability of Arisen to use Utterances suggest that it could be viable for them to master the Will as well. Or, maybe, the Rite may prevent them from doing so, but Mummies who achieve Apotheosis will get access to that kind of power.<br /> <br /> So many possibilities. Only three-four months before we find out the truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T13:11:04-07:00","id":197124,"title":"","content":"There's some Deceived magic in the Guildhalls book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T21:58:46-07:00","id":197495,"title":"","content":"Is there? It's been a while since I read it. What part are you talking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T22:10:44-07:00","id":197524,"title":"","content":"The mechanics section, the Sesha Hebsu entry - it has one or two Deceived Utterances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T22:16:35-07:00","id":197536,"title":"","content":"I dunno. They may have been born of research into the Lost Guild, but they are very much Word-based Utterances. Everything we know about the Deceived says they go in the opposite direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T01:14:40-07:00","id":197673,"title":"","content":"The Deceived master the Word, though, right? They are the masters of true names","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T09:35:02-07:00","id":197975,"title":"","content":"The Word is separate from The Name. Sesha Hebsu master the former. It's why they considered the Deceived to be their sister guild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T05:15:09-07:00","id":198833,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see.<br /> <br /> Also, this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>- Book of the Deceived</b> (MtC): In Editing. Full page art is coming in.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>- Sothis Ascends</b> (MtC): Some text was re-distributed and needs further writing, otherwise in redlines.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>- Cursed Necropolis: Rio</b> (MtC): First drafts heading into redlines.<br /> <br /> <b>- nWoD: Dark Eras:</b><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> The VtR section is benefiting from a focused dev pass, while the rest of the Eras are in editing.</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T10:24:33-07:00","id":200208,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the information on the Deceived suggests they were something called will-workers, focussing on the Will part of magic while the Sesha-Hebsu focussed on the Word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T17:03:46-07:00","id":263257,"title":"","content":"It's been a couple months since this has been updated and there's been...well, some changes by the looks of it. Mostly Book of the Deceived will begin layout soon, with placeholders for the art! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T20:45:04-07:00","id":263369,"title":"","content":"I have high hopes that the book will allow us to run chronicles with Lost Guild PCs. I suppose we'll find out next month!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T05:20:19-07:00","id":263654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=263369#post263369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have high hopes that the book will allow us to run chronicles with Lost Guild PCs. I suppose we'll find out next month!</div> </div> </div> </div>Deceived PCs has been part of the supplement's pitch since day one. You're in luck! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T07:21:29-07:00","id":263754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=263654#post263654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deceived PCs has been part of the supplement's pitch since day one. You're in luck! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought so, but I couldn't remember if that was the case. Definitely glad to hear it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T08:46:36-07:00","id":269122,"title":"","content":"Looks like as of yesterday, Book of the Deceived has completed text and is fully art directed. Work on it seems to be on hold until Dark Ages Vampire gets roughed in and Art of the Changing Breeds is complete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T10:08:16-07:00","id":269228,"title":"","content":"Also Sothis Ascends has vaulted past Redlines and Second Draft straight into Dev. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T17:00:18-07:00","id":269604,"title":"","content":"<b>Sothis Ascends</b> was started a long while ago, according to the Gentleman Gamer who's writing parts of it. So it's stage progress isn't too much of a surprise, but I'm glad to see it's coming. I think Malcolm (?) also has been working on <b>Dreams of Avarice</b> for a while, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T08:42:30-07:00","id":270825,"title":"","content":"If Memory serves then Dreams of Avarice was contracted December 2013 (according to one of the last Kickstarter backer e-mails). When CAS briefly returned to this thread about 6ish months ago he mentioned in passing it was in first drafts at the time. I think the only thing keeping it from Redlines is the fact its got two other books in front of it. Or that's what I hope is the case at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T06:47:53-07:00","id":274691,"title":"","content":"It seems that <b>Book of the Deceived</b> is...<b>cursed</b>.<br /> <br /> ...no one has made that pun yet, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T07:01:50-07:00","id":274699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=274691#post274691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems that <b>Book of the Deceived</b> is...<b>cursed</b>.<br /> <br /> ...no one has made that pun yet, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what we get for stealing the Forbidden Texts from those ancient tombs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T07:47:23-07:00","id":274718,"title":"","content":"See, the thing of the matter? is that <i>the entire Mummy Line is cursed</i>.<br /> <br /> And let's be fair, we heard all about that going in. I'm not sure how surprised we should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T09:24:00-07:00","id":275500,"title":"","content":"I'm working on Mummy stuff right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T09:32:11-07:00","id":275507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=275500#post275500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on Mummy stuff right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are my <i>emotions</i> you're toying with right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T15:32:08-07:00","id":275812,"title":"","content":"I had to research creation myths and cover sheets for classified documents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T16:59:36-07:00","id":275871,"title":"","content":"Sounds remarkably like the research required to write the opening story piece of the Storyteller's section in the Mummy core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T05:10:39-07:00","id":276182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=275812#post275812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had to research creation myths and cover sheets for classified documents.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the most <b>Mummy</b> spoilers we've had since <b>DC</b> came out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T09:07:00-07:00","id":276411,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing <b>Dreams of Avarice</b>. The classified cover sheet makes me think of stuff like the Horror Recognition Guide or the Testament of Longinus. Maybe a cult managed to get their hands on a copy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T19:27:15-07:00","id":276915,"title":"","content":"Last I heard, that is what Malcolm has been working on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T04:37:35-07:00","id":277100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=274718#post274718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the thing of the matter? is that <i>the entire Mummy Line is cursed</i>.<br /> <br /> And let's be fair, we heard all about that going in. I'm not sure how surprised we should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me started...just don't.<br /> <br /> (All I have to say is that Demon is less then 12 Months old as a line and is waiting for 1 final book (not including Dark Eras) before its done. Mummy is over 18 months old as a line and we are waiting on the majority of the core-line books and at least half the Kickstarter products.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T15:04:22-07:00","id":277584,"title":"","content":"I think what's frustrating about Mummy isn't the fact that it's late - any book can have bad luck. It's that the community appears to have zero effect on development. Honestly, that's how most games are developed, but I've gotten really used to how the other Onyx Path games are made. <br /> <br /> I can make all sorts of suggestions on most other Onyx Path projects, and be reasonably sure that the devs will consider them. They might reject them, or even decide that they need to make the counterpoint even stronger, but we have a collective effect in open development. With Mummy, the community isn't usually asked anything at all. I know RichT isn't into pushing an unwilling dev into open dev, and I respect that.<br /> <br /> Maybe the reason for the secrecy is just the nature of Mummy's design, where the storyteller knows all the secrets and the players learn as their characters memory raises. I don't really know. <br /> <br /> I have high hopes for Deceived, though and if it ends up being good, I'll make some noise, do what I can to spread the word. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T16:13:15-07:00","id":277666,"title":"","content":"I'm not terribly bothered by the lack of open development, personally. If I had serious problems with some of the content of previous books, sure, but thus far every book in the Mummy line (all, what, three of them?) has been great. So long as I end up with a quality product to use in my games, I have no qualms about a lack of input in the book's design.<br /> <br /> The delays are frustrating, but increasingly less so since I started actually running the game. As much as I'd love to actually use the Deceived, it's not as if I'm lacking for stories to tell at the moment. I think the revelation of just how many possibilities there are in Mummy already helped temper the desire for more content. That said, I will be absolutely ecstatic when Deceived finally does drop. I've been looking forward to it more than any other book in the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T16:35:53-07:00","id":277676,"title":"","content":"One very good reason that there's not open dev is that Mummy is a new line. All the products in open dev are games that are getting second, third, or fourth editions. Who knows, maybe there will be open dev in a few years when they start thinking about updating it to nWoD 2nd Ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T16:37:34-07:00","id":277677,"title":"","content":"Yeah, open development hasn't been my concern either. It's just...a big part of selling people on your awesome game is <i>hype</i>, and without CAS or writers around very often to talk about the game it's hard to build hype. DaveB is, you know, on the other end of the extreme where you <i>can't get him to stop talking</i> about <b>Mage</b> - which is great! I just don't expect that from every developer.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy</b> gets all these nominations and awards as a great game, but I think a lot of people don't know what they can do with the game. A few people have APs up, and I'll write one once I start mine (playing other games until <b>Dark Eras</b> comes out), but yeah. Hype.<br /> <br /> At least all of <b>Mummy</b>'s supplements are amazing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T18:34:15-07:00","id":277736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=277676#post277676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One very good reason that there's not open dev is that Mummy is a new line. All the products in open dev are games that are getting second, third, or fourth editions. Who knows, maybe there will be open dev in a few years when they start thinking about updating it to nWoD 2nd Ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's absolutely part of it. It seems like open development for a new game where so much of the premise revolves around secrets and hidden knowledge would be a wee bit difficult.<br /> <br /> Watching Mummy development does feel a bit strange after coming from other games, where spoilers abound up to six months before release. Deceived was meant to drop this month but we haven't had a peep. It's a... novel approach to advertising, certainly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T18:58:27-07:00","id":277750,"title":"","content":"Every new mummy book seems to drop bigger bombshells than the demon supplements. I can sort of understand the secrecy--i feel bad for sts just getting into Mummy already starting with Guildhalls. The pacing seems to be because every supplement fundamentally changes the game in some way. As an ST id be too tempted to share late-book secrets before new players have even gotten into the corebook Mummy mindset. I dislike the delays, but the lack of two sided communication is disheartening. Spoilery previews, mysterious statements, or even &quot;we cant comment on that, but it will be addressed somewhere&quot; is better than silence. DaveB may have more free time perhaps, but he alone is a major sparkle in the game line because he is around to clarify things or even help you design things for your personal games. At the very least, the mummy devs could be a little more Anpu and a little less Sutek. It might draw more people to the game. Heres to hoping!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T19:05:52-07:00","id":277752,"title":"","content":"I am a big fan of the core, but I've had mixed feelings about the supplements. Maybe they merit a re-read now that I've played some Mummy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Edit: No mixed feelings about Cursed Necropolis. That's good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T19:25:22-07:00","id":277756,"title":"","content":"So just mixed feelings about Guildhalls then?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=277750#post277750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every new mummy book seems to drop bigger bombshells than the demon supplements. I can sort of understand the secrecy--i feel bad for sts just getting into Mummy already starting with Guildhalls. The pacing seems to be because every supplement fundamentally changes the game in some way. As an ST id be too tempted to share late-book secrets before new players have even gotten into the corebook Mummy mindset. I dislike the delays, but the lack of two sided communication is disheartening. Spoilery previews, mysterious statements, or even &quot;we cant comment on that, but it will be addressed somewhere&quot; is better than silence. DaveB may have more free time perhaps, but he alone is a major sparkle in the game line because he is around to clarify things or even help you design things for your personal games. At the very least, the mummy devs could be a little more Anpu and a little less Sutek. It might draw more people to the game. Heres to hoping!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if starting with access to Guildhalls of the Deathless is in any way bad. In fact, I feel sorry for anyone who tried to run a game of Mummy before it came out. Back-of-book spoilers aside, it's a fundamental piece of world design about the most important elements of Mummy society. It makes it so much easier to understand how the guilds work and the scale at which they operate. This isn't stuff that's easy to insert into a chronicle on the fly, like an antagonist book such as Book of the Deceived will hopefully be. Guildhalls is about how you design the world your players will be living in.<br /> <br /> The stuff in the spoiler section isn't even all that groundbreaking. Some nice Affinities and Utterances, a few cool bits of information about each Guild (the Tef-Aabhi in particular are fascinating), but nothing that I feel spoils the game by having integrated right from the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T20:36:48-07:00","id":277802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=277756#post277756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So just mixed feelings about Guildhalls then?</div> </div> </div> </div>That and the Ready Made Character Pack, which seemed a lot like a VtR supplement. <br /> <br /> Guildhalls had excellent mechanics - specifically the Talisman creation rules, but I preferred the corebook's presentation of the Guilds themselves. Like I said though, I may be judging it a little harshly and the book definitely merits a re-read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T23:30:00-07:00","id":277945,"title":"","content":"First off, let me say that Mummy stuff is in the pipe, though there have been hiccups as there often are not only with individual lines, but the significantly escalated business of Onyx Path itself. Part of this ramp up has included the announcement and release of a bunch of new games and books in rapid succession. Mummy looks submerged, but keep in mind we're a year and a half in, just as other lines are ramping up. Beyond that, CAS is a pretty busy guy who works with other games, fiction and music.<br /> <br /> I don't want to put words in CAS' mouth but my feeling is that Mummy's combined releases are really designed for a unified look at a work of epic scope with immortals, a lost civilization and its gods. At the same time CAS believes strongly in collaboration, took in a huge amount of input at various stages from you, and it informs the collaboration that takes place between writers, but all with the aim of making something as uncompromising about its core ideas as possible. Maybe in a perfect world Mummy would have been released in 2015 in three 800 page volumes of a single, titanic work, but nobody can afford to produce or really purchase that and besides, this would make the option of taking what you want from the game a tad more difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T02:00:32-07:00","id":278004,"title":"","content":"Speaking of movement: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...f-the-deceived</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T05:52:15-07:00","id":278090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=277750#post277750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pacing seems to be because every supplement fundamentally changes the game in some way. As an ST id be too tempted to share late-book secrets before new players have even gotten into the corebook Mummy mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I intend on being very conscious of, with the first few sessions to be very corebook-only. My PC isn't going to have any character creation options beyond what was initially presented, and the plot is just a basic relic hunt. The core book is absolutely usable, while admittedly thin, but my entire campaign arc was formed before <b>Guildhalls</b> or <b>DC</b> were released. I want revelations to come progressively, so no crazy <b>Deceived</b> stuff in my campaign for a while.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which...I'm gonna go head over to that thread now! Thanks, Malcolm. Your presence is always appreciated :*<br /> <br /> Yes. That's a kiss <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T06:09:15-07:00","id":278095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=278090#post278090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something I intend on being very conscious of, with the first few sessions to be very corebook-only. My PC isn't going to have any character creation options beyond what was initially presented, and the plot is just a basic relic hunt. The core book is absolutely usable, while admittedly thin, but my entire campaign arc was formed before <b>Guildhalls</b> or <b>DC</b> were released. I want revelations to come progressively, so no crazy <b>Deceived</b> stuff in my campaign for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an attitude I can't wrap my head around. As an antagonist book, the Book of the Deceived will naturally be somewhat different, but there are elements in Guildhalls of the Deathless that a high Guild Status player character should know before the game even begins. There's no reason such a character shouldn't be manifesting Guild-specific Affinities or Utterances from the get-go, and I don't see how letting them do so in any way detracts from the game or its themes. I can't think of any such powers that &quot;fundamentally&quot; alter the game either, or in any way dilute the themes present in the corebook (Talismans do somewhat, but that aside...).<br /> <br /> The additional elements presented in Guildhalls add depth to the most basic elements of Mummy society, and I feel should absolutely be taken into effect when constructing a nome. And if it makes sense for a character to have access to them, it feels natural to allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T06:27:00-07:00","id":278098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=278095#post278095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The additional elements presented in Guildhalls add depth to the most basic elements of Mummy society, and I feel should absolutely be taken into effect when constructing a nome. And if it makes sense for a character to have access to them, it feels natural to allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, when I'm building the setting I'll make some use of it; and for sure, I understand your sentiment in the last sentence. But it's not <i>necessary</i>, and really I want to just experience the core for a little while. I mean, really, don't the supplements kinda mark progress through a Descent?<br /> <br /> 1) pursue your purpose. 2) once you have some Memory back and have some time to spend before henet, partake in guild politics. 3) once you have more Memory back, learn some deep dark <b>Mummy</b> secrets like the Deceived. 4) idk have some flashbacks to pharaonic Egpyt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T01:47:18-07:00","id":278678,"title":"","content":"As someone who ran a Mummy campaign when just the core was out, I can say that Guildhalls produced a fair few issues for my game when it was released. <br /> <br /> Basically, the core presents the Guilds as reasonably apolitical. Sure they are/where institutions with aims and how they go about achieving those aims can cause &quot;politics&quot; to occur. However, I viewed most of the immediate scheme related stuff to the Cult level rather then the Guild level. Likewise, I'd take the idea from the core that in the modern day the Guilds were more fragmented ideologies on how to view the world and Sekhem.<br /> <br /> Guildhalls did wonderful things for the Guilds, really made them actually function as political and social bodies in the modern world. I really liked this and honestly, in retrospect really wish a lot of the info in Guildhalls had been an extra 50 pages in the Corebook. However, it broke the way I and my players had previous looked at the guilds. So trying to suddenly institute guild structure and hierarchy and aims and such was a bit jarring. Its not the main reason that the game fell apart before I could finish it (that was more real life stuff and a crossover element that just did not work) but it did not help. <br /> <br /> To address some points from the previous page -<br /> <br /> Yes I too would have liked Mummy to be more &quot;open-dev&quot; then its been. One of the things I am looking forward too when they give the game a Second Edition is having the chance to comment on the open-dev process for it. Its really jarring that people like Dave Brookshaw, Steve, David Hill, Rose Bailey and &quot;Black Hat&quot; Matt are all really big on open dev blogs, forum posts and preview docs for their lines (which is pretty much the rest of the New World of Darkness and some of the Classic one as well) and then CAS does nothing with it beyond a pre-release forum post about a month before release. (I really hope that Dave Hill or &quot;Black Hat&quot; Matt get to do the second edition, some of the stuff those guys are doing for Dark Ages and Promethean makes me confident they could take Mummy in a different and interesting direction in second edition.) <br /> <br /> It just feels really jarring compared with the rest of what Onyx Path is doing and like CAS is realistically just very busy with &quot;other stuff&quot; and viewing his dev with Onyx Path in a different light to the rest of the devs that work for the company (in so far as its just a lesser priority, which is fair if he's juggling a lot of different projects in other media). <br /> <br /> I don't think in-game secrecy of information is a good excuse for massive delays. In the age of search engines, gaming forums, Wikipedia and TvTropes keeping anything secret about a fictional setting once the material for it is in the public domain is neigh impossible. I understand Mummy is about forgotten memory and discovery of self, but I think we can trust players to separate what they know OOC and what they know IC and not metagame. <br /> <br /> Yes every Mummy splat-book drops bombshells about the setting and this is one of the things that makes them awesome books. However, this links back the somewhat problematic &quot;modular&quot; nature of Mummy and the fact its the only line to not have all the info you need to run a 100% fleshed out game in the core book. Personally, my players were always put off by the sentiment some of the books have that is basically &quot;the rules and info on this will be in the next book (better go buy it when its out if you want them), but we've teased it here&quot;. Likewise, the fact the books are adding vital setting info rather then supplementing it like say the Demon splat-books is not really a reason for massive delays. <br /> <br /> Mummy came out at a busy time for Onyx Path when it was still going through transitions and finalizing its new business model and such. That has meant the game as got &quot;lost in the grind&quot; a little. Still, its not like any of that can't be reversed and one would hope now that everything has settled down (comparably to what it was) that things could move forward a bit more smoothly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T01:56:14-07:00","id":278680,"title":"","content":"Been running Mummy with just the corebook for a while now. Working fine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T02:48:59-07:00","id":278691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=278680#post278680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been running Mummy with just the corebook for a while now. Working fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to sound trite, but please note I said &quot;100% fleshed out game&quot;, not that a game of Mummy could not be run with just the Corebook. As my previous post mentioned, I ran a Mummy game for a prolonged period of time with just the core. Filling the gaps in the setting with my own material. <br /> <br /> Perhaps a better phrase would be - 100% fleshed out game setting. My apologies for the unclear language of my last post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T13:06:29-07:00","id":278983,"title":"","content":"I don't think any corebook without any supplements can be 100% fleshed out. I think the Mummy corebook provides the essential experience that later supplements are building on.<br /> <br /> Demon is the same way, IMO. First book teased Seattle and the children of Demons. Heirs of Hell and the Seattle book provided fleshed out rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 10-12-2014, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T13:29:22-07:00","id":278993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=278983#post278983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think any corebook without any supplements can be 100% fleshed out. I think the Mummy corebook provides the essential experience that later supplements are building on.<br /> <br /> Demon is the same way, IMO. First book teased Seattle and the children of Demons. Heirs of Hell and the Seattle book provided fleshed out rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, you can have a very exciting chronice using just the Corebook. That being said it could have included some material from Guildhalls of the Deathless and some information on Nome structure like DC to helpe the Storyteller and Player have a better grasp of the game and how Mummy Society worked. I hope if we ever get a 2ed, the corebook includes some of these elements, like Guild structure, Nomes, Talismans, and unison casting besides of course nice rules revisions and a better organized book. I expect some changes to make it more organic and evocative like Blood and Smoke did for Vampire, but the backstory shouldn\u00b4t be touched at all, Cas did a really work of art there, I don\u00b4t want any of it to change! It is really really dark, and very addictive!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T17:22:05-07:00","id":279184,"title":"","content":"I think talismans and unison casting were better left off until the supplement. Base Mummies can engage in political scheming once they remember their Guild at Memory 3 plus they have cults; talismans are super nice but not necessary.<br /> <br /> The core said, &quot;Okay, your Sekhem drops as soon as you wake up.&quot; It's up to the supplements to provide another engaging dynamic by saying, &quot;Okay. Actually, here's some ways to work around that.&quot; Note, too, the core provides ways to work around the Descent by providing rules to drain vessels","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T01:23:41-07:00","id":279446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=278983#post278983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think any corebook without any supplements can be 100% fleshed out. I think the Mummy corebook provides the essential experience that later supplements are building on.<br /> <br /> Demon is the same way, IMO. First book teased Seattle and the children of Demons. Heirs of Hell and the Seattle book provided fleshed out rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its true that the Demon core lacks details on the Children of Demons and they are unplayable up until Heirs to Hell. Seattle was a very fleshed-out setting in the core, that made it a perfectly playable without a splatbook. The Seattle book just added a lot more plot hooks. <br /> <br /> Mummy's core lacked a lot more then that. Lets discount just purely mechanical things like group castings, Guild Affinities and Talismans and just focus on setting material. <br /> <br /> So just sticking with that category I would say the Corebook could use more info on - Modern Guild Structure, how Nomes function, inter-Guild and multi-Guild politics and relations between a Mummy's cult and their parent Guild. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the thing that should have got more word count was Memory, its talked about a bit more in the ST half of the core, but it really needed more and an explanation in the players part of the book. Certainly each &quot;level&quot; of Memory could have done with more word count then the couple of sentences they each got. Fleshed out examples of it use for sample PC's would have been nice (like the sample Cyphers for the example Demon character in that core book). My players consistently had issue/trouble grasping the finer points of Memory. The fact that some of the Devs have had to expand on it here to help people grasp the concept does not speak to the corebooks levels of clarity being quite what it should have been. <br /> <br /> Just to be clear, I'm not saying you can't run a game of Mummy out of the corebook, you can, but in my personal experiences, just running with the core makes the setting for the game feel kinda incomplete (Guild unique stuff is missing, the Deceived are absent, etc) and does kinda limit the type of Mummy stories you can tell (Relic Hunting, Cult Management or Apotheosis). <br /> <br /> However, this is an old argument with an old grievance of mine that I should shut up about really and stop repeating myself. I'll end on the point I've ended on for awhile, Mummy's a great game, but it has its design flaws and I am really looking forward to 2nd Edition clearing all this mess up in around 2017ish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T03:04:21-07:00","id":279475,"title":"","content":"My group hasn't had any problems with Memory at all. What kind of issues were it that the developers felt the need to step in and explain? I'd be interested in seeing those, and in what kind of problems have been having with the system. I agree that the sections in the book could have used more word space, given that it is pretty much <i>the</i> foundational element of Mummy, but it does seem fairly clear in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T06:01:06-07:00","id":279571,"title":"","content":"Memory's effect on Guilds was a big confusion we had on here for a while. A lot of people felt talismans were essential to how Guilds function since a Mummy can remember so little. Really, Malcolm just kind of cleared up the obvious by saying, &quot;It says in Memory 3's description that you remember your Guild and thus can 'play politics.'&quot; Which, yeah, why would the game claim to be so politic-heavy if starting level PCs couldn't even be privy to it? lol<br /> <br /> And then there's a vague line between memory and Memory. The former is about like, remembering phone numbers or what color your house was a thousand years ago; the latter is about what it means to act like a human being. The two, though, are related and bundled together in the Memory stat but the line is kinda fine and vague. I personally don't think it's too necessary to clear this up, but I think other people might get caught up by it?<br /> <br /> I do agree, though, about 'sample memories' for the pre-made PCs. Then again, I think that's by far the weakest and, frankly, mind-boggling supplement <b>Mummy</b> has. Vampires run night clubs because 1) it's at night and they burn in the sun and 2) lots of people go there to dance, do drugs, and fuck so it's the perfect spot to blend in your vampiric blood-drinking. Mummies...shouldn't run night clubs. But anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T13:49:56-07:00","id":280093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=279475#post279475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My group hasn't had any problems with Memory at all. What kind of issues were it that the developers felt the need to step in and explain? I'd be interested in seeing those, and in what kind of problems have been having with the system. I agree that the sections in the book could have used more word space, given that it is pretty much <i>the</i> foundational element of Mummy, but it does seem fairly clear in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>My players found the brief descriptions next to each Memory level quite vague. Yes I know it does &quot;spell-out&quot; what you technically &quot;remember&quot; at each level, but the were curious about what that actually meant for them as characters. <br /> <br /> In addition, I was one of those people that Reseru talked about in the previous post. I was under the impression that Guilds basically functioned via Talismans and that Mummy's did not cause whole cities to go mad (if more then one of them woke up around the same time) from Sybaris through the use of Relic Architecture (this was just after DC was published). Until Malcolm posted his explanation about a more detailed account of what a Mummy remembers at Level 3 Memory. <br /> <br /> Notably I felt his description contained a better explanation then the one in the book and could have been very useful for players and ST's to have had access to (and similar accounts for each other Memory level) from the start in the core. <br /> <br /> Oh also from the core...Vestiges. They add to your life web, that its, which gives you a minor bonus on the Cults &quot;repair&quot; roll if you get killed early. They can also be cannabalized, but unlike relics they are one shot items. <br /> <br /> DC added the fact they suppress Sybaris effects...which was kinda important and should have been in the core. Then again, I don't exactly love the way Sybaris works as is, so maybe thats a bigger hang up for me then most fans. <br /> <br /> Sorry...I'll stop now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T16:39:17-07:00","id":280257,"title":"","content":"I agree the <b>DC</b> info on vestiges could've been core material, but I don't see unease Sybaris as something completely 'overpowered' or whatever like so many people seem to think. Malcolm cleared that up a bit, too, though I can't remember exactly what he said. I think it was something like, you know, it's not as extreme of an effect as you might assume and it's only a vector for drama and conflict.<br /> <br /> Really that's what I think it comes down to, although of course it's admittedly vague: it's a rough guideline for how weird things get. An awakened Mummy 'creates plots' just by being awake, if you get my meaning. Plus, how often will a nome have a dozen Mummies around besides a Sothic turn anyway? And the whole point of Sothic turns is that they're CRAZAY","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T17:12:54-07:00","id":280274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280093#post280093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh also from the core...Vestiges. They add to your life web, that its, which gives you a minor bonus on the Cults &quot;repair&quot; roll if you get killed early. They can also be cannabalized, but unlike relics they are one shot items.<br /> DC added the fact they suppress Sybaris effects...which was kinda important and should have been in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for mentioning that. I think I missed that when I read through DC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T17:21:25-07:00","id":280276,"title":"","content":"You may not have the updated file. The sidebar containing said information wasn't put in until the errata went through, so you might have to re-download it. It's the last page before the sample adventure, I think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T18:40:49-07:00","id":280376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280276#post280276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may not have the updated file. The sidebar containing said information wasn't put in until the errata went through, so you might have to re-download it. It's the last page before the sample adventure, I think</div> </div> </div> </div>Fantastic, thank you very much!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T19:28:00-07:00","id":280423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280093#post280093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh also from the core...Vestiges. They add to your life web, that its, which gives you a minor bonus on the Cults &quot;repair&quot; roll if you get killed early. They can also be cannabalized, but unlike relics they are one shot items.<br /> <br /> DC added the fact they suppress Sybaris effects...which was kinda important and should have been in the core. Then again, I don't exactly love the way Sybaris works as is, so maybe thats a bigger hang up for me then most fans.<br /> <br /> Sorry...I'll stop now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Vestige section in the Mummy core book was really quite disappointing, and the expansion of their effects in D.C. felt a bit like the developers tossing in a cool extra idea they came up with later. Completely agree on that count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T20:23:01-07:00","id":280470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280423#post280423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Vestige section in the Mummy core book was really quite disappointing, and the expansion of their effects in D.C. felt a bit like the developers tossing in a cool extra idea they came up with later. Completely agree on that count.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, sometimes a problem can be solved in a supplement that wasn't in the corebook. In Demon, the interaction between pacts and exploits (a very minor part of the pact system) wasn't really clarified (in a way I could understand) until the Interface fiction anthology introduced the conditional pact rules. <br /> <br /> The only problem I have with supplements and cores is if the core is made unplayable and needs a supplement as a patch. cMage 1e, for instance, had a kinda broken magic system that Phil Brucato had to patch in the very first supplement (storyteller's handbook). <br /> <br /> Mummy's core works well, but there was definitely a lot of design space that the supplements fill nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T23:32:25-07:00","id":280640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280470#post280470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy's core works well, but there was definitely a lot of design space that the supplements fill nicely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, Octavo.<br /> <br /> It should probably go without saying, but in case it doesn't, it wasn't my choice or preference for <b>Mummy</b> to get what amounts to the smallest core in the history of the WoD. Sometimes, the cookie crumbles how it crumbles, and you have to try and make the best of it.<br /> <br /> Had I another 64 pages to work with, I'm sure you can imagine what other material would have ended up in the core, but... at least that stuff is getting out there.<br /> <br /> C.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T00:30:32-07:00","id":280667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=278678#post278678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes I too would have liked Mummy to be more &quot;open-dev&quot; then its been. One of the things I am looking forward too when they give the game a Second Edition is having the chance to comment on the open-dev process for it. Its really jarring that people like Dave Brookshaw, Steve, David Hill, Rose Bailey and &quot;Black Hat&quot; Matt are all really big on open dev blogs, forum posts and preview docs for their lines (which is pretty much the rest of the New World of Darkness and some of the Classic one as well) and then CAS does nothing with it beyond a pre-release forum post about a month before release. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy went through an open development process when it was actually being designed and developed throughout 2012-2013, and CAS posts here when there's movement--and remember, the game is a year and a half old. Evidently, the vagaries of Memory are at work. <br /> <br /> And speaking of Memory (and Sybaris) really folks, it helps when you look it up in the book. These Special Clarifications were substantially &quot;look it up in the book. See that thing is says? Do that.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how Guildhalls represents a transition any greater than with faction books for other games. I designed an entire political tier for Mage: The Awakening in the Silver Ladder book as well as rules for a new supernatural type! Guildhalls is considerably more conservative than elements in things like Covenant and clan stuff for Requiem, for example. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T00:37:39-07:00","id":280685,"title":"","content":"Don't get the wrong impression. It's just, for me, it's my favorite game and to know it has such potential it's just unfortunate that it got the short end of the stick. If it came out nowadays, with OPP being successful and, hell, having more than one full employee, I'm sure it would've gotten more right away.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy</b>, out of all the lines, evokes its source material the best, I think. <b>Vampire</b> and <b>Changeling</b> are contenders, but when I run <b>Mummy</b> I feel like...a resurrected Egyptian lich. It's the game that makes me really feel like I'm 'peeling back the hidden layers' of its classic namesake films.<br /> <br /> &quot;Look out! It's an amkhat! What would Bela Lugosi do?!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T00:56:01-07:00","id":280688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280685#post280685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mummy</b>, out of all the lines, evokes its source material the best, I think. <b>Vampire</b> and <b>Changeling</b> are contenders, but when I run <b>Mummy</b> I feel like...a resurrected Egyptian lich. It's the game that makes me really feel like I'm 'peeling back the hidden layers' of its classic namesake films.<br /> &quot;Look out! It's an amkhat! What would Bela Lugosi do?!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what sold me on Mummy and made my group into devotees of the game. Mummy has a *feel* to it. It approaches the World of Darkness in a way no other game has, just from its basic mechanic alone - you start off godlike, you conclude as a withered husk. It just has this tone of the epic, in the truest sense of the word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T01:27:46-07:00","id":280732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280667#post280667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummy went through an open development process when it was actually being designed and developed throughout 2012-2013, and CAS posts here when there's movement--and remember, the game is a year and a half old. Evidently, the vagaries of Memory are at work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember the discussion threads on RPGnet and through the KS and a general query that kept coming up was 'what players do and what's the game about'. So, yes, there was an open Dev series of blogs with previewed powers and art and setting and such but, for whatever reason, it didn't come together as a coherent whole from those previews as people (myself included) didn't know what Mummy was about.<br /> <br /> Then the core book dropped and discussion threads...remained fairly confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T01:31:36-07:00","id":280735,"title":"","content":"Every Dev decides their own level of involvement in Fight Clu^k^k^k Open Development, and the writers follow on from that. Malcolm and I could talk about our chapter in Sothis Ascends (which Malcolm had to finish when I got terribly sick after it was already hilariously late,) but until Deceieved comes out there's not much point, and it's CAS' absolute right to decide his own spoiler schedule. <i>Especially</i> in a game like Mummy where Player knowledge is a Thing.<br /> <br /> And, as a protip, saying someone should lose control of their game because you prefer another Dev's posting habits? Not cool. Not cool at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T01:37:01-07:00","id":280739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280735#post280735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, as a protip, saying someone should lose control of their game because you prefer another Dev's posting habits? Not cool. Not cool at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was always ludicrous to me. CAS is kind of my hero, especially concerning non-RPG stuff. We share mutual political concerns. My partner's family used to live in Syria (bad) and fled to Egypt (worse) a few years ago. I hate to say it like this, but the struggle is real. The world can be unkind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T01:45:24-07:00","id":280742,"title":"","content":"There will always be criticism on timescales and transparency. Look at A Song of Ice &amp; Fire as a damn good example. It's a stylistic choice though, so while it's fair to say &quot;I don't like the way this is done&quot; I wouldn't advocate judging a game line by that same factor.<br /> <br /> Additionally, to echo Dave, it's poor form to say &quot;I wish X author / developer was writing this instead of X author / developer&quot;. That doesn't sound like the kind of thing you'd say to X author's / developer's face, as it's pretty insulting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T01:52:00-07:00","id":280744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280732#post280732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember the discussion threads on RPGnet and through the KS and a general query that kept coming up was 'what players do and what's the game about'. So, yes, there was an open Dev series of blogs with previewed powers and art and setting and such but, for whatever reason, it didn't come together as a coherent whole from those previews as people (myself included) didn't know what Mummy was about.<br /> <br /> Then the core book dropped and discussion threads...remained fairly confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you were to ask me if there was a non-confused RPGnet discussion about anything in particular I would need a long, long time to answer. In any event I looked at the old thread just now and it's pretty much an ordinary thread of its type and topped out at discussing the Kickstarter and various releases. Otherwise, I can't really respond to a vague assessment of a two year old discussion on a message board somewhere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T03:39:25-07:00","id":280789,"title":"","content":"I remember those RPG.net discussions. Most of the &quot;confusion&quot; I remember was speculation over the game before info leaked out. Stuff like would it have a lot of elements of the CWoD(but not!) in ways that are closer to things you saw early with Requiem(ie some of the early games evoking more of the CWoD than what you see nowadays or with later games), if we were getting mummies from all over or just &quot;egyptian&quot; mummies.etc.<br /> <br /> Once spoilers started it was more of the same just speculation on what things meant. Once we got to the parts we saw and heard from the GenCon panel things really started to come together as far as what was &quot;vanilla&quot; Mummy. The sort of personal, and perhaps odd, mental game I play with perceiving the slow roll out of Mummy is it's like the slow work of an archeological dig. Considering no simply the approach of Mummy's presentation of player and ST knowledge have subtle differences compared to the other lines. It really makes sense given the time lines we are working with compared to say Mage, Vampire or even Werewolf's murkier pasts. There's a kind of neat little 4th wall breaking in considering that the Arisen are trying to piece together for the most part the story behind themselves and this empire they were a part of that is all but dust now and that slow exposure of it's buried secrets to us the players as the supplements peel back layers.<br /> <br /> That new info we are getting? That's you getting Sebayt experience :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-14-2014, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T04:32:03-07:00","id":280831,"title":"","content":"Personally, I have very few criticisms about the way Mummy has been written. It honestly feels better &quot;balanced&quot;, for want of a better word, than many of the other games I've played. Changeling, as the most recent one, springs to mind. There are far fewer dud Affinities and almost no dud Utterances (Waters of Life and Death is the only one where I can't conceive of any reason to actually want it) than there were clauses and contracts, for example, and generally the mechanics of the game are a lot more clear. I don't find that there are any major ambiguities in central game mechanics, and the vestige thing just struck me as odd in that a core part of the mechanics of an entire category of vessels was relegated to a city book supplement, rather than the core rules where they discuss how vestiges function.<br /> <br /> Mummy is my favourite RPG, bar none. It is a beautifully written book, and as much as the slow pace is killing me, I wouldn't wish the writing team to change in the slightest. You guys have already produced the best roleplaying product I have ever had the pleasure to spend money on, and once the books are all out I won't even have my own impatience detracting from the affection I have for the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T05:50:00-07:00","id":280910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280831#post280831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy is my favourite RPG, bar none. It is a beautifully written book, and as much as the slow pace is killing me, I wouldn't wish the writing team to change in the slightest. You guys have already produced the best roleplaying product I have ever had the pleasure to spend money on, and once the books are all out I won't even have my own impatience detracting from the affection I have for the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gambled $300 on <b>Mummy</b>'s KS and let me tell you, I won and it was worth it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T05:54:07-07:00","id":280916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280910#post280910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gambled $300 on <b>Mummy</b>'s KS and let me tell you, I won and it was worth it</div> </div> </div> </div>For me it was a stroke of luck. I had heard of the game, and was going through a Mummy kick (rewatched the new Trilogy, went and dug out the original '31 Mummy with Boris Karloff), but if I hadn't been at my FLGS which had stocked Deluxe corebooks for some reason I don't think I would really have &quot;discovered&quot; it. One of the best $50 I ever spent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:33:28-07:00","id":281141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280742#post280742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, to echo Dave, it's poor form to say &quot;I wish X author / developer was writing this instead of X author / developer&quot;. That doesn't sound like the kind of thing you'd say to X author's / developer's face, as it's pretty insulting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, please, please spare me the hypothetical character judgement. Considering this is a forum discussion and like all anonymous/semi-anonymous communication its basically impossible judge anything about anyone beyond what they say and how they say it (by which you can ascertain that I am frustrated by some of the stuff involved in the Mummy lines development and I'm not afraid of being &quot;rood&quot; to voice my opinion on a public forum that allows for freedom of opinion to be voiced) this sort of statement is pointless. Any statement I could make is response to such a comment would likewise, be pointless. So I'm just going to leave that whole can of worms alone now.<br /> <br /> As for the other topics raised, because this thread got really busy in the day I've been away.<br /> <br /> 1) I think CAS has mentioned it before and I've agreed with him in the past about the page count issue for the Mummy Corebook. Nice to see that refreshed, at the same time, its an old point I'll leave alone from now on. No point beating a dead horse and everyone on the thread pretty much seems to wish we had had more pages but as CAS said the books page issue was just something that happened. End of story. I won't be bringing it up again.<br /> <br /> 2) True Malcolm sometimes all one needs to do is go back and refresh ones Memory of the rules in the books. I find a lot of problems are solved this way. Sometimes people go back and reread the books and don't find the explanation or info they are looking for. Sometimes they find the language unclear or confusing or that its lacking a clear defined meaning them.<br /> <br /> I've seen both happen to my players in Mummy's case and I've had that same thing happen to me. Its not like its endemic to the book, its just that some things (like Memory levels) could have been helped with examples and a little more word count. Once again though this is just mine and my players experience (though several other people on the forum have mentioned it I think, if Memory serves)<br /> <br /> In addenda, the idea that the Mummy lines age removes it from the possibility of open-dev is one I find a bit strange. V20's been going for a while too, each one of its supplements has had open dev? Blood and Smoke is currently running open dev for its first splat-book. Obviously this sort of thing might have seen more wide-spread implementation after Mummy's initial release. Likewise, I appreciate that the final decision on stuff like this rests with the devs and its their choice to do open-dev or not.<br /> <br /> 3) Yes I agree that Mummy is probably the best game at getting its &quot;mood&quot; across in actual play. Particularly I've found in the distinction it draws between its magic (which in general is more grotesque and visceral) and several other types in the WoD (my players were veteran Mage players).<br /> <br /> 4) I'd like to clarify I never asked for additional info on future releases that are past Deceived in the release chain while Deceived is still not out. That's insane in a game as interlinked as Mummy and in general not something I've seen any developers for the various WoD lines do.<br /> <br /> 5) I've touched on this previously in this post. However, to expand.<br /> <br /> I mentioned possible devs for Mummy 2nd ed for a number of reasons. Firstly, because every other second edition so fare (save Awakening) has had a different lead developer then the previous edition. Secondly, this has allowed the second editions to go in different directions from their first edition counterparts (I like change between editions, I know that's not to everyone's taste), as it goes without saying that different devs have different ideas. Thirdly, I listed two Devs that I find genuinely engaging and interesting in their take (which takes material in a different direction while being loyal to core themes and mood established by said material) on pre-established material (Dark Ages is Daves case, Promethean in Matts) and felt could likewise do something interesting with Mummy. Fourthly, I listed two devs I enjoy the involvement of in the Onyx Path community (and obvious commitment to that community and Onyx Path as major priorities) and yes, like the open-dev process of.<br /> <br /> Fifthly, it was not my intent to cause offense to any other Devs currently working on the Mummy line (edit - As I know I have in the past, around page 7 of this thread where I launched a semi-personal attack on CAS's handling of the game. Not something I'm proud of and something that CAS and I addressed shortly after). Surprise, surprise I'm a big fan of the game, Mummy's in my top 4 NWoD games. I've praised its setting and feel to high heavens in the past (not to mention try to sell the game to a group of massively skeptical players in the first place). Content wise its second to none in the NWoD, no doubt about that. I'm sure Mummy would not be the game it is without CAS and is meticulous attention to the setting and his love of the history involved.<br /> <br /> 6) I'll add my voice to Azahhul in saying that I have very few criticism of how Mummy has been written and how the world of Mummy has been created and presented in the books. Likewise, (because I get the feeling rotten fruit and vegetables are being prepared) I have no huge criticisms of any of the writing teams content on the line.<br /> <br /> My criticism are and always have been based on the implementation of the Mummy line in regards to its schedule (especially in relation to other Onyx Path lines) and the actual structure of the game itself e.g. the idea of having a big in-game &quot;meta-secret&quot; that the players should not know about in the age of the internet and its various online achieves for this stuff.<br /> <br /> However, I simultaneously recognize that these are largely criticism that I myself view in a different manner to many of the other fans on the forums who may have similar criticisms. As such I've made an attempt to not really talk about them. Since most of the argument and discussion about them has already occurred in this thread and I don't like going around in circles. I've had a little slip obviously judging by the last 2 pages of this thread.<br /> <br /> With all that said lets just hold out till Deceived and then we can all talk about how awesome that book is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 10-14-2014, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:34:22-07:00","id":281142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280910#post280910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gambled $300 on <b>Mummy</b>'s KS and let me tell you, I won and it was worth it</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I really enjoy Mummy's setting. The mystery behind it makes it more fun to be honest, because it gives storytellers and players a chance to come up with surprisingly interesting theories and ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:38:21-07:00","id":281150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=280640#post280640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, Octavo.<br /> <br /> It should probably go without saying, but in case it doesn't, it wasn't my choice or preference for <b>Mummy</b> to get what amounts to the smallest core in the history of the WoD. Sometimes, the cookie crumbles how it crumbles, and you have to try and make the best of it.<br /> <br /> Had I another 64 pages to work with, I'm sure you can imagine what other material would have ended up in the core, but... at least that stuff is getting out there.<br /> <br /> C.</div> </div> </div> </div>It speaks to the quality of the work you and your team put into Mummy when I say that it's one of the most thrilling and interestingly designed games I've ever read(and I've collected a lot of games in my time). Other games might win me over due to my attachment to their themes(Changeling and Demon), but Mummy excites me and gets me itching to play every time I look at the books now, they're that well designed and written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T18:05:27-07:00","id":281744,"title":"","content":"I am kind of devastated that I wasn't paying any attention to the World of Darkness when Mummy was going through Kickstarter. I would happily go back in time and drain my bank account donating to this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T21:11:01-07:00","id":281903,"title":"","content":"A guy could wear out his &quot;Like&quot; finger on a day like this. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the kind words, guys. After an especially difficult summer, it does mean a lot.<br /> <br /> C.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T15:02:46-08:00","id":310583,"title":"","content":"For completionist's sake in this thread, <b>Book of the Deceived</b> has been released and is <i>awesome</i>. <b>Cursed Necropolis: Rio</b> is being written, and <b>Sothis Ascends</b> is in development, for hopefully a quick release following this one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T15:20:34-08:00","id":310595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=310583#post310583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For completionist's sake in this thread, <b>Book of the Deceived</b> has been released and is <i>awesome</i>. <b>Cursed Necropolis: Rio</b> is being written, and <b>Sothis Ascends</b> is in development, for hopefully a quick release following this one!</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget that the Fiction Anthology is in redlines!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T18:53:59-08:00","id":311847,"title":"","content":"I just now saw that closed &quot;Mamma Mia&quot; thread.<br /> <br /> Wow.<br /> <br /> Erm... so, yeah, in addition to the stuff Felipe mentioned -- the anthology is called <b>Curse of the Blue Nile</b>, and one of the writers on it is a six-time Bram Stoker Award winner -- remember that we've also got (THE) <b>Dreams of Avarice</b> coming up, courtesy of the ineffable Malcolm &quot;Fists of Bronze&quot; Sheppard. I'm getting the first bits of that in this week, and trust me when I say that you guys are not going to be disappointed. (Well, the Mammia Mia fellow might be, but I don't imagine I'm talking to him anymore at this point.)<br /> <br /> C.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T18:57:10-08:00","id":311849,"title":"","content":"I don't think any of us will be.<br /> <br /> Thank Moderators for wise bans, folks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T20:45:59-08:00","id":311899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=311847#post311847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just now saw that closed &quot;Mamma Mia&quot; thread.<br /> <br /> Wow.<br /> <br /> Erm... so, yeah, in addition to the stuff Felipe mentioned -- the anthology is called <b>Curse of the Blue Nile</b>, and one of the writers on it is a six-time Bram Stoker Award winner -- remember that we've also got (THE) <b>Dreams of Avarice</b> coming up, courtesy of the ineffable Malcolm &quot;Fists of Bronze&quot; Sheppard. I'm getting the first bits of that in this week, and trust me when I say that you guys are not going to be disappointed. (Well, the Mammia Mia fellow might be, but I don't imagine I'm talking to him anymore at this point.)<br /> <br /> C.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean &quot;The Dreams of Avarice&quot; will show up on the Monday Meeting Blog Notes soon?<br /> <br /> As for the Mamma Mia thing...lets just say I thought I was slightly unreasonable in regards to Mummy...that guy put &quot;unreasonable&quot; in perspective for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T23:53:05-08:00","id":312013,"title":"","content":"Can someone remind me again what is Dreams of Avarice again. Sorry, I forgot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For myself, as far as the investment into Mummy it's sort of an odd tale. I've always been an Egyptophile so with the CWoD days it was things like the first W:tA purchase was the first edition of the Silent Striders tribebook, though never took to the Setites as much. I wish I still had my copies of World of Darkness:Mummy, Mummy 2nd edition and the two books I had for Mummy:the Resurrection. Always too hard to get into them with most people running standard Camarilla affairs. The excitement geared up not simply just hearing the news shortly after perusing a thread on people trying to make Mummy rules for NWoD, but finding out CAS was involved.(which was funny as a few people on that thread were essentially trying to hush people up saying NWoD would never get a Mummy game), with even more excitement after finding out Nephiphal was involved after enjoying his work from Exalted. That was a big deal as fond memories of CAS's work from CWoD still resonated. It was somewhat tough in reading the spoilers as a small part of me initially pined for multi-cultural Mummies and the heroic angle of CWoD Mummy.<br /> <br /> Given how much was tied to the metaplot though, it was easy to understand that a reiteration was not in the works. The surprising part was the way it meshed with the NWoD's style of horror. I don't know what exact would use for how the general flavour of horror I would use for the NWoD overall:eldritch, insidious perhaps. It has a sort of creeping quality, like awful things Man Was Not Meant to Know\u2122 lurks in every alley and rural hamlet of the NWoD just waiting for unsuspecting people to fall into. The blue book caught me by surprise with that sense and Mummy captured and expanded upon it, to me, more so than I had felt with other lines. It, along with the NWoD in general has been a pleasant surprise that I hope to eventually get my CWoD friends to finally try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T01:02:00-08:00","id":312043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=312013#post312013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone remind me again what is Dreams of Avarice again. Sorry, I forgot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In Game:<br /> <br /> Its the &quot;holy book&quot; for those Arisen pursuing Apotheosis. Its written by &quot;The Heretic&quot; the only Arisen known to achieve this much vaunted/maligned (depending on who you ask) state.<br /> <br /> Other then then that very little is known about the Heretic. Lots of tid-bits in the books hint at some aspects of his life, but since he achieved Apotheosis he's been one big mystery, even how long ago he achieved Apotheosis is debated. Some put it in the last century, others some time in the last millennium. <br /> <br /> Supposedly studying the book gives one insight into achieving Apotheosis. The ongoing chronicle for the Mummy books details the results of this text becoming a little more commonly distributed among the Arisen community in the current Sothic Turn. <br /> <br /> Out of Game:<br /> <br /> Its a &quot;fluff&quot; book for the Mummy line. A bit like The Book of Nod or the Lilith Cycle was for Vampire the Masquerade back in the day. So lots of in-setting information with a lot of pretty art (I hope they get the guy who did the Deceived splats to illustrate the whole thing). Like Deceived I think its supposed to &quot;blow the doors off&quot; a few ideas the fanbase has been kicking around since the core book was launched.<br /> <br /> Its likely to detail not only more of the &quot;truth&quot; of Irem, but also what's really going on in Duat with the Judges, since Apotheosis lets an Arisen remember what happens to them in Duat and what the Judges might be up too. I'm looking forward to it massively, as while I'm sure Sothis Ascends will have a few more pieces of the Mummy puzzle I think Dreams is more likely to give us possible answers to the last couple of big questions hagging over the setting. <br /> <br /> Also fluffy art books that can be used as in-game props are pretty much my favourite sorta book in general. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T02:15:45-08:00","id":312082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=311899#post311899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Mamma Mia thing...lets just say I thought I was slightly unreasonable in regards to Mummy...that guy put &quot;unreasonable&quot; in perspective for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that would be the other side of the spectrum. And I thought <i>you</i> wrote walls of text <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, let's not dwell on that. I'm excited for the fiction anthology, but forgive me that I always forget its updates because I'm (no offense) not as excited for it as I am the other releases. I'm glad the <b>Mummy</b> KS provided a variety of goodies and I'm glad fans of other games are all getting their fiction groove on as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T04:30:11-08:00","id":312142,"title":"","content":"And if they sell well we might get the Book of Going Westward (the book of judges), or even a 2nd edition/Chronicle book","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T05:08:07-08:00","id":312156,"title":"","content":"Do we have a Novel as well scheduled or I'm mistaken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T05:10:01-08:00","id":312157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=312142#post312142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if they sell well we might get the Book of Going Westward (the book of judges), or even a 2nd edition/Chronicle book</div> </div> </div> </div>After I saw the fantastic work they did on the Temakh I became very psyched for the Book of Going Westward. I really hope they get an opportunity to work on it someday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T05:50:32-08:00","id":312212,"title":"","content":"I'm convinced they'll do a second edition for every game. They pace themselves at two updates a year (<b>Werewolf</b> and <b>Mage</b> were initially scheduled for this year, though the former will still probably make it) so we wouldn't see <b>Mummy</b> until 2017 at the earliest anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>Book of Going Westward</b> I think we'll see but there's a lot of biased hope in that conviction. CAS said in that two-part interview a while back that there were 'plans' for an unannounced supplement or something when asked about learning more about Apotheosis <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T06:01:16-08:00","id":312220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=312212#post312212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm convinced they'll do a second edition for every game. They pace themselves at two updates a year (<b>Werewolf</b> and <b>Mage</b> were initially scheduled for this year, though the former will still probably make it) so we wouldn't see <b>Mummy</b> until 2017 at the earliest anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>Book of Going Westward</b> I think we'll see but there's a lot of biased hope in that conviction. CAS said in that two-part interview a while back that there were 'plans' for an unannounced supplement or something when asked about learning more about Apotheosis <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well maybe when talking about Apotheosis he may be refering to Dreams of Avarice, after all it's the treatise that the Heretic work. And I have a suspicion that Sothis will also have something on that regard, after all the Sothic Turns are the period of time that the Arisen awaken without any purpose, free to pursue Memory, so it would make an ideal time to seek Apotheosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T06:34:47-08:00","id":312229,"title":"","content":"I agree with everything you just said, but wasn't <b>Dreams of Avarice</b> announced by the time he did that interview? It seems to my wildly speculative imagination that after <b>Book of Going Westward</b> there would've been another supplement as a stretch goal, at some point, which they decided they're making anyway but haven't announced. I don't know.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see a book expanding the roles and rules for cults, sadikh, and witnesses, though. And a book expanding shuankhsen - like more bane relics and affinities (maybe bane Utterances, if such a thing could be), Ammut's corrupting influence on the world, things like that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T06:46:59-08:00","id":312233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=312229#post312229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with everything you just said, but wasn't <b>Dreams of Avarice</b> announced by the time he did that interview? It seems to my wildly speculative imagination that after <b>Book of Going Westward</b> there would've been another supplement as a stretch goal, at some point, which they decided they're making anyway but haven't announced. I don't know.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see a book expanding the roles and rules for cults, sadikh, and witnesses, though. And a book expanding shuankhsen - like more bane relics and affinities (maybe bane Utterances, if such a thing could be), Ammut's corrupting influence on the world, things like that</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you point me out to the interview you are mentioning?<br /> Hum.. Ammut corrupting influence would been nice. Places touched by it like the Shan'iatu found and unique creatures besides the Amkhata. Rules for mortals using Iremite magic would be nice too, tough we can make do already with Utterances and Seba.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T09:21:04-08:00","id":312314,"title":"","content":"Once again, to be the pessimist in a group of optimists...<br /> <br /> Any additional books for Mummy beyond the ones we know about is at current pure speculation.<br /> <br /> Considering Mummy is a &quot;limited line&quot; like Promethean, Changeling, Geist and Demon it will have a set number of &quot;releases&quot; in its initial run. Usually these lines then get some minor support in general supplements such as Glimpses of the Unknown and the upcoming Dark Eras. How many books each line gets is does depend on the line. Promethean only got 4 books (which is frankly all it really needed), Geist only got 1 (due to troubles at White Wolf at the time), Changeling and Hunter were popular enough they both got &quot;expanded&quot; lines up to around 8 books during their initial run (and a couple extra just focused on them after the fact).<br /> <br /> Mummy is in a bit of a strange situation. We know that it was supposed to have the core book plus 3 splat books (Guildhalls, Deceived, Sothis). The Kickstarter added city books in DC and Rio, a prop book in Dreams and to fiction books (Curse of the Blue Nile and the yet unnamed novel). As I mentioned previously Mummy is also getting a chapter in the Dark Era's book and might get additional content depending on how that Kickstarter goes (and its format, since Rich has suggested some interesting things). Anything else, is as I mentioned pure speculation at this point.<br /> <br /> As Reseru pointed out Mummy is likely to see a 2E in 2017, likely towards the end of that year, so about three years from now. In that time all the other pending releases for Mummy are going to make it out.<br /> <br /> For me its that final factor that's the deciding one. Mummy will soon (in the next 18 months) be in the minority of NWoD's still in 1E (Hunter and Geist will likely have announced 2E by then and everything from Vampire-Changeling will likely be out) and it will be the only one getting new content with the 1E rule set by that point. Considering the development time for these books it could take that 18 months (or longer) to get Dark Eras,Sothis, Rio, Dreams, (possible Dark Era's bonus content), Curse of the Blue Nile and the Novel out to the fans. Its likely that only after all these planned books are out that Onyx Path will be able to take a look at the sales numbers for the line that they will then decide doing more with the line.<br /> <br /> Considering that this possible takes us into early-mid 2016 remember to get all this stuff out (once again, I'm presuming a consistent pace of development with realistic delays here). Not that big a deal on face value. However, I'm sure their will be substantial lead in time to Second Edition Mummy's development as it seems to be the case with the other Second Edition games. For example, BlackHatMatt mentioned that Promethean 2E has been in development for about 6 months before it was announced. Likewise 2E Mage had a fair bit of planning and writing done on it before it was announced I think. Which means at least a years with of development before release. Meaning work on Mummy 2E could start in mid-late 2016. Once the development of the new 2E core has started I doubt the 1E version of the line will see any updates.<br /> <br /> I'm sure if their is time and the sales are going on the books we know about they might try and squeeze another book it. Book of Going Westward would be a good choice for sure. It was a possible Kickstarter goal and people seemed to want it pretty bad (the fact its still talked about now, nearly two years later, is a good clue to its potential popularity). Ultimately, its a matter of time and timing.<br /> <br /> Considering my situation (my local group not touching Mummy with a 10ft pole until it hits 2E) I'd be happy for them to finish all the books they have planned for now by the end of 2015 and then have a year to do development on 2E before its even announced. Obviously, more content is good and I hope Mummy gets more, but I'm trying to be a realist in terms of both time and timing, development cycle for books in the line, business of Onyx Path in general (they are getting more popular each year) and the general popularity/sales of the line (which I cannot directly comment on, but I have heard Mummy compared to Promethean in that area, excellent game, but not exactly the easiest to get into or sell to most roleplayers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T10:49:02-08:00","id":312410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-