n (in the next 18 months) be in the minority of NWoD's still in 1E (Hunter and Geist will likely have announced 2E by then and everything from Vampire-Changeling will likely be out) and it will be the only one getting new content with the 1E rule set by that point. Considering the development time for these books it could take that 18 months (or longer) to get Dark Eras,Sothis, Rio, Dreams, (possible Dark Era's bonus content), Curse of the Blue Nile and the Novel out to the fans. Its likely that only after all these planned books are out that Onyx Path will be able to take a look at the sales numbers for the line that they will then decide doing more with the line.<br /> <br /> Considering that this possible takes us into early-mid 2016 remember to get all this stuff out (once again, I'm presuming a consistent pace of development with realistic delays here). Not that big a deal on face value. However, I'm sure their will be substantial lead in time to Second Edition Mummy's development as it seems to be the case with the other Second Edition games. For example, BlackHatMatt mentioned that Promethean 2E has been in development for about 6 months before it was announced. Likewise 2E Mage had a fair bit of planning and writing done on it before it was announced I think. Which means at least a years with of development before release. Meaning work on Mummy 2E could start in mid-late 2016. Once the development of the new 2E core has started I doubt the 1E version of the line will see any updates.<br /> <br /> I'm sure if their is time and the sales are going on the books we know about they might try and squeeze another book it. Book of Going Westward would be a good choice for sure. It was a possible Kickstarter goal and people seemed to want it pretty bad (the fact its still talked about now, nearly two years later, is a good clue to its potential popularity). Ultimately, its a matter of time and timing.<br /> <br /> Considering my situation (my local group not touching Mummy with a 10ft pole until it hits 2E) I'd be happy for them to finish all the books they have planned for now by the end of 2015 and then have a year to do development on 2E before its even announced. Obviously, more content is good and I hope Mummy gets more, but I'm trying to be a realist in terms of both time and timing, development cycle for books in the line, business of Onyx Path in general (they are getting more popular each year) and the general popularity/sales of the line (which I cannot directly comment on, but I have heard Mummy compared to Promethean in that area, excellent game, but not exactly the easiest to get into or sell to most roleplayers).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh we are very much aware that Book of Going Westward is just a possibility I think it's reflected in our posts anyway. It might be done or not but I will always show my fan support for it anyway!<br /> Just an addendum to your post, Onyx Path has said that there are no limited lines anymore, so if they feel there's an opportunity they will write new material for pretty much any line. And about 2e I'm frankly not even thinking about it right now. If(and I know it's a vague possibility) they greenlit Book of Going Westward I doubt it will even matter on the discussion, it strikes me a purely tematic book like Dreams of Avarice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T10:49:44-08:00","id":312411,"title":"","content":"It must be mentioned that the entire 'limited line' thing has actually been dropped. Any and all game lines are open to receive supplements if Onyx Path thinks they can pull it off and get a decent return for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T11:37:33-08:00","id":312452,"title":"","content":"Book of the Deceived is the best release I've seen out of Onyx Path since OPP became a thing, and is one of my highlight products in the entire nWoD. The quality of that book sold me on Mummy, having previously been a rabid hater of the line, and now Dreams of Avarice and a potential Book of Going Westward are the releases I want more than anything. For what it's worth, CAS and fans alike, Mummy is the one thing that gives me hope for the future of WoD; I've been let down by pretty much everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T12:53:47-08:00","id":312496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/69712-2014-mummy-releases-previews?p=312452#post312452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book of the Deceived is the best release I've seen out of Onyx Path since OPP became a thing, and is one of my highlight products in the entire nWoD. The quality of that book sold me on Mummy, having previously been a rabid hater of the line, and now Dreams of Avarice and a potential Book of Going Westward are the releases I want more than anything. For what it's worth, CAS and fans alike, Mummy is the one thing that gives me hope for the future of WoD; I've been let down by pretty much everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I'm in love with Book of the Deceived as well. Best villain material since Belial's Brood. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T14:19:52-08:00","id":312543,"title":"","content":"I won't be surprised if one of the first crossover games I run is ultimately about helping a Deceived obtain Mentaar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> F